<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/1001-reasons-for-a-data-management-plan-gcb2023> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Helena Schnitzer, Daniel Wibberg (FZ Jülich / de.NBI / ELIXIR-DE)\r
\r
Date:\r
11. Sept. 2023, 13:00 - 17:00\r
\r
Location:\r
Hamburg - GCB 2023\r
\r
Contents:\r
Have you ever wondered what research data management really is? Why is it so important? Then ELIXIR-DE has created the perfect training for you!\r
\r
More and more funders require the establishment of research data management plans to distribute their grants. Over the course of just three hours, you get the chance to learn about how to transfer research project proposals into proper Data Management Plans (DMPs). Data management experts will guide you through the basics of research data management, the dos and don’ts and how to improve the management of the data produced in research projects. After a short introduction of the research data life cycle and the FAIR data principles, we will explore in multiple hands-on sessions what a data management plan (DMP) is. We will sink our teeth into components, language, software and examples of DMPs. In light of the FAIR principles, we will evaluate possible problems and solutions and self-assess a drafted DMP for our own projects.\r
\r
Learning goals:\r
- Know the research life cycle\r
- Know the FAIR principles and understand their importance\r
- Know the expectations for a DMP\r
- Be able to sketch a DMP\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
None\r
\r
Keywords: \r
Research data management, planning, FAIR\r
\r
Tools: \r
- Computer with internet connection, webcam, and microphone\r
- Browser""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2023-09-11 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Germany" ;
                    schema1:addressLocality "Hamburg" ;
                    schema1:postalCode "22607" ;
                    schema1:streetAddress "Notkestraße 85, 85 Notkestraße" ] ;
            schema1:latitude "53.573032" ;
            schema1:longitude "9.880975" ] ;
    schema1:name "1001 reasons for a Data Management Plan - GCB2023" ;
    schema1:startDate "2023-09-11 13:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.denbi.de/training/1584-1001-reasons-for-a-data-management-plan-gcb2023> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/10eme-ecole-de-bioinformatique-aviesan-ifb-inserm> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:alternateName "EBAII 2021" ;
    schema1:description """La formation s’adresse à des biologistes directement impliqués dans des projets “Next Generation Sequencing” (NGS). Cette édition de l’école aborde les nouveaux enjeux technologiques: elle s’articulera autour de trois ateliers thématiques en session parallèle (RNA-seq, ChIP-seq/ATAC-seq, variants DNA-seq), et inclura une introduction à l’intégration des données, une ouverture aux approches “single-cell” ainsi qu’aux technologies “long reads”.\r
\r
L’école vise à introduire les concepts et à manipuler les outils informatiques et à en interpréter les résultats. Elle est basée sur une alternance de courtes sessions théoriques et d’ateliers pratiques. Les participants bénéficieront d’un tutorat personnalisé pour élaborer leur plan d’analyse, et effectuer les premières étapes de traitement de leurs propres données ou de celles de leur plateforme.""" ;
