<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/10th-nanosafety-training-school> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:alternateName "From Basic Science to Risk Governance - Interprofessional Education Training School 2021" ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "mixed audience" ] ;
    schema1:description """Risk Governance - Risk Assessment with Social Dimension\r
\r
Martin Himly, Sabine Hofer and Nobert Hofstaetter (University of Salzburg), as well as Dmitri Ciornii (BAM) and Daan Schuurbiers (DPF) built this session on the question “Risk assessment with social dimension: how does risk governance differ from risk assessment or management?” Starting with introducing the process of risk governance, it was discussed how data support decision-making, what data are needed, and what researchers can do in order to provide such data. This also covered FAIR databases and quality assurance, defined by the Knowledge Readiness Level (KaRL). Next to that, different stakeholder views and how socioeconomic aspects can be included into the risk governance process to warrant inclusiveness for different values into the risk/benefit estimation were discussed.\r
\r
Agenda:\r
- Intro to the Risk Governance process\r
- Interactive session: „What makes RG different from risk assessment?“\r
- Scientific/technical assessment requires YOUR data – FAIR and quality assured\r
- Intro to data QC: „What is the KaRL concept?“\r
- Interactive session: Applying KaRL\r
- „What is the social dimension in Risk Governance?“\r
- Joint Q+A and take-home message\r
""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "online" ;
            schema1:endDate "2021-06-24 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:funder [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "www.nanocommons.eu" ],
                [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "https://nanorigo.eu/" ] ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "Martin Himly, PLUS, Chair of EU NanoSafety Cluster WG-A" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2021-06-24 15:30:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:keywords "Knowledge Readiness Levels",
        "NanoCommons Knowledge Base",
        "data FAIRness",
        "data quality",
        "metadata completeness",
        "socioeconomic aspects",
        "stakeholder views" ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Slides sets and recordings of presentations" ;
            schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/record/5057543#.YN5CYudCRhE> ] ;
    schema1:name "Risk Governance Session at the 10th Nanosafety Training School" ;
