<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/1st-microbiome-pt-summit> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3301>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3344> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Microbiologists" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Researchers" ] ;
    schema1:description """**BioData.pt | ELIXIR-PT is setting a national microbiome community to align with ELIXIR's mission.**\r
\r
## About this Event\r
\r
Microbiome research has grown substantially and produced massive data over the past decade in terms of the range of biomes sampled, facing challenges in terms of data findability, accessibility, interoperability and reuse. \r
\r
**ELIXIR**, the** European Infrastructure for Biological Data**, is addressing these topics via domain-specific communities, namely via its **Microbiome Community**. \r
\r
**BioData.pt**, as the Portuguese Node of **ELIXIR**,** **is assembling its National Community to engage Portuguese researchers on this topic in this European effort. \r
\r
The Portuguese **Microbiome Community**, led by Isabel Gordo, from Instituto Gulbenkian de Ciência, is organizing its first National Summit to raise awareness and gather scientists addressing microbiome research in Portugal.\r
\r
If you are one of these, join us in the Summit and in this new community.\r
\r
## Important Dates\r
\r
[Abstract submission](https://www.eventbrite.pt/e/1st-microbiome-pt-summit-registration-128866123043) (posters): 5th January \r
\r
Note: Posters will be presented through a pre-recorded 2-minutes video on the respective sessions. Abstract submission is made through the general registration form.\r
\r
[Registration](https://www.eventbrite.pt/e/1st-microbiome-pt-summit-registration-128866123043) (free but mandatory, limited places): 28th January\r
\r
## Contact\r
\r
info@biodata.pt\r
\r
## Preliminary Programme\r
\r
Opening Session + Keynote \r
\r
**Rob Finn** (EMBL-EBI) - Head of ELIXIR Microbiome Community and EMBL-EBI’s Microbiome Informatics team - _Can microbiome analysis be FAIR?_\r
\r
_- Microbiomes of Humans and other Mammals_\r
\r
**Constança Pomba** (CIISA - FMV) - _Microbiome in Veterinary Healthcare_  \r
**Karina Xavier** (IGC) - _Discovery of Keystone Microbiota Member Providing Colonization Resistance to Pathogens in the Mammalian Gut_  \r
**Susana Solá** (iMed.ULisboa - FFUL) - _Impact of Gut Microbiome on Adult Neurogenesis_\r
\r
_- Microbiome Communities in the Sea and other Aquatic Environments _\r
\r
**Catarina Magalhães** (CIIMAR) - _Monitoring Arctic Ocean Microbiome to Link Taxonomy with Functional Capacity in a Rapidly Changing Environment_  \r
**Francisco Coelho** (CESAM - UA) - _From Marine Ecology to Biotechnological Entrepreneurship_  \r
**Rodrigo Costa** (Técnico ULisboa) - _The Microbiome of Marine Sponges: Diversity, Function, and Biotechnology_\r
\r
_- Microbiomes of Plants_\r
\r
**Ana Ribeiro** (ISA) - _Mining the Microbiome of African Legume Trees from the Miombo and Mopane Ecossystems_  \r
**Juan Ignacio Vilchez** (ITQB-NOVA) - _A call for Interactions: Beneficial Plant-Bacteria Relationships from Root to Apex (and more?)_  \r
**Maria Margarida Oliveira** (ITQB-NOVA) - _The plant Microbiome for Biofortification - Maize as Case Study_\r
\r
_- Microbiomes of Invertebrates _\r
\r
**Luís Teixeira** (IGC) - _Functional genomics of the antiviral endosymbiont Wolbachia_  \r
**Waldan Kwong** (University of British Columbia, soon IGC) - _Bees &amp; Corals: Microbial Insights from Non-model Systems_\r
\r
Closing Session + Keynote\r
\r
**Nandita Garud** (UCLA) - Head of the UCLA Evolutionary Genomics in Natural Populations laboratory - _Evolution in the Human Gut Microbiome_\r
\r
Executive Committee\r
Marta Silva, ITQB-NOVA | BioData.pt\r
Rafael Santos, BioData.pt | Instituto Gulbenkian de Ciência\r
Scientific Committee\r
Ana Portugal Melo, BioData.pt | Instituto Gulbenkian de Ciência\r
Cymon Cox, CCMAR | BioData.pt\r
Isabel Gordo, Instituto Gulbenkian de Ciência\r
Luis Teixeira, Instituto Gulbenkian de Ciência\r
Maria Margarida Oliveira,  ITQB-NOVA | BioData.pt\r
Code of Conduct\r
The BioData.pt Code of Conduct has been adapted from ELIXIR Hub Code of Conduct for Events so all participants at BioData.pt events can interact with each other in a respectful and safe environment safeguarding their personal integrity in case they believe there has been a breach to this Code of Conduct.\r
Please note that the event will be recorded.""" ;
