<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/3rd-hands-on-computational-enzyme-design> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0821>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_2275> ;
    schema1:description "Computational tools can dramatically accelerate the discovery and design of improved enzymes. This online course will introduce a number of user friendly web-based computational tools for redesigning enzyme properties and will provide intensive practical training. The developers of those tools will run this highly interactive course. Participants will be able to use the software tools independently at the end of the course. Prior experience in modelling or bioinformatics is not required and experimentalists are welcome to participate. " ;
