<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/3rd-microbiome-pt-summit> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Researchers" ] ;
    schema1:description """The Microbiome PT Summit is a collaborative initiative led by BioData.pt | ELIXIR Portugal Microbiome Community, bringing together national and international researchers, clinicians, industry leaders, and policymakers to explore the latest advances in microbiome science.\r
\r
The main purpose of this event is to serve as a platform to present and discuss the latest research developments in the Microbiome field, more specifically the role of the microbiome in human health.\r
\r
## Key topics\r
\r
The Microbiome PT Summit 2026 will explore cutting-edge research and innovation in microbiome science, with a particular focus on its role in human health. The programme covers a broad range of themes, from foundational research to clinical applications, including:\r
\r
- Gut Microbiome &amp; Health\r
- Diet, Nutrition &amp; the Gut Microbiome\r
- Microbiome Data Analysis &amp; Computational Approaches\r
- Microbiomes &amp; Host Interaction\r
- Microbiome Citizen Science\r
\r
These topics are designed to foster dialogue across disciplines and sectors, bridging academic research, clinical practice, industry, and society.\r
\r
## Target audience\r
- Academic and clinical researchers\r
- PhD students and early-career scientists\r
- Healthcare professionals\r
- Biotech and pharmaceutical industry representatives\r
- Policy makers and decision-makers in health and research\r
- Professionals in data science and bioinformatics\r
- Scientific communicators and citizen science practitioners\r
\r
## Organising Commmittee\r
[BioData.pt | ELIXIR Portugal Microbiome Community](https://biodata.pt/communities/microbiome)""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2026-04-16 17:30:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:event_types "meetings_and_conferences" ;
