<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/an-introduction-to-chip-seq-data-analysis> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Malik Alawi (UKE), Ceren Saygi (UKE) (External Partner)\r
\r
Date:\r
16th July 2019\r
\r
Location:\r
Center for Bioinformatics Hamburg, Bundesstrasse 43, 20146 Hamburg, Room 18\r
\r
Contents:\r
- Short introduction to ChIP and sequencing\r
- Quality assessment and control of sequence reads\r
- Aligning reads to a reference assembly (mapping)\r
- Peak calling\r
- Associating peaks with genes and other genomic features (peak annotation)\r
- Visualization\r
- Motif detection\r
 \r
Learning goals:\r
Hands-on exercises performed during this one-day workshop will enable participants to perform ChIP-seq data analyses on the Linux command line.\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
A basic understanding of the Linux command line and the (biological) ChIP-seq method are required to attend this course.\r
\r
Keywords:\r
Chip-seq, Chipseq\r
\r
Tools:\r
Fastqc, trimmomatic, bowtie, macs2, homer, igv""" ;
