<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/basics-of-single-cell-analysis-77bf0c2c-5b1c-4c7f-bd8b-3c12b8b73f73> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """This training will give attendees an introduction to state-of-the-art technologies for single cell analysis, including single-cell -omics methods and in situ approaches.

After an introduction to the field and the VIB Single Cell Innovation lab, we start with the most frequently used methods to isolate single cells (flow cytometry and microfluidics).

Given that the material obtained from single cells is limited, specialized sample prep methods are needed to enable single cell -omics experiments. Once the DNA/RNA/Protein sequences have been determined, we move on to the basics of data-analysis for single cell experiments. Next to single -omics, also multi-omics integration for single cells will be discussed. Also, the latest developments for in situ analysis of single cells resulting in information on spatial patterns of for instance gene expression within a tissue section will be approached.

We will close the training with a keynote talk highlighting some biological applications of single cell research.

VIB also offers hands-on training focusing on single cell transcriptomics data analysis. These courses are organized several times a year in Ghent and Leuven. Check the VIB Training website for more information.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2019-06-20 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Belgium" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Leuven" ;
                            schema1:postalCode "3010" ;
                            schema1:streetAddress "Leuven - Provinciehuis Vlaams-Brabant, Provincieplein 1" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "50.876972" ;
                    schema1:longitude "4.716817" ] ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "VIB" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2019-06-20 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:inLanguage "en" ;
    schema1:name "Basics of Single Cell Analysis" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "VIB Training" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/all-trainings/basics-single-cell-analysis> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/basics-to-advanced-genome-annotations-at-ensembl-and-rest-application-programming-interfaces-apis> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType """Who can participate:&nbsp;Students (B.Sc./B.Tech/M.Sc./M.Tech), Research Fellows, PhD Student, Faculty, Scientists, and Company Personals.&nbsp;\r
\r
Prerequisites\r
\r
\r
	\r
	Participants must have access to the laptop/desktop with&nbsp;a stable&nbsp;internet connection.\r
	\r
	\r
	Basic knowledge of R or Python for full REST API course (only for last four day of workshop e.g. 27th - 30th July).""" ] ;
    schema1:description "We are organising this high quality workshop for the participants interested in the genomics, bioinformatics, and genome annotations. In this workshop, one of the trainers from European Bioinformatics Institute ([EMBL-EBI](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/)), United Kingdom, will provide the hands-on training sessions of 'Ensembl Genome browser, and Ensembl REST Application Programming Interfaces (APIs)'. This workshop will cover the topics from basics to advanced techniques of genome annotations. This workshop will be equally useful for the researchers working with any domain of life (e.g. microbes, animals, fungus, and plants). At the successful completion of this workshop, participants will be become expert of all the modules of Ensembl Genome browser, and Ensembl REST Application Programming Interfaces (APIs) for their research.  " ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "online" ;
            schema1:endDate "2021-07-30 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "European Bioinformatics Institute (EBI)" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2021-07-19 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:keywords "Ensembl" ;
    schema1:name "Basics to Advanced Genome Annotations at Ensembl and REST Application Programming Interfaces (APIs)" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "European Bioinformatics Institute (EBI)" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.ebi.ac.uk> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/training/events/basics-advanced-genome-annotations-ensembl-and-rest-application-programming-interfaces-apis> .

