<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/best-practices-on-nris-clusters> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "researchers" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "students" ] ;
    schema1:description """ Do you want to expand your knowledge on HPC usage? \r
\r
Later in May, NRIS conducts a follow up course to the NRIS HPC onboarding course.\r
\r
The focus will be on different aspects related to the everyday usage of HPC facilities in order to facilitate a valuable and productive framework to develop your research. These include best practices and troubleshooting, resource management, software installation, gpu computing with slurm and advanced user support.\r
\r
Who can join? \r
Our targets groups are students, researchers and employees who want to deepen their knowledge of the usage of HPC facilities.\r
\r
Registration will close 12 May  """ ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "online" ;
            schema1:endDate "2022-05-24 12:30:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:startDate "2022-05-23 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:keywords "HPC",
        "software-development" ;
    schema1:name "Best Practices on NRIS Clusters " ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "ELIXIR Norway" ;
            schema1:url <https://elixir.no/> ],
        [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "NRIS" ;
            schema1:url <https://www.sigma2.no/nris> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://documentation.sigma2.no/training/events/2022-05-best-practices-on-NRIS-clusters.html> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/best-practices-on-nris-clusters-1-3-november-2022> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:coursePrerequisites """Targeted Audience: The course is aimed at students, researchers and employees who want to deepen their knowledge of the usage of HPC facilities. This is a follow-up course to the NRIS HPC on-boarding course (although it is not a prerequisite).\r
\r
If you are new to HPC, we highly recommend to refer the course material of NRIS HPC on-boarding course to benefit from this course.""" ;
    schema1:description """The Norwegian Research Infrastructure Services (NRIS) is offering a best practices course for users of national HPC systems (Saga, Fram, Betzy).\r
\r
The three half days course is the follow up to the NRIS HPC on-boarding course. We will focus on different aspects related to the everyday usage of HPC facilities in order to facilitate an valuable and productive framework to develop your research. These include NRIS HPC systems overview, best practices and trouble shooting,resource management, software installation etc.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
