<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/biocuration-q-a-session> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/operation_0306>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_0219>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3372>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3489> ;
    schema1:description """This Q&amp;A (question and answer) webinar will provide an opportunity for anyone who has completed ‘[Biocuration: A curated set of EMBL-EBI online courses](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/training/online/courses/biocuration-collection/)’ to join some of EMBL-EBI's experts and ask their own questions. This session will focus on the role of biocuration in maintaining life science data and general data management. It will also highlight the application of programming and text mining in biocuration.

The questions covered during the Q&amp;A webinar will depend on those asked by attendees, however we will likely cover topics such as:

- Biocuration principles
- Data management of biological data and open data
- Programming and text mining for biocurators
- Finding the right EMBL-EBI resource for accessing or submitting data""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
