<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/bioexcel-community-forum> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """\r
\r
BioExcel Community Forum is a networking event with a programme of small interactive working groups aligned with the BioExcel Interest Groups\r
\r
The BioExcel Community Forum provides an opportunity for members of BioExcel’s interest groups (IGs) and other members of the BioExcel community to come together for discussions and to work on issues of interest to the group. This will be an “unconference”, so it won’t just be a set of presentations; this will be a chance for you to work together with other IG members on topics that are of interest to you.\r
\r
In particular, the Entry-Level Users IG and Workflows IG are running a combined programme where, after an initial round table to find out the interests of those present, we will discuss a number of different MD tools and related workflows and will have a Bring-your-own-workflow (BYOW) session in which participants will discuss the MD workflows with a chance to ask experts questions and discuss potential solutions.""" ;
