<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/bioexcel-software-tools-for-intermediate-to-advanced-users> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:coursePrerequisites "The participants must have experience in basic Linux/Unix skills. Ability to use the command line: navigate files and directories through shell commands, create/move/delete files and directories, set environment variables etc." ;
    schema1:description """Our second Ambassador Program workshop is jointly organised with and supported by our colleagues at the National Competence Centres in Portugal, France, Spain and Ireland. The hands-on 2.5-day workshop will be a hybrid (on-site/online) event and will focus on the use of BioExcel core codes: GROMACS, HADDOCK, PMX and BioBB; and will include an Alphafold tutorial.\r
\r
Participation: Open application with a selection. 40 applicants will be selected for on-site participation. Applicants from Portugal, France, Spain and Ireland will be prioritised for on-site participation. We can only accept participants from EuroHPC Joint Undertaking member institutions.\r
\r
Registration fee: free\r
\r
Program:\r
\r
The program is under development and will contain the following elements:\r
\r
* Introduction to GROMACS (membrane-protein simulations) including how to perform alchemical transformation with GROMACS\r
\r
* HADDOCK Antigen-Antibody or/and Protein-DNA modelling\r
\r
* BioBB tutorial on protein conformational transitions calculations and automatic ligand parameterization\r
\r
* Advance free energy method / amino acid mutations\r
\r
* AlphaFold tutorial""" ;
