<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/bioinformatics-for-data-scientists-4-day-course> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:alternateName "Enhance your knowledge of the tools used to harness big data" ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Participants are expected to be familiar with Linux and scripting" ] ;
    schema1:description """Explore the open source world over 4 days with experience bioinformaticians.\r
\r
A course focusing on tools for data exploration and visualisation using the R language and bash scripting. This workshop is designed to help increase your productivity by developing frequently used scripts into tools.\r
\r
Develop robust practices when working with large datasets\r
\r
A balanced combination of lectures and practical sessions will allow you to apply newly-acquired\r
skills to a real data science problem. This allows participants to feel confident in their ability to\r
implement these solutions independently. \r
\r
• Linux™ power scripting (awk, xargs) – free yourself from spreadsheets\r
• Fundamentals of data management – assesing data integrity\r
• Handling genomics ranges (BED, SAM, BAM, etc.) – finding overlapping ranges""" ;
