    schema1:description """The aim of this course is to provide principal investigators with an introduction to the challenges of working with biological data as a research leader; to provide guidance on strategies for managing data and the importance of data sharing; how to encourage bioinformatics development in your team and / or work with collaborators and what resources are available across the life sciences.  This course will not provide a platform for teaching hands-on bioinformatics analysis.

This course is organised in parallel with [Managing a Bioinformatics Core Facility](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/training/events/2019/managing-bioinformatics-core-facility) to maximise opportunities for networking. Shared sessions are **highlighted in bold** in the course programme.""" ;
