<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/bioschemas-hackathon> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Helena Schnitzer (CAU), Leyla Jael García-Castro (ZBMed - Assoicated Partner), Nick Juty, Phil Reed (University of Manchester), Giger Tsueng (Su Lab), Alban Gaignard (University of Nantes)\r
\r
Date:\r
2025.06.25 to 2025.06.27 from noon to noon\r
\r
Location:\r
ZB MED in Cologne - Gleueler Straße 60\r
\r
Contents &amp; Learning Goals:\r
Let’s meet together to\r
\r
improve Bioschemas and Schemas.science websites based on open GitHub issues\r
improve or add tutorials on how to use Bioschemas and its specifications\r
improve or propose profiles, for instance there is some interest in reviewing the alignment between ComputationalTool and bio.tools metadata schema, creating a profile for FAIR4ML, creating a profile for Croissant ML\r
add Bioschemas/schemas.org markup to your own resource\r
Prerequisites:\r
This is an advanced course designed for participants with a solid foundation in Bioschemas. To fully benefit from the material and engage effectively in discussions, you will need to possess deeper insights into Bioschemas and their application.\r
\r
Keywords: \r
Bioschemas\r
\r
Tools:\r
Bioschemas""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
