<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/cabana-train-the-trainer-in-belem-brazil-f9088223-940f-4026-95b2-f27e7cf620f2> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType """This is a two-day interactive workshop which will be delivered in English. Applications are open for researchers based in ITV only.\r
\r
Selection criteria:\r
There are a number of criteria upon which selection of participants for this workshop will be made. Candidates should be able to demonstrate:\r
\r
\r
	They are at postdoctoral level OR have several years of research experience\r
	They are working in a Latin American institution and are likely to remain in the institution for the next year or more\r
	They are actively involved in a research project and actively using bioinformatics tools / methods\r
	They have a strong interest in training and have been involved in some training prior to joining the course\r
	They have identified a need / gap where training could be provided, and have thought about potential training they would like to deliver.\r
\r
\r
The ideal candidate will have 3+ years of research experience which includes a bioinformatics component, and a strong interest in developing or delivering bioinformatics training. You do NOT have to be a bioinformatician to apply.""" ] ;
    schema1:description """This course is currently under development and full details about the course are not yet available.  Once the programme is confirmed we will post it here along with details on how to apply and registration costs.  If you would like to be informed when applications open for this course then please click on the “Register your interest” button above.

 If you would like to see details of similar course from previous years, please take a look at our [course listings](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/training/handson), using the filter boxes to refine your search by year and subject.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
