    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType """This is a highly interactive virtual workshop which will be delivered fully in Portuguese. Applications are open for researchers based in Latin America.\r
\r
Selection criteria:\r
There are a number of criteria upon which selection of participants for this workshop will be made. Candidates should be able to demonstrate:\r
\r
\r
	They are at late-stage PhD level OR have equivalent years of research experience\r
	They are working in a Latin American institution and are likely to remain in the institution for the next year or more\r
	They are actively involved in a research project and actively using bioinformatics tools / methods\r
	They have a strong interest in training and have been involved in some training prior to joining the course\r
	They have identified a need / gap where training could be provided, and have thought about potential training they would like to deliver\r
	The ideal candidate will have 3+ years of research experience which includes a bioinformatics component, and a strong interest in developing or delivering bioinformatics training. You do NOT have to be a bioinformatician to apply.\r
\r
\r
Early-stage researchers and researchers from underrepresented gender and ethnic groups are especially encouraged to apply.&nbsp;""" ] ;
    schema1:description """This highly interactive virtual workshop takes place within the [X-meeting eXperience 2020](https://x-meeting.com/events/xmxp2020), organized by [AB3C](https://www.ab3c.org.br/site/). It will provide new trainers with knowledge, skills, guidance and tips for developing and delivering training. Trainees will explore a range of methods to enable and encourage learning, examine the requirements for a successful course and acquire appropriate feedback. The workshop itself will depend on trainee participation in group activities.

The workshop will:

- provide guidance on general training techniques and appropriate use of methods based on learner needs, including some general 'DO's' and 'DO NOTs' for successful training
- provide a framework for successful curriculum design and further development, to enable trainers to build a course appropriate to their learners' needs

The workshop will take place virtually via [Zoom](https://zoom.us/). """ ;
