<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/cabana-workshop-ngs-analysis-applied-to-virome-sequencing-in-agricultural-systems> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:contact "CABANA UCR Costa Rica" ;
    schema1:description "This workshop will provide wet-lab and/or computational training around the experimental design, laboratory techniques and detailed computational analysis of virome data from agricultural systems." ;
    schema1:endDate "2020-03-04 17:30:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:keywords "HDRUK" ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Costa Rica" ;
                    schema1:addressLocality "San Jose" ;
                    schema1:streetAddress "University of Costa Rica (UCR), Ciudad universitaria Rodrigo Facio Brenes" ] ;
            schema1:latitude "9.932543" ;
            schema1:longitude "-84.079578" ] ;
    schema1:name "CABANA Workshop: NGS analysis applied to virome sequencing in agricultural systems" ;
    schema1:startDate "2020-02-24 08:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/training/events/2020/cabana-workshop-ngs-analysis-applied-virome-sequencing-agricultural-systems> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/cabana-workshop-ngs-analysis-applied-to-virome-sequencing-in-agricultural-systems-9915446f-7878-4a0c-b6e9-818deb4d6837> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0622>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_0781>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3168>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3678> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType """This course is aimed&nbsp;at wet-lab researchers at any career stage within Latin America undertaking pathogen population genetics and surveillance, interested in applying next generation sequencing to virus identification. Those working in plant protection organizations and/or academia are welcome to apply, and priority will be given to those who have not yet attended a CABANA workshop.\r
\r
\r
\r
\r
\r
Please note this course will be taught in English, however the trainers are fluent in Spanish, and can offer language support where feasible.&nbsp;\r
A number of travel fellowships are available for this course - early-stage researchers and researchers from underrepresented groups are especially encouraged to apply for CABANA travel fellowships. You can apply for travel fellowships via the course application form. Priority will be given to those who have not previously been awarded a CABANA fellowship.\r
\r
Knowledge in R&nbsp;and NGS technologies is required. Therefore, these free resources should be studied beforehand:&nbsp;\r
\r
\r
	Basic R concept tutorials:&nbsp;www.r-tutor.com/r-introduction\r
	&nbsp;https://r4ds.had.co.nz/tidy-data.html\r
\r
\r
Learning outcomes""" ] ;
    schema1:description """Virome sequencing is a high throughput method to identify and classify communities of viruses, not only in plants but also animals and humans. We will focus on the sequencing of small-interfering RNAs (siRNAs) to discover the virus population in plant samples. The resulting information analysis relies on viral databases that are constantly evolving, and software tools constantly being updated. Therefore, we will explore all of these aspects in this workshop.

The workshop will consist of two modules: i) a wet bench workshop for training around the experimental design and DNA library preparation, and ii) a bioinformatics module overviewing multiple applications of Virome Sequencing, and its application in agricultural systems. People interested in this workshop may apply for both modules (limited to 10 participants) or only for the bioinformatics module (limited to 25 participants). Selection of participants will be based on [application form](https://forms.gle/WhSEFTwh82tvK4TQ9).   
 The bioinformatics module includes a pipeline for detailed computational analysis of virome data; including genomic analysis tools such as Virus-DetectW, phylogenetic and recombination analysis with MegaX and RDP and network  analysis using the statistical package R. Also, publicly available resources for virus analysis and their application will be implemented during the workshop.

The detection of pathogens is an essential task for people working on agricultural systems. In recent years the use of sequencing technologies has enabled the discovery and description of new viruses, even communities of pathogenic entities within crops, for example potato and sweet potato. This is relevant for surveillance and to develop strategies to control these pathogens across borders. """ ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2020-03-04 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Costa Rica" ;
                            schema1:addressRegion "San José" ;
                            schema1:streetAddress "University of Costa Rica (UCR), Ciudad universitaria Rodrigo Facio Brenes" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "9.935922" ;
                    schema1:longitude "-84.09196" ] ;
            schema1:maximumAttendeeCapacity 10 ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "European Bioinformatics Institute (EBI)" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2020-02-24 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:keywords "CABANA" ;
    schema1:name "CABANA Workshop: NGS analysis applied to virome sequencing in agricultural systems" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "European Bioinformatics Institute (EBI)" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.ebi.ac.uk> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/training/events/cabana-workshop-ngs-analysis-applied-virome-sequencing-agricultural-systems> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/cabana-workshop-plant-bioinformatics-analysis-of-crop-genomics-data> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType """This course is aimed at wet-lab researchers within Latin America (excluding Chile and Uruguay due to funding restrictions) who are working with and/or generating their own crop genomic data or who are working on genotyping technologies, including data analysis software development.&nbsp;\r
\r
Researchers who apply for CABANA courses should have projects in one or more of the CABANA challenge areas (sustainable crop production, communicable diseases, protection of biodiversity).\r
\r
Please note this course will be taught in English, however some trainers are fluent in either Spanish/Portuguese, and can offer language support where feasible. Priority will also be given to those who have not attended a CABANA event yet.\r
\r
Scientists from underrepresented ethnic and gender groups are especially encouraged to apply for this workshop, for example women and those with Black and/or Indigenous heritage.\r
\r
\r
Prerequisites: basic computational or previous bioinformatics experience is required for this workshop, such as basic commands in R. Undergraduate-level knowledge of plant biology would be an advantage. \r
\r
Please note: The course will use genomic data from crop plant species throughout the week. It will not explore in detail methods for assembling genomes.""" ] ;
    schema1:description """This course will introduce crop biologists to methods and approaches for analysing crop genomics data for genotyping. During the course participants will learn about genotyping experimental design, variant calling, comparative genomics using Ensembl, analyse variation data with Ensembl Variant Effect Predictor and explore concepts of genome wide association studies (GWAS).  The content will explain how to make use of existing public data, retrieve, submit and share your data with the community.

Trainers will cover the basics of diversity analysis using R, before analyzing various genomes to assess diversity, investigating gene-phenotype relationships and microsatellites. The course will be delivered through a combination of hands-on training sessions and lectures.

This course will be a virtual event. The content will be delivered over[Zoom](https://zoom.us/).  In order to make the most out of the course, you should make sure to have a stable internet connection throughout the week.

Computational practicals will be run on EMBL-EBI's virtual training infrastructure; this means there is no need to have a powerful computer to run exercises or a requirement to install complex software before the course.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "online" ;
            schema1:endDate "2021-12-17 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Costa Rica" ;
                            schema1:addressRegion "San Jose" ;
                            schema1:streetAddress "University of Costa Rica (UCR), Ciudad universitaria Rodrigo Facio Brenes" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "9.932543" ;
                    schema1:longitude "-84.079578" ] ;
            schema1:maximumAttendeeCapacity 30 ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "European Bioinformatics Institute (EBI)" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2021-12-13 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:name "CABANA Workshop: Plant bioinformatics - analysis of crop genomics data" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
