<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/cibi-data-clinic-october-2020> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Steffen Neumann, Rene Meier (CIBI)\r
\r
Date:\r
2020/10/26 @ 10:00 - 11:00 CET\r
\r
Location:\r
Online Meeting (connection details after registration)\r
\r
Workshop goals:\r
We want to invite you to the next edition of our online Data and Code Clinic. The Data and Code Clinic is a web-based video help desk for proteomics and metabolomics researchers and associated bioinformaticians and data analysts. We want to help people with their first steps in the exciting and multifaceted field, to facilitate the (sometimes) steep learning curve, and help using advanced data analysis options.\r
\r
In this CIBI Data Clinic, we will focus in particular on:\r
- Metabolomics\r
- MetaboLights Data Sharing\r
- Metabolite Identification\r
\r
Mode of action:\r
Our Data and Code Clinic is not a classical webinar, you can rather think of the coffee break during a conference, where oftentimes valuable suggestions are exchanged. We usually won’t have slides and don’t prepare a lecture.\r
\r
You are interested and have a question? We will try to answer them or tell you who might be the expert to ask. If you ask a question in the registration for or mail your questions to denbi-mash@ipb-halle.de a few days before the data clinic we can prepare and improve our response.\r
\r
Looking forward to seeing you,\r
Yours,\r
The de.NBI Data Clinic Team\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
None.\r
\r
Keywords:\r
metabolomics, mass spectrometry, R, MetaboLights, Metabolite identification""" ;
