<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/coderefinery-workshop-678f2262-23c2-4e07-97f6-b14640639e68> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:alternateName "- free online workshop on tools and techniques for more reproducible research" ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "advanced beginners" ] ;
    schema1:description """The event is open for everyone to join. \r
\r
## Content\r
\r
-    Version control with git with focus on collaboration and not only for the command line\r
-    Reproducibility: Preparing code to be usable by you and others in the future\r
-    What can you do to get credit for your code and to allow reuse\r
-    How to document your research software\r
-  Jupyter Notebooks: A tool to write and share executable notebooks and data visualization\r
-   Preventing yourself and others from breaking your functioning code\r
-    Modular code development: Making reusing parts of your code easier\r
\r
## Schedule and Registration\r
\r
For more information and registration, please visit the [CodeRefinery workshop page](https://coderefinery.github.io/2025-03-25-workshop/).""" ;
