<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/constraint-based-modeling-and-design-of-metabolic-networks-with-cellnetanalyzer-and-cnapy> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Steffen Klamt, Axel von Kamp, Pavlos Bekiaris (de.NBI-SysBio)\r
\r
Date:\r
5 – 6 November 2024\r
\r
Location:\r
Online\r
\r
Contents:\r
This 2-days course introduces principles of constraint-based modeling and computational design of metabolic networks coupled with a live demonstration and hands-on exercises with the MATLAB package CellNetAnalyzer (CNA) and its Python-variant CNApy.\r
\r
Day 1\r
Overview of key methods of constraint-based modeling and metabolic network design (coupled with live demonstration of CNA and CNApy):\r
\r
Fundamentals of constraint-based modeling of metabolic networks\r
Metabolic flux (balance) analysis\r
Flux Variability analysis\r
Phase planes and Yield spaces\r
Metabolic pathway analysis\r
Minimal cut sets and computational design of metabolic networks\r
Day 2\r
Hands-on exercises with CNA and CNApy: the participants will practice the use of CNA or/and CNApy by exercises with small example networks as well as with realistic metabolic models.\r
\r
Registration: \r
Please register at this link.\r
\r
Learning Goals:\r
\r
Comprehensive understanding of (1) stoichiometric and constraint-based modeling of metabolic networks and of (2)  related key functionalities of CellNetAnalyzer and CNApy.\r
Hands-on exercises with CellNetAnalyzer and CNApy will enable the participants to routinely use these software tools in their daily work.\r
Prerequisites:\r
None\r
\r
Keywords:\r
Metabolic networks, Flux Balance Analysis, Constraint-based modeling, Metabolic design, Microbial metabolism, Systems Biology\r
\r
Tools:\r
CellNetAnalyzer, CNApy""" ;
