<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/converge-workshop-series-outreach-to-funders-and-policy-makers> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """\r
\r
With Andrew Smith, Head of External Relations at the ELIXIR Hub\r
\r
This hands-on workshop is aimed at ELIXIR-CONVERGE Work Package 4 and ELIXIR members working on issues and tasks related to funding and long-term sustainability, including grant applications at the national-level and internationally (e.g Heads of Nodes, Node Coordinators).\r
\r
In this workshop you will:\r
\r
\r
	Understand better your key funder/policy-maker stakeholders\r
	Exchange best practices in communicating to national, European and other international funders\r
	Learn how to develop effective advocacy campaigns.\r
\r
\r
Seats are limited, registrations are on a first-come, first-served basis.\r
\r
 """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2021-02-12 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "CONVERGE Workshop Series | Outreach to funders and policy-makers" ;
    schema1:startDate "2021-02-12 10:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/converge-workshop-outreach-funders> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/converge-workshop-series-repeat-webinar-for-getting-started-with-impact-evaluation> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """\r
\r
Who is it for\r
\r
This is a repeat webinar for the fully subscribed Getting started with impact evaluation training event. This time, there is no limit to the number of attendees, and anyone interested in impact (of research infrastructures) is welcome to join. You do not need to be part of ELIXIR. \r
\r
The event will be shorter (2.5h) and less hands-on (no group work using MURAL) than the original event, yet still providing the core contents. Learning will again be facilitated by impact evaluators from our partner EFIS - see their article on this very topic! \r
\r
Objectives\r
\r
\r
	Gain new knowledge and skills related to impact evaluation, through formal teaching\r
	Complement this with knowledge-exchange based on four ELIXIR-relevant case studies developed during the first event (Skills &amp; capacity-building; Service provision; Cloud investment; Cooperation)\r
\r
\r
Outputs and related events\r
\r
Outputs from this event (incl. slides and video recording) will be made available through the ELIXIR Intranet (requires login). The video recording will also be posted here. \r
\r
This event is part of the CONVERGE WP4 Workshop Series: Innovation, impact &amp; communication - previous events were about Stakeholder mapping and landscape analysis, Outreach to funders and policy-makers, Communications, Getting started with impact evaluation (original event), and Organising impactful hybrid conferences.\r
\r
Agenda\r
\r
\r
	\r
		\r
			Time CET\r
			Item\r
		\r
		\r
			09:00\r
			Welcome, housekeeping, introduction to the event\r
		\r
		\r
			09:10\r
			Presentation of impact pathways method, followed by a plenary discussion\r
		\r
		\r
			09:50\r
			Break\r
		\r
		\r
			10:00\r
			Presentation on indicators, monitoring and measurement, followed by a plenary discussion\r
		\r
		\r
			10:30\r
			Sharing insights from case studies developed by breakout groups during the November 15th edition (details below)\r
		\r
		\r
			11:10\r
			Briefing on stages in impact assessment process\r
		\r
		\r
			11:30\r
			Event ends\r
		\r
	\r
\r
\r
List of case study outputs to be presented\r
\r
\r
	\r
		\r
			\r
				 Topic title  \r
			\r
			Topic description\r
			Main ELIXIR Impact area\r
		\r
		\r
			Skills &amp; capacity-building\r
			Setting-up and running a MOOC as part of a EU-funded project\r
			Human capital, skills development, e.g. better skills for users and resource providers\r
		\r
		\r
			Service provision\r
			Developing and operating a bioinformatics service (e.g. database, software, etc)\r
			Research efficiency, e.g. faster, easier, more integrated\r
		\r
		\r
			Cloud investment\r
			Investing in storage/compute for infrastructures operators to accelerate the creation of data assets (e.g. reference genomes) for others to use in their research\r
			Research efficiency, e.g. faster, easier, more integrated\r
		\r
		\r
			Cooperation\r
			Establishing and running an industry engagement programme\r
			Relationship capital, e.g. benefits of working together, facilitated knowledge-sharing &amp; cooperation\r
		\r
	\r
\r
\r
 """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2022-03-10 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "CONVERGE Workshop Series | Repeat webinar for Getting started with impact evaluation" ;
    schema1:startDate "2022-03-10 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/converge-workshop-series-repeat-webinar-getting-started-impact-evaluation> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/converge-workshop-series-stakeholder-mapping-and-landscape-and-market-analysis> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """With Hannes Rothe — professor for entrepreneurship at the Freie Universitaet Berlin\r
\r
Understanding your stakeholders is vital to position your services or training in your local innovation ecosystem or in the global stage. This workshop will equip you with tools, tips and tricks on landscape analysis, stakeholder mapping and market analysis. You are encouraged to work on your own project during this workshop and you will receive immediate feedback from your peers and the trainer.\r
\r
Hannes Rothe, who will accompany you throughout this workshop, is an entrepreneur with years of experience advising start-up companies and academics. He helps them understand their ecosystem and successfully position their products, research or services\r
	Would you like to obtain his expert advice?\r
\r
\r
	Get introduced to the topic and methodologies\r
	Hands-on session. Identify how your institute/ELIXIR Node/project fits into your local ecosystem. You will take into consideration your city/area/country and all other stakeholders (particularly industry), who need or offer data management services.\r
	Get feedback. Present your outcomes to the other participants\r
\r
\r
We are no longer accepting applications.\r
\r
\r
About the series\r
\r
You asked — we deliver\r
\r
Earlier this year, we run an industry and impact survey. Based on the results, we have put together a workshop series addressing the most voted topics: effective communication with different stakeholder groups, impact evaluation and stakeholder mapping.\r
\r
\r
	This series of workshops are open to ELIXIR members only. They can attend either one of them or the entire series.\r
	There is no need to travel! All courses will be held online.\r
\r
\r
Forthcoming workshops\r
\r
\r
	January 2021 | Knowledge-exchange: best practices for communicating with funders and influential stakeholders\r
	January 2021 | Introduction to performance and impact evaluation in the context of ELIXIR (part 1)\r
	January 2021 | Introduction to performance and impact evaluation in the context of ELIXIR (part 2)\r
	TBA | Effective Communication and engagement with industry stakeholders\r
""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2020-12-15 00:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "CONVERGE Workshop Series | Stakeholder mapping and landscape and market analysis" ;
    schema1:startDate "2020-12-15 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/converge-workshop-series-stakeholder-mapping-and-landscape-and-market-analysis> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/convincing-debating-negotiation> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Scientists are often in the situation that they need to discuss their scientific findings or their need for extra funding or resources with other members of the scientific community or with the public. The ability of expressing yourself in a concise and clear manner, using strong arguments, is therefore of utmost importance.

 """ ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
