<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/crash-course-in-r-and-prostate-bioinformatics> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description "In this workshop, you will be learning how to analyse RNA-seq count data, using R. This will include reading the data into R, quality control and performing differential expression analysis and gene set testing, with a focus on the edgeR analysis workflow. You will learn how to generate common plots for analysis and visualisation of gene expression data, such as boxplots and heatmaps. You will also be learning how alignment and counting of raw RNA-seq data can be performed in R. This workshop is aimed at biologists interested in learning how to perform differential expression analysis of RNA-seq data when reference genomes are available.." ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2020-02-20 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "United Kingdom" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Oxford" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "51.752013" ;
                    schema1:longitude "-1.25785" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2020-02-18 09:30:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:keywords "NGS",
        "R",
        "RNA-seq",
        "bioinformatics" ;
    schema1:name "Crash Course in R and Prostate Cancer Bioinformatics" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "Sheffield Bioinformatics Core" ;
            schema1:url <http://sbc.shef.ac.uk//training/> ] ;
    schema1:url <http://sbc.shef.ac.uk/training/prostate-bioinformatics-2020-02-18> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/create-a-data-management-plan-with-dsw> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3071> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Researchers" ] ;
    schema1:coursePrerequisites "None" ;
    schema1:description "This workshop aims at providing a hands-on session on creating a data management plan (DMP) using the Data Stewardship Wizard (DSW), a dynamic web forms system provided by ELIXIR Europe. The Norwegian node of ELIXIR is curating a national instance of DSW (https://elixir-no.ds-wizard.org) and provides a DMP form customised for life scientists in Norway. In this workshop, the primary instructor will initially walk the audience through the features of DSW while explaining the information to be captured in a DMP. As part of this demonstration, the instructor will show how to create a DMP, starting either from scratch or from a set of recommendations based on specific scientific domains including, among others, sequencing, light microscopy and high-throughput screening. A demonstration of how to work collaboratively on DMPs and how to export them to a document compliant with national and international funding bodies' requirements will also be given. In the second part of the workshop, the participants will work, individually or as groups, on a DMP for projects they are involved or for projects of interest. The two instructors will give advice and bring up interesting discussion points based on feedback from the participants. Depending on the audience, a discussion on how to modify a questionnaire or other, more technical aspects might occur as part of the workshop." ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2022-12-12 12:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Norway" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Oslo" ;
                            schema1:addressRegion "Oslo kommune" ;
                            schema1:postalCode "0373" ;
                            schema1:streetAddress "Department of Informatics, 23B Gaustadalléen" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "59.943337" ;
                    schema1:longitude "10.717823" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2022-12-12 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:keywords "DMP",
        "Data management planning",
        "ELIXIR-CONVERGE",
        "data management plan" ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Data Stewardship Wizard" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/Data_Stewardship_Wizard> ] ;
    schema1:name "Create a data management plan with DSW" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "ELIXIR Norway" ;
            schema1:url <http://elixir-norway.org> ],
        [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "University of Oslo" ] ;
    schema1:teaches """* Understand the relevant information to be captured in a DMP\r
* Start a new DMP on DSW, from scratch or from a set of pre-filled recommendations\r
* Share a DMP and work collaboratively on it\r
* Assess good practices in research data management\r
* Export a DMP according to funders' templates including the Science Europe template (adopted by the Research Council of Norway) and the one from Horizon Europe""" ;
    schema1:url <https://www.mn.uio.no/sbi/english/events/oslo-bioinformatics-week-2022/#07> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/create-and-handle-a-data-management-plan> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3071> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Researchers" ] ;
    schema1:coursePrerequisites "A user account on the Norwegian instance of DSW (https://elixir-no.ds-wizard.org)" ;
    schema1:description "This workshop aims to provide a hands-on session on creating a data management plan (DMP) using the Data Stewardship Wizard (DSW), a dynamic web forms system provided by ELIXIR Europe. The Norwegian node of ELIXIR is curating a [national instance of DSW](https://elixir-no.ds-wizard.org) and provides a DMP form customised for life scientists in Norway. The audience will learn about the information that needs to be captured into a DMP and how to use DSW for this purpose. We will demonstrate how to create a DMP, starting either from scratch or from a set of recommendations based on specific scientific domains including, among others, sequencing, light microscopy and high-throughput screening. A demonstration of how to work collaboratively on DMPs and how to export them to a document compliant with national and international funding bodies' requirements will also be given. In the second part of the workshop, the participants will work, individually or as groups, on a DMP for projects they are involved in or for projects of interest. The instructors will give advice and bring up discussion points based on feedback from the participants. Depending on the audience, discussions on how to modify a questionnaire or other technical aspects might take place." ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2023-12-13 12:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Norway" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Oslo" ;
                            schema1:addressRegion "Oslo kommune" ;
                            schema1:postalCode "0373" ;
                            schema1:streetAddress "Department of Informatics, 23B Gaustadalléen" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "59.943337" ;
                    schema1:longitude "10.717823" ] ;
            schema1:maximumAttendeeCapacity 20 ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "The workshop is provided by the Oslo node of ELIXIR Norway as part of an extended event organised by the Student Committee of the Centre for Bioinformatics at the University of Oslo in collaboration with the ISCB Regional Student group in Norway" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2023-12-13 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:keywords "DMP",
        "Data management planning",
        "data management plan" ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "RDMkit" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/rdmkit> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "FAIRsharing" ;
            schema1:url <https://fairsharing.org/10.25504/FAIRsharing.2abjs5> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Data Stewardship Wizard" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/Data_Stewardship_Wizard> ] ;
    schema1:name "Create and Handle a Data Management Plan" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "University of Oslo" ],
        [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "ELIXIR Norway" ;
            schema1:url <http://elixir-norway.org> ] ;
    schema1:teaches "After this workshop, learners will: Understand the relevant information to be captured in a DMP Start a new DMP on DSW, from scratch or from a set of pre-filled recommendations Share a DMP and work collaboratively on it Assess good practices in research data management and FAIRness Export a DMP according to formal requirements from funding bodies such as the Research Council of Norway, Science Europe, and Horizon Europe" ;
    schema1:url <https://www.mn.uio.no/sbi/english/events/oslo-bioinformatics-workshop-week-2023/index.html#17> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/create-and-handle-data-management-plans-with-the-data-stewardship-wizard> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3071> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Data stewards" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Data Managers" ] ;
    schema1:coursePrerequisites "None" ;
    schema1:description "The tool consists of a dynamic forms system operated within a web browser and offers a number of templates based on national and international requirements, including Science Europe and Horizon Europe. On top of these, DSW also offers a template based on the machine-actionable DMP standard developed by the Research Data Alliance, which recently entered the guidelines from The Research Council of Norway. DSW is emerging at a national and European level as the go-to solution for creating and handling DMPs, also outside of the life sciences community where it is developed (ELIXIR). This workshop is run with the intent of building capacity in light of its possible adoption. The primary instructor will introduce DSW and its features to the audience. The instructor will show how to create a DMP, starting either from scratch or from a set of recommendations and how to export DMPs to a document compliant with funding bodies' requirements or to a machine actionable standard. A general overview of how DSW handles different DMP models including version control will follow, together with a demonstration of how generic questionnaires can be adapted to a specific domain or use case. A practical session will follow: the participants will use a dedicated instance of DSW for creating or customising a DMP questionnaire. The two instructors will give advice and bring up interesting discussion points based on feedback from the participants." ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2023-01-13 12:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Norway" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Oslo" ;
                            schema1:addressRegion "Oslo kommune" ;
                            schema1:postalCode "0851" ;
                            schema1:streetAddress "Moltke Moes vei 39, 39 Moltke Moes vei" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "59.938478" ;
                    schema1:longitude "10.721364" ] ;
            schema1:maximumAttendeeCapacity 15 ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "Digital Scholarship Centre, University of Oslo" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2023-01-13 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:inLanguage "en" ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Data Stewardship Wizard" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/Data_Stewardship_Wizard> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "RDA DMP Common Standard for Machine-Actionable Data Management Plans" ;
            schema1:url <https://fairsharing.org/10.25504/FAIRsharing.6e60e5> ] ;
    schema1:name "Create and Handle Data Management Plans with the Data Stewardship Wizard" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "ELIXIR Norway" ;
            schema1:url <http://elixir-norway.org> ],
        [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "University of Oslo" ] ;
    schema1:teaches """* Understand how an organization can adopt DSW to its users respectively from its domain\r
* Understanding of how ELIXIR Norway operates its DSW instance\r
* Start a new DMP on DSW, from scratch or from a set of pre-filled recommendations\r
* Share and work collaboratively on the DMP\r
* Export a DMP according to funders' templates, including the Science Europe template (adopted by the Research Council of Norway) and Horizon Europe\r
* Create customised questionnaires and adapt existing ones, and make these questionnaires public""" ;
    schema1:url <https://www.ub.uio.no/english/courses-events/events/all-libraries/2023/digital-scholarship-days/data-stewardship-wiz.html> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/create-customise-and-maintain-a-data-management-plan> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3071> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Researchers" ] ;
    schema1:coursePrerequisites "A general understanding of DMPs and common practices in data management is an advantage. No additional software is required, but the participants are requested to create an account beforehand on UiO’s instance of DSW (https://uio.ds-wizard.org)." ;
    schema1:description """Create your own Data Management Plan template, share it with your group and export it according to a format compliant with requirements from the funders.\r
\r
DSW is a dynamic forms system operated within a web browser. It provides:\r
\r
* Templates adhering to national and international requirements, including those from Science Europe and Horizon Europe.\r
* A special template aligned with the machine-actionable data management plan (maDMP) standard. The Research Council of Norway highly recommends this.\r
\r
DSW is fast emerging at both national and European levels as the primary solution for creating and handling Data Management Plans.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
