<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/data-management-planning-workshop-for-life-science-projects-4e39d168-ea35-4850-9710-2a59d6a8548d> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0219>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3071>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3263> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Post Docs" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "PhD students" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Professors" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "All postgraduates" ] ;
    schema1:description """We are pleased to announce the Data Management planning workshop for Life Scientists organised in Trondheim by [ELIXIR Norway](https://www.elixir-norway.org/), [Digital Life Norway](https://digitallifenorway.org/) and [Research Data@NTNU](https://innsida.ntnu.no/researchdata).\r
\r
The intended audience are researchers (PhD candidates, Post Doctoral Fellows, Researchers, Associate Professors and Professors) that are planning to submit a grant application for a research project. Max. number of participants is 35.\r
\r
How-to generate a data management plan for a Life Science research project that will meet the requirements of the funding organisations? \r
\r
[Ingrid Heggland](https://www.ntnu.edu/employees/ingrid.heggland) (ResearchData@NTNU), [Ane M Gabrielsen](https://www.ntnu.no/ansatte/ane.gabrielsen) (ResearchData@NTNU), [Heine Skipenes](https://www.ntnu.no/ansatte/heine.skipenes) (Research IT NTNU), [Anne Heidi Skogholt](https://www.ntnu.edu/employees/anne.heidi.skogholt) (NTNU/HUNT-Cloud), [Kjersti Rise](https://www.ntnu.edu/employees/anne.heidi.skogholt) (NTNU/ELIXIR-Norway) and [Korbinian Bösl](https://www.uib.no/en/persons/Korbinian.Boesl) (UiB/ELIXIR-Norway/Centre for Digital Life Norway)\r
\r
## Course content:\r
\r
\r
#### 30.11.2020\r
##### 0900 - 0915 Introduction\r
##### 0915 - 0945 Requirements from institutions &amp; funding bodies\r
NTNU\r
H2020/ERC\r
Research Council Norway\r
\r
##### 0945 - 1015 Information on national and local storage infrastructures\r
NeLS/StoreBioInfo\r
NIRD\r
NTNU Computing &amp; Storage resources\r
TSD\r
HUNT-Cloud\r
NICE-1\r
\r
##### 1015 - 1030 Short break\r
##### 1030 - 1230 Relevant deposition repositories/ data archives\r
domain specific archives (ELIXIR/EMBL-EBI, NCBI)\r
NIRD archive\r
NTNU Open Research Data/ DataverseNO\r
NSD\r
\r
#### 1.12.2020\r
##### 0900 - 1000 GDPR and other legal requirements for research on humans\r
Health Research Act\r
Personal Data Act\r
\r
##### 1000 - 1015 Short break\r
##### 1015 - 1045 Licensing of data, biological material and software\r
##### 1045 - 1300 Hands on training and assistance to generate a data management plan\r
\r
#### Requirements:\r
\r
Join us online and bring your research project if you have one. You will get the opportunity to set up a data management plan for your project with help of the [Data Steward Wizard tool](https://elixir-no.ds-wizard.org/dashboard) using a structured and detailed questionnaire with references to relevant resources.\r
[Register before 25 November 2020](https://skjemaker.app.uib.no/view.php?id=9329496)""" ;
