    schema1:description """We are pleased to announce the Data Management planning workshop for Life Scientists in Norway provided by ELIXIR Norway \r
and Digital Life Norway.\r
\r
All projects receiving funding from the Norwegian Research Council (RCN) are required to submit a data management plan (DMP) shortly after the contract with the RCN has been signed. All Norwegian universities also require a DMP for all projects. \r
This workshop focuses on how to generate a data management plan for a Life Science research project that will meet \r
the requirements of the RCN.\r
\r
We would like to invite researchers (PhD candidates, Post Doctoral Fellows, Researchers, Associate Professors and Professors) \r
in existing and upcoming Life Science projects to develop their DMP in this workshop.\r
\r
Register [here](https://nettskjema.no/a/dmp-apr) by 31st of March 2022\r
\r
The workshop will take place if there are at least 10 participants\r
\r
## Program\r
\r
### 04.04.2022\r
\r
0830 - 0900 Login support\r
\r
0900 - 0915 Introduction\r
\r
0915 - 0930 Requirements from the RCN\r
\r
0930 - 1000 Parallel session: Local recommendations &amp; storage infrastructures Institutional DMP guidelines\r
\r
1000 - 1015 Short break\r
\r
1015 - 1100 Introduction DSW\r
\r
1100 - 1120 Information on national storage infrastructures\r
\r
    NeLS/StoreBioInfo\r
    NIRD\r
    TSD\r
\r
1120 - 1135 Short break\r
\r
1135 - 1230 Persistent identifiers, Controlled Vocabularies &amp; Ontologies\r
\r
 \r
### 05.04.2022\r
\r
0900 - 1000 Key legal requirements for research in the GDPR and Health research act\r
\r
    Personal Data Act\r
    Health Research Act\r
\r
1000 - 1015 Short break\r
\r
1015 - 1045 Relevant deposition repositories/ data archives\r
\r
    domain-specific archives (ELIXIR/EMBL-EBI, NCBI)\r
    Dataverse NO\r
    EGA\r
    NIRD archive\r
    NSD\r
\r
1045 - 1100 Short break\r
\r
1100 - 1115 Licensing of data, biological material and software\r
\r
1115 - 1300 Hands-on training and assistance to generate a data management plan\r
\r
Requirements: Join us online and bring your project proposal. You will get the opportunity to set up a data management plan for your project with help of the Data Stewardship Wizard tool using a structured and detailed questionnaire with references to relevant resources.\r
\r
Looking forward to seeing you at the workshop.""" ;
