<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/de-kcd-de-nbi-cloud-terraform-meets-infracost> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Educators: \r
Martin Braun, Max Boshof (HD-HuB)\r
\r
Date: \r
26.11.2025 2:30 PM - 4:00 PM CET (Berlin)\r
\r
Location: \r
Online\r
\r
Contents: \r
In this hands-on session we demonstrate how to use Infracost with Terraform to estimate public cloud resource costs before deployment. \r
\r
This session is a hands-on demonstration covering:\r
\r
- Setting up the Infracost CLI\r
- Analyzing Terraform costs locally from the command line.\r
- CI/CD Integration using GitHub Action to add Infracost to Pull requests\r
\r
Learning goals: \r
Participants will learn practical methods for incorporating cost awareness into their infrastructure as code (IaC) for public cloud environments.\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
This is not an introduction to Terraform. Participants are expected to have experience in using Bash, Linux and Terraform.\r
\r
Keywords: \r
Cloud, Terraform, Linux, Cost, Infrastructure as code\r
\r
Tools: \r
Terraform, Infracost, Linux, Bash, Git""" ;
