<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/de-kcd-meet-the-experts-consultancy-hour-series> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """We at de.KCD look forward to welcoming you to our open consultation hour and answering your questions about cloud or data management. Our open consultation hour takes place every two weeks on Fridays from 14:30 - 15:30 and is held as an open Zoom meeting. \r
\r
In addition, our consultation hours always deal with a specific overarching topic on which experts from our network will give a short presentation. We cordially invite you to take part in our consultation hours. Whether you have technical or theoretical, simple or complex questions, or simply need to talk and want to exchange ideas - we look forward to your participation!\r
\r
##Details:\r
\r
**The next consultancy hours:** \r
\r
14 Nov 2025:  Data Management Platforms, Planning, Set-up and Usage\r
28 Nov 2025: Easy Cloud Access via SimpleVM\r
12 Dec 2025: Software Management with Containers and Bioconda\r
23 Jan 2026: Introduction to Object Storage\r
06 Feb 2026: Intro to LLMs Specific to Medical Applications\r
20 Feb 2026: Software Stacks Based on Ansible Roles and Playbooks\r
06 Mar 2026: How to do version control with git\r
20 Mar 2026: Web Service Security\r
\r
from 14:30 to 15:30 CET, respectively. \r
\r
The link to the zoom meeting, along with an opportunity to raise questions, can be found [here](https://datenkompetenz.cloud/en/ask-our-experts/)""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2025-12-19 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:keywords "de.KCD" ;
    schema1:name "de.KCD Meet the Experts Consultancy Hour - Series" ;
    schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "de.KCD de.NBI" ] ;
    schema1:startDate "2025-08-08 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://datenkompetenz.cloud/en/ask-our-experts/> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/de-kcd-summer-school-2024-deploying-llms-in-the-cloud> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Everyone interested in digging into the technical and organizational details of deploying large language models for research via cloud infrastructure. Most of our trainers come from a biomedical and IT background. However, we are looking forward to an interdisciplinary exchange with research-developers and developer-researchers from all kinds of academic disciplines." ] ;
    schema1:coursePrerequisites """- Basic terminal knowledge \r
- Some experience with programming languages, ideally python, but R, perl, SQL etc. are also fine\r
- Basic knowledge of docker""" ;
    schema1:description """Ever wanted to look behind the – technical and organizational – scenes of large language models ? Already have your own AI research project sketched out but unsure of how to actually get started? Looking for cloud storage to power up your LLM but getting caught up in regulatory requirements?\r
\r
This summer school will provide practical answers by working with you on your own hands-on sample LLM in the de.NBI cloud. Instead of struggling through the steps on your own and reinventing the AI wheel over and over again, we at the de.KCD project  aim to pool our joint expertise and provide you with a shared, tried-and-tested workflow for cutting-edge research.\r
\r
Over the course of the week, we will walk you through the entire lifecycle of LLM deployment in the cloud. We will take a deep dive into the individual stages of the “day zero one two operation” concept of software engineering – where day 0 is the planning and design phase (including setting up your cloud access and drafting your data management plan), day 1 is go-live (installing and deploying your LLM), and day 2 is continuous operations (including backups and user authentication) and everything else that comes after going live.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "online" ;
            schema1:endDate "2024-09-20 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Germany" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Berlin" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "52.517037" ;
                    schema1:longitude "13.38886" ] ;
            schema1:maximumAttendeeCapacity 40 ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "de.KCD & BIH @ Charité" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2024-09-16 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:keywords "Cloud Computing",
        "Data Protection",
        "LLM",
        "Machine Learning",
        "Research Data Management",
        "Summer School",
        "de.KCD",
        "generative AI",
        "hands-on",
        "online" ;
    schema1:name "de.KCD Summer School 2024: Deploying LLMs in the Cloud" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "de.KCD" ;
            schema1:url <https://datenkompetenz.cloud> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """Participants will deploy their own LLM in the de.NBI cloud via a step-by-step guided journey throughout an entire lifecycle from design via deployment to productive operation.\r
\r
- Day 1: How to Cloud – Introduction, de.NBI Cloud & Project Idea\r
- Day 2: How to Data – Data Management, Data Protection & Data Ethics\r
- Day 3: How to LLM – Installation & Deployment of a Large Language Model\r
- Day 4: How to Service – Ensuring Continuous Support throughout Operations\r
- Day 5: How to Success – Real-Life Examples, Q&A and Discussion""" ;
    schema1:url <https://llmcloud24.github.io/> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/de-kcd-summer-school-2025-cloud-essentials-for-medical-data> a schema1:Event ;
