<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/de-nbi-cloud-user-meeting-2023> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """We offer our current de.NBI Cloud users an opportunity to delve into best practices in cloud computing. Additionally, we aim to introduce newcomers and potential future users to the capabilities of the de.NBI Cloud, which can expedite their research in forthcoming projects. The event will feature talks and workshops covering cloud computing topics, such as Kubernetes-based container orchestration, infrastructure as code technologies, and bioinformatics-related workshops like Bioconda and BioContainers introductions, as well as insights into bioinformatics workflow systems. The meeting's scope encompasses:\r
\r
	• Talks of experienced users in different research areas\r
	• Workshops for both new and experienced users\r
	• Opportunities to engage with experts on various cloud computing topics\r
	• The possibility to present your own project or project idea and receive feedback from other users and cloud experts\r
	• Social events designed to foster a sense of community\r
\r
Registration and participation are free of charge, but participants are responsible for arranging and covering their own travel and accommodation expenses. Register now to secure your spot before November 22: https://events.denbi.de/e/clum2023""" ;
