<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/de-nbi-spring-school-2024-bioinformatics-for-microbial-omics> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Robert Heyer, Sebastian Jünemann, Nils Kleinbölting, Andreas Rempel, Tizian Schulz, Alexander Sczyrba, Jens Stoye, Roland Wittler (BiGi), Nils Hoffmann, Helena Schnitzer, Daniel Wibberg (CAU), Thomas Rattei, Lukas Weilguny (ELIXIR Austria)\r
\r
Keynotes:\r
Oliver Schwengers – Justus Liebig University Gießen, ELIXIR DE, Topic: Genome Annotation\r
TBA\r
TBA\r
TBA\r
\r
Date:\r
18-03-2024 to 22-03-2024\r
\r
Location:\r
Center for Biotechnology - Bielefeld University\r
Room G2-104\r
Universitätsstraße 27\r
33615 Bielefeld\r
\r
Location map venue\r
\r
Contents:\r
The BiGi center is specialized in the field of Omics data analysis for microbes and is well-known for its software platforms. This de.NBI Spring School will focus on genomics, pangenomics, metagenomics and multi omics analysis. During the training, participants will gain insights into state-of-the-art bioinformatics tools. Participants will be introduced to the genomics workflow and gain an understanding of the possibilities and limitations of genome and metagenomics sequencing as well as sequence and multiomics analysis. The de.NBI Spring School 2024 will cover lectures and hands-on sessions by de.NBI and renowned experts, e.g. from ELIXIR Austria, in the fields and is aimed at PhD students, postdoctoral fellows or other scientists with a solid background in bioinformatics and molecular biology.\r
\r
Learning goals:\r
Participants will be instructed in genomics workﬂows and gain understanding of the possibilities and limitations of genome and metagenomics sequencing as well as sequence and multiomics analysis.\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
The Spring School is targeted towards early career scientists like PhD students and Postdocs, but also experienced scientists, who want to learn more about Bioinformatics for Microbial Omics.\r
\r
Keywords:\r
Genomics, Metagenomics, Pangenomics, Systems Biology, Multiomics, Metaproteomics\r
\r
Tools:\r
de.NBI cloud, Bacta, EDGAR, EMGB, Metaprotserv, SANS, Panacus, Corer,""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2024-03-22 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
