<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-3d-bioinfo-community-f2f-hybrid-meeting-annual-general-meeting> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """\r
\r
The 2022 ELIXIR 3D BioInfo F2F/hybrid meeting, the Communities Annual General Meeting, takes place from 2 November 2022,  12:00 GMT (13:00 CET) to 4 November 2022,  14:00 GMT (15:00 CET).  This meeting is planned as a hybrid meeting, with the F2F component at the Wellcome Genome Campus, Hinxton, UK. \r
\r
\r
	F2F registration has closed. We are still welcoming virtual attendees until 1 November 2022. Please see details at the bottom of this page. \r
\r
	 \r
\r
\r
The meeting will include presentations, workshops and participant engagement and will focus on the five Community activities: ​\r
\r
\r
	FAIR infrastructure for protein 3D-models and associated structural and functional annotations\r
	Open resources for sharing, integrating and benchmarking software tools for modelling the Interactome in 3D\r
	Development of models for protein-ligand interactions\r
	Nucleic Acid Tools: Progress and further plans\r
	Protein Engineering\r
\r
\r
More details can be found on the Community website. \r
	 \r
\r
Meeting Programme\r
\r
This meeting has a limit of 80 in-person attendees, with no-limit on virtual participant numbers. A number of selected invited participants will receive funding to attend the meeting. These will be specifically informed regarding the reimbursement arrangements.\r
\r
 \r
\r
The registration link is available to those logged in to the intranet (for both, F2F and hybrid attendees).  \r
\r
Additional Registration information\r
\r
Please note, if you have selected to attend face to face, this option is limited to a number of selected attendees. All registrants will be informed via email regarding their registration. \r
\r
Travel and accommodation cost for a number of participants will be covered, they will be contacted directly in this regard. For those we advise to not book any travel till after you have been notified. \r
\r
Travel and venue\r
\r
Once notified of your F2F attendance you will be expected to make your own travel arrangements to the venue. Reimbursement information will be shared with invited attendees after their successful registration.\r
\r
Information regarding travel for attendees, attending F2F on their own cost will be shared after registration.\r
\r
F2F Registration is now closed.\r
\r
Poster submission deadline: October 16th, 2022\r
\r
Online participants registration deadline: November 1st, 2022\r
\r
Contacts: \r
\r
Clare Garrard - clare.garrard@elixir-europe.org\r
\r
Katharina Heil - katharina.heil@elixir-europe.org\r
\r
 """ ;
