<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-all-hands-2017> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """The third ELIXIR All Hands meeting will take place 21-23 March 2017, bringing together members of the ELIXIR community from across the ELIXIR Nodes, and collaborators from partner organisations, in order to review ELIXIR achievements and activities so far and discuss plans for the future. The All Hands also acts as the ELIXIR-EXCELERATE Annual General Meeting. The agenda will include:


	Detailed agenda in pdf »
	Floor plan »
	List of posters » 


All Hands overview


	
		
			
				Day
			
			
				Programme
			
		
		
			Tuesday 21 March
			
				Welcome from Niklas Blomberg and Graziano Pesole 
					Keynote talk by Francis Ouelette, Genome Quebec
					Presentation of ELIXIR-EXCELERATE outputs
					ELIXIR User Cases
					ELIXIR Platforms

				Poster session
					Dinner at Palazzo Rospigliosi organised by ELIXIR Italy
			
		
		
			Wednesday 22 March
			
				Keynote talk by Robert Gentleman (VP Computational Biology, 23andMe) and Nicola Mulder (Professor, University of Cape Town)

				Flashtalks (parrallel sesions)
					Workshops (parrallel sessions)
					followed by dinner for remaining guests
			
		
		
			Thursday 23 March
			Parallel workshops Monday / Wednesday / Thursday  
		
		
	





	Recommended hotels

	Barceló Aran Mantegna 4*

	All inquiries about the All Hands event should be sent to allhands[at]elixir-europe[dot]org.""" ;
