<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-all-hands-2020> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """The sixth ELIXIR All Hands meeting will take place virtually 8 -10 June 2020. The meeting brings together members of the ELIXIR community from across the ELIXIR Nodes, and collaborators from partner organisations, in order to review ELIXIR’s achievements and activities so far and discuss plans for the future. We welcome attendance from participants from ELIXIR Nodes and invited guests. \r
\r
We’re excited to announce that two of our planned All Hands keynote talks have been turned into webinars which will take place on 26 May and 5 June.\r
\r
\r
	ELIXIR All Hands Keynote I — Janet Kelso: Archaic genomics\r
	ELIXIR All Hands Keynote II — Dimitris Koureas: Electric Butterflies, from field to bytes and back\r
\r
\r
Registration\r
\r
\r
	\r
		Registration is closed.\r
		If you need to cancel your registration, please contact allhands@elixir-europe.org.\r
	\r
\r
\r
Posters\r
\r
\r
	\r
		Participants of the meeting are invited to present a poster to enable all researchers with an interest to contact you and ask questions.\r
		Submitted posters will be made accessible via the ELIXIR Gateway on the F1000Research platform and we will advertise the online poster area at various times across the virtual ELIXIR All Hands 2020 meeting.\r
		We will also be awarding prizes to each of the top three posters, as selected by our Poster Prize Committee.\r
	\r
\r
\r
Code of Conduct\r
\r
\r
	The ELIXIR Code of Conduct has been created to ensure that people at ELIXIR events can interact with each other in a respectful and safe environment. It provides ways you can voice your concern if you believe there has been a breach to this Code of Conduct.\r
\r
	The ELIXIR Code of Conduct will be in place at this event.\r
\r
\r
The event will make extensive use of Zoom and Slack across the three days. \r
\r
Note: The virtual All Hands meeting ends on Wednesday 10 Jun 2020 at 16:30 BST. There are two project meetings taking place virtually on 11 June: the CONVERGE AGM and the Federated Human Data Strategic Implementation Study meeting. Both of these meetings are restricted to named project partners.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2020-06-10 16:30:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:event_types "meetings_and_conferences" ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:streetAddress "Eye Filmmuseum" ] ] ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR All Hands 2020" ;
    schema1:startDate "2020-06-08 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-all-hands-2020> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-all-hands-2021> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """The 7th ELIXIR All Hands meeting will be a virtual event taking place 1-11 June 2021. The meeting will bring together around 500 members of the ELIXIR community from across ELIXIR Nodes and collaborators from partner organisations. In a series of keynote sessions, mini-symposia and workshops, the participants will review ELIXIR’s achievements and activities and discuss plans for the future.\r
\r
Timeline\r
\r
\r
	Workshop call open:  15 February 2021\r
	Workshop call closed:  12 March 2021\r
	Notification of accepted workshops: 12 April 2021\r
	Final Programme ready: 19 April 2021\r
        Registration for the meeting open: 23 April 2021\r
	Registration for the meeting closed: 21 May 2021\r
\r
\r
Registration\r
\r
\r
	Registration has now closed. If you have already registered you can review or change your session bookings (use the 'Manage bookings' button). You can do this until Thursday 27 May. \r
\r
\r
Programme\r
\r
\r
	The All Hands Programme is now published, please find it via the "Programme" button below.\r
\r
	The ELIXIR 2019-23 Programme Mid-term Review will take place during the All Hands meeting in the afternoon of 7 - 9 June and is for invited participants only. The CONVERGE project Annual General Meeting takes place on the 10 June. \r
\r
\r
Code of Conduct\r
\r
\r
        The ELIXIR Code of Conduct has been created to ensure that people at ELIXIR events can interact with each other in a respectful and safe environment. It provides ways you can voice your concern if you believe there has been a breach to this Code of Conduct.\r
\r
         The ELIXIR Code of Conduct will be in place at this event.\r
""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2021-06-11 16:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
