<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-all-hands-2022> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """\r
	The ELIXIR All Hands 2022 will be held in the Eye Filmmuseum, Amsterdam.\r
\r
\r
The 8th ELIXIR All Hands meeting will take place 7-10 June 2022 in Amsterdam. The meeting brings together members of the ELIXIR community from across the ELIXIR Nodes, and collaborators from partner organisations, in order to review ELIXIR’s achievements and activities so far and discuss plans for the future. The All Hands meeting is also the venue for the ELIXIR-CONVERGE Annual General Assembly Meeting.\r
\r
The meeting is going to be a face-to-face meeting with the programme focussed on those attending in person. There will only be limited remote access to some of the workshops of the meeting. \r
\r
Please note that Monday 6 June is a bank holiday in the Netherlands and many other European countries. There will be plenary and workshop sessions on Tuesday and Thursday, while Wednesday is focussed on mini-symposia with a poster session and meeting dinner in the evening. The CONVERGE AGM will take place on Friday 10 June starting at 8:30, and the CONVERGE AGM ends at 16:25.\r
\r
Timeline\r
\r
\r
	\r
		\r
			1 November - 8 December 2021\r
			Call for workshops\r
		\r
		\r
			December 2021\r
			Selection of workshops\r
		\r
		\r
			7 March 2022 - 10 March\r
			Registration to the meeting is now closed\r
		\r
	\r
		\r
			31 March 2022\r
			Deadline for poster submissions, or earlier, if capacity is reached.\r
		\r
	\r
\r
\r
Accommodation\r
\r
\r
	For the 2022 All Hands meeting, ELIXIR will have a block reservation for accommodation for 100 rooms. More information is available to those who have registered.\r
\r
	The venue is located in central Amsterdam with plenty of options, but keep in mind that June is a busy month in the city and therefore it is recommended to reserve accommodation early. \r
\r
\r
Registration\r
\r
\r
	The registration to the All Hands meeting is now closed.\r
\r
\r
Poster session\r
\r
\r
	There will be a poster session on the second day of the All Hands meeting. The goal of this session is to share the broad variety of ELIXIR-related work and foster partnerships across the ELIXIR network. Posters have been one element of any meeting that is not easily reproduced online so this is a great opportunity to share your recent work and build contacts in a relaxed setting. Submissions will be available to those registered for the meeting for any activities that fall within the ELIXIR Programme, with a judging panel awarding prizes during the event.\r
Link to submit a poster has been shared with those registered to the event.\r
\r
Should you wish to give your poster an online presence (and a unique Digital Object Identifier!), you are encouraged to upload it to the Poster section of ELIXIR’s Gateway on F1000 Research.\r
\r
\r
\r
Code of Conduct\r
\r
\r
	The ELIXIR Code of Conduct has been created to ensure that people at ELIXIR events can interact with each other in a respectful and safe environment. It provides ways you can voice your concern if you believe there has been a breach to this Code of Conduct.\r
\r
	The ELIXIR Code of Conduct will be in place at this event.\r
""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2022-06-10 13:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Netherlands" ;
                    schema1:addressLocality "Amsterdam" ;
                    schema1:postalCode "1031 KT" ;
                    schema1:streetAddress "Eye Filmmuseum" ] ] ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR All Hands 2022" ;
    schema1:startDate "2022-06-07 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-all-hands-2022> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-all-hands-2023> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """\r
	The ELIXIR All Hands 2023 will be held in the Dublin Convention Centre, Ireland.\r
\r
\r
The 9th ELIXIR All Hands meeting will take place 5-8 June 2023 in Ireland. The meeting brings together members of the ELIXIR community from across the ELIXIR Nodes, and collaborators from partner organisations, in order to review ELIXIR’s achievements and activities so far and discuss plans for the future. The All Hands meeting is also the venue for the ELIXIR-CONVERGE Annual General Assembly Meeting.\r
\r
The meeting is going to be a face-to-face meeting with the programme focussed on those attending in person. There will be remote access to workshops of the meeting, and limited access to the rest of the programme, this will be confirm closer to the event.\r
\r
The programme is being finalised and this website will be updated as soon as we know the structure of the days. \r
\r
Submissions\r
\r
Mini-symposia\r
\r
This year 90 minute sessions will be organised in the following themes:\r
\r
\r
	Three on the theme ''Science - Enabling scientists to access and analyse life science data"\r
	Three on the theme ''Technology - Delivering services to support federated data management and analytics"\r
	Three covering the themes "Nodes - Equipping national Nodes for successful long-term operations" and "People - Developing people and capacity to benefit science and society"\r
\r
\r
Workshops\r
\r
\r
	25 workshops confirmed (thank you to all who applied)\r
	5 parallel session of 5 across the week\r
	Subjects ranging from FAIR data and Machine Learning to national funding for ELIXIR Node operations\r
	Fully Hybrid (for those who register to attend remotely)\r
\r
\r
Posters \r
\r
\r
	Two day Poster session\r
	Submissions open to anyone attending in person, deadline for submissions is 3rd April 2023\r
	Covering all ELIXIR-related activities\r
	Prize for best poster and best by a student / new researcher\r
\r
\r
Code of Conduct\r
\r
\r
	The ELIXIR Code of Conduct has been created to ensure that people at ELIXIR events can interact with each other in a respectful and safe environment. It provides ways you can voice your concern if you believe there has been a breach to this Code of Conduct.\r
\r
	The ELIXIR Code of Conduct will be in place at this event.\r
\r
""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2023-06-08 13:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Ireland" ;
                    schema1:addressLocality "Dublin" ;
                    schema1:postalCode "D01 T1W6" ;
                    schema1:streetAddress "Dublin Convention Centre, Spencer Dock, North Wall Quay" ] ;
            schema1:latitude "53.349801" ;
            schema1:longitude "-6.260296" ] ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR All Hands 2023" ;
    schema1:startDate "2023-06-05 12:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-all-hands-2023> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-all-hands-2024> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """This is a landing page for the 2024 meeting. All details are to be confirmed, and will be on the All Hands Eventscase website.\r
\r
	Log in to view the registration links. (Note: F2F booking is now full, though a waiting list is available.)\r
\r
\r
Workshops\r
\r
Requirements\r
\r
Workshops must be inclusive and consider diversity in all aspects, including speakers, hosts and participants, especially regarding balanced gender representation. Please encourage contributions from everyone using different techniques, such as small group discussions or platforms that allow anonymous participation, such as Sli.do. Most negative feedback from previous workshops often relates to a lack of dynamic engagement, i.e. too many back-to-back slide presentations.\r
\r
Workshops will run as hybrid events, so efforts should be made to include remote attendees to a similar level as those in the room. \r
\r
Resources available\r
\r
Each room will have a laptop computer, projector, screen, pointer for presentations and an OWL video conferencing camera. A Sli.do account is available on request to engage with the workshop participants, so please list this clearly in your agenda by 9 March. Late requests will be on a best effort basis. \r
\r
Due to space constraints, some of the workshop rooms this year have fixed seating. However, if you require a particular chair or table set-up, or require some specific resources, please send an email to allhands@elixir-europe.org by 15 May with the subject “[Room Setup]” and we will do our best to help. \r
\r
Each Workshop is provided with a Google Drive Folder, Leads should already have edit access. It will include a blank agenda pre-populated with the Title, Abstract and co-Lead names. Please use this document to plan the workshop structure, and upload any slide decks or other resources to the Folder and link to them from the agenda. The allocated day and start time of the workshop and dedicated Zoom links etc. will be added to the agenda by the Hub in due course. All workshops will be recorded and only made available to ELIXIR members on request.\r
\r
There will be five parallel sessions of five workshops. Assuming similar attendance to previous years, you should anticipate up to 80 participants in person with a number joining remotely. Please visit rooms well ahead of your session to check the physical layout is suitable and to test for any technical or connection issues. Technical support will be available, but this will be shared between parallel workshops, so we ask for your patience and understanding. \r
\r
Any further questions please contact fabio.liberante@elixir-europe.org or david.lloyd@elixir-europe.org\r
\r
Mini-symposia\r
\r
In addition to the workshops, a smaller number of mini-symposia will be organised in separate sessions. These will function more as explorations of specific topics.\r
\r
Posters\r
\r
Successful submissions have been informed, the poster session will be on Tuesday 11 June (17:30-20:00). There is a guidance document available. \r
\r
Data Privacy\r
\r
Data Privacy document \r
\r
Code of Conduct\r
\r
\r
	The ELIXIR Code of Conduct has been created to ensure that people at ELIXIR events can interact with each other in a respectful and safe environment. It provides ways you can voice your concern if you believe there has been a breach to this Code of Conduct.\r
\r
	The ELIXIR Code of Conduct will be in place at this event.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2024-06-12 00:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Sweden" ;
                    schema1:addressLocality "Uppsala" ] ;
            schema1:latitude "59.858613" ;
            schema1:longitude "17.638744" ] ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR All Hands 2024" ;
    schema1:startDate "2024-06-10 00:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-all-hands-2024> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-all-hands-2025> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """The 11th ELIXIR All Hands meeting will take place from 2 to 5 June 2025 in Thessaloníki, Greece. This is a highly anticipated annual event for members of the ELIXIR community from across the ELIXIR Nodes and collaborators from partner organisations. It is an opportunity to review ELIXIR’s recent achievements and activities, and to discuss future plans.\r
\r
All Hands is a face-to-face meeting and the programme is focused on those attending in person. However, remote access to workshops will be possible, as well as limited access to the rest of the programme. These details will be confirmed closer to the event.\r
\r
Workshop proposals call\r
\r
The All Hands programme will include a series of engaging workshops selected from those proposed by the ELIXIR community. We welcome proposals from all ELIXIR Platforms, Communities, Focus Groups and Node Officers (Node, Technical and Training Coordinators). Workshops should address cross-cutting themes which benefit from collaboration across the ELIXIR ecosystem. \r
\r
Workshop format\r
\r
Duration: 90 minutes\r
	Capacity: Up to 25 workshops, running in parallel (up to five at a time)\r
	Format: Hybrid (on-site participation by workshop leads, with remote attendee options)\r
\r
Why submit a workshop proposal?\r
\r
Workshops are an opportunity to:\r
\r
\r
	Tackle a challenge that benefits from the input of specific cross-sections of ELIXIR (e.g. Platforms, Communities, Focus Groups, Projects and Node organisations)\r
	Build connections between different sets of ELIXIR members, encouraging them to engage with activities across the organisation\r
	Deliver actionable outcomes that support the ELIXIR Scientific Programme\r
\r
\r
As well as workshops, the programme will feature a smaller number of mini-symposia exploring higher-level topics. Workshops should complement rather than replicate these sessions by focusing on in-depth discussions and collaborative problem-solving rather than strategic planning.\r
\r
Evaluation criteria\r
\r
The All Hands Programme Committee will evaluate submissions based on the following criteria:\r
\r
\r
	Demonstrate a clear alignment with at least one of the four Strategic Tiers (Science, Technology, Nodes and People)\r
	Require collaboration across multiple ELIXIR groups (Platforms, Communities, Focus Groups) to address a shared scientific or technical challenge connected to ELIXIR’s core mission\r
	Need dynamic input and interaction from participants, with a focus on collaborative problem-solving, discussion or brainstorming, rather than passive presentations\r
	Have clear goals and a potential for meaningful outcomes relevant to the ELIXIR Scientific Programme and Commissioned Services\r
\r
\r
Requirements for workshop leads \r
\r
The lead and co-lead of each selected workshop are expected to attend the meeting in person, as attendance allocations will only be reserved for these two leads.\r
	Other participants must register in the usual way, with the option to participate remotely.\r
	Proposals must include a description of the session’s virtual components, ensuring meaningful engagement for remote participants.\r
\r
Submission details\r
\r
Word limit: 400 words\r
	Platform: Submit via Oxford Abstracts\r
	Key dates:\r
\r
\r
	Call opens: 25 November 2024, 08:00 UTC\r
	Call closes: 20 January 2025, 16:00 UTC\r
\r
\r
Don’t miss this opportunity to shape the future of ELIXIR through collaboration and by addressing shared challenges within the life science community.\r
\r
Data privacy\r
\r
Please see our Data Privacy document for more information.\r
\r
Code of Conduct \r
\r
	\r
		The ELIXIR Code of Conduct has been created to ensure that people at ELIXIR events can interact with each other in a respectful and safe environment. It provides ways you can voice your concern if you believe there has been a breach to this Code of Conduct\r
		The ELIXIR Code of Conduct will be in place at this event.""" ;
