<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-bioinformatics-industry-forum> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """To avoid the risk of attendees being exposed to or infected with Coronavirus (COVID-19), quarantined or restricted in their travel, we have made the decision to change the ELIXIR Bioinformatics Industry Forum and move from a face-to-face meeting to a series of virtual events. \r
\r
 \r
\r
With the ELIXIR Bioinformatics Industry Forum we want to build a community for technical specialists to discuss visionary ideas, bottlenecks and solutions to some of the major challenges in the data driven life science sector. What unites all participants is the drive to move science forward through a collaborative effort.\r
\r
Follow-on Webinars \r
\r
\r
	Exploiting semantics web technology for a service cross-talk between companies; Blanca Jordan (Atos) Sira Sarntivijai (ELIXIR)    5th May 2020  \r
	Open source Software in the Life Sciences; Alex Wade (Chan Zuckerberg Initiative) Jen Harrow (ELIXIR Tools)   28th May 2020 \r
	Large scale cloud computing in the life sciences; Chair: Jonathan Tedds (ELIXIR Compute) Philipp Maurer (Google Cloud) Tony Wildish (EMBL-EBI) Diana Coman (ETH Zurich/ BioMedIT)   23rd June 2020\r
\r
\r
 """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2020-04-28 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:event_types "meetings_and_conferences" ;
