<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-compute-platform-2024-face-to-face-meeting> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """We are pleased to invite you to join for the forthcoming ELIXIR Compute Platform face-to-face event in Brno, Czech Republic.\r
\r
Day 1: Wednesday 24th January, 2024 from 09:00-17:00 CET (including lunch)\r
\r
Day 2: Thursday 25th January, 2024 from 09:00-13.00 CET\r
\r
Venue and accomodation\r
\r
The event will take place at the Courtyard Hotel by Marriott, Brno.\r
\r
For those requiring accomodation we reccomend attendees to stay at the same hotel as the event. Room bookings can be made on the Courtyard Hotel by Marriott, Brno website. The event rate is: 2,650 CZK per night per single room or 2,850 CZK per night per twin room.  \r
\r
If a booking cannot be made due to capacity issues we can reccomend further hotel options in the locale. Please contact Gavin Farrell (gavin.farrell@elixir-europe.org) if requiring additonal suggestions for accomodation. \r
\r
Travel logistics\r
\r
Direct to Brno airport\r
	There are only Ryanair flights from London Stansted.\r
	https://www.ryanair.com/gb/en\r
\r
Via Vienna airport to Brno\r
	We reccommend this option due to faster connection to Brno by direct buses RegioJet or Gepard Express (stop Grand Station, approx. 2 hours drive).\r
	https://regiojet.com/ or https://tickets.gepard.com/\r
\r
Via Prague airport to Brno\r
	From Prague airport, you need to count with approx. 3-3,5 hrs drive to Brno. From the airport, take the Airport Express to the main station (every 30 min) and then train to Brno by České Dráhy or Regiojet.\r
	https://www.cd.cz/en/dalsi-sluzby/navazna-doprava/-27548/\r
	https://regiojet.com/\r
\r
Public transportation in Brno\r
	To the venue Courtyard Hotel, Brno: From the Main Station or Grand Station, take tram 7 or 8 to Křídlovická station and walk 550 meters (~9 mins).\r
	Contactless ticket purchase - https://www.pipniajed.cz/en.html\r
	Tickets are valid for any form of public transport. City centre – zones 100 and 101.\r
\r
Online attendance\r
\r
Through the event registration link it is possible to register for remote attendance. Remote attendance will be possible via our live streaming set-up at the event. \r
\r
Agenda\r
\r
This year’s focus of the Compute Platform will be centred around the new 2024-2026 ELIXIR Compute Platform Work Plan and strategic alignments to complementary compute related projects and initiatives (GAIA-X/GDI/EOSC/EuroHPC/+).\r
\r
The agenda document will be received upon successful attendee registration. """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2024-01-25 13:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Czech Republic" ;
                    schema1:addressLocality "Brno" ;
                    schema1:streetAddress "Courtyard Hotel by Marriott, Brno, Holandská Street 12, 639 00 Brno-Brno-střed" ] ;
            schema1:latitude "49.192244" ;
            schema1:longitude "16.611338" ] ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Compute Platform 2024 Face-to-Face Meeting" ;
    schema1:startDate "2024-01-24 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-compute-platform-2024-face-face-meeting> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-compute-platform-ask-us-anything> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """The ELIXIR Compute Platform will be holding a teleconference on Friday October 11 2019 from 14:00 to 15:00 CEST. It is designed as an "Ask Us Anything” session, with the aim to facilitate interactions between the Platform and the rest of ELIXIR. We will use mentimeter to help capture questions and feedback and use this to build an FAQ page which can be revisited in future. \r
\r
All are invited to attend.  Please mark your calendars, further details will be posted shortly.\r
\r
 """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2019-10-11 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Compute Platform 'Ask Us Anything'" ;
    schema1:startDate "2019-10-11 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-compute-platform-ask-us-anything> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-compute-platform-face-to-face-meeting-may-2019> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """ELIXIR Compute Platform are holding their annual face-to-face meeting at the Wellcome Trust in London. This face-to-face meeting follows on from the Lyon meeting in October 2018 and comes at a key moment as we conclude the work of EXCELERATE and begin new streams of activity in the core platform programme for 2019-21 including the ELIXIR AAI Infrastructure Service, the cross platform Containers Strategic Implementation Study and related externally funded activities including EOSC-Life, CINECA and our GA4GH collaborations.\r
\r
Please find the provisional agenda.\r
\r
 \r
\r
This Compute Platform meeting follows the first ELIXIR Bioinformatics Suppliers Forum (EBSF) the day before, 7 May 2019, at the same location. We hope that you will be able to attend both this Compute Platform meeting as well as the EBSF. There is a seperate registration for EBSF and you must register for both events seperately if you wish to attend.\r
\r
Please note, we plan to have a networking dinner the evening of Wednesday 8th May. During the resgitration, please indicate if you would like to attend the dinner.\r
\r
We look forward to seeing you in London!\r
\r
Location\r
\r
Henry Auditorium, Wellcome Collection, 183 Euston Road, London NW1 2BE\r
\r
Contacts\r
\r
For all agenda inquiries, please contact: Jonathan Tedds (jonathan.tedds@elixir-europe.org) \r
\r
For all logistical inquiries, please contact: Melissa Balzano (melissa.balzano@elixir-europe.org) """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2019-05-09 16:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:event_types "meetings_and_conferences" ;
