<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-data-carpentry-ljubljana> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0622>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3071>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3316> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Master students" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "PhD students" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Life Science Researchers" ] ;
    schema1:description """**ELIXIR Data Carpentry for Genomics - Ljubljana**\r
\r
**29-30 Jan 2019, Faculty of Medicine, Vrazov trg 2, Ljubljana (Slovenia)**\r
\r
**ELIXIR Data Carpentry for Genomics** is a course intended for all those who would like to learn more about the basics of data processing and data management in the field of genomics.\r
\r
The course will be in English. **The limit of participants is 20.** If there are more applicants than available places, the participants will be selected based on their institutional and geographic background, while also taking into account the time of their registration. The course is free of charge. You can find more info about the course on the [**ELIXIR-SI eLearning Platform (EeLP)**](https://elixir.mf.uni-lj.si/course/view.php?id=44).\r
\r
The course will take place in the computer classroom at the **Institute of Biostatistics and Medical Informatics (IBMI)**, Faculty of Medicine, Vrazov trg 2, Ljubljana. \r
\r
Sessions will be intensive and hands-on, and taught by experienced data carpentry instructors. Instructors will be **Vasilis Lenis (University of Plymouth, UK)** and **Živa Ramšak (ELIXIR Slovenia; National Institute of Biology Ljubljana)**. The course is recommended for anyone who would like to learn more about how to process and manage big scale genomic data.\r
\r
**Program topics:**\r
* Introduction - Presentation of ELIXIR Slovenia and ELIXIR-SI eLearning Platform\r
* Project management in genomics and introduction to cloud computing\r
* Introduction to Linux/Unix command line\r
* Data wrangling and processing for genomics\r
\r
The course is organised by **ELIXIR Slovenia** in collaboration with **ELIXIR Hub** and **Data &amp; Software Carpentry**.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
