<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-outreach-webinar-with-latin-america-data-management-and-training-opportunities-for-engagement> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """\r
\r
This is the first joint webinar between ELIXIR, the Argentinean Association of Bioinformatics and Computational Biology (A2B2C), the Iberoamerican Society of Bioinformatics (SOIBIO), the Mexican Network of Bioinformatics (BioNetMX) and the European Conference for Computational Biology (ECCB). The aim is to provide an overview of ELIXIR data management, training activities, as well as opportunities for engagement for Latin American scientists. The webinar is openly accessible and we encourage anyone interested in the programme to join!\r
\r
This event will take place from 14:00 –16:30 (CEST).\r
\r
The connection details can be found in the programme, which is available on Google Drive and is as follows:\r
\r
\r
	\r
		\r
			Time\r
			Presentation\r
		\r
		\r
			14:00 - 14:05\r
			Welcome and Introduction\r
				José María Carazo, Spanish National Center for Biotechnology (CNB-CSIC), INB/ELIXIR Spain and Andrew Smith, ELIXIR Head of External Relations\r
		\r
		\r
			14:05 - 14:20\r
			\r
				ELIXIR Europe: overview and opportunities\r
					Andrew Smith, ELIXIR Head of External Relations\r
			\r
		\r
		\r
			14:20 - 14:35\r
			Development and evolution of Bioinformatics Societies in Latin America: A2B2C (Argentina), AB3C (Brasil), BIOCANET (Costa Rica &amp; Panama), BioNetMX (Mexico), SC2B2 (Colombia), SCB (Chile), SPB2C (Peru) and SOIBIO (Iberoamerica)\r
				Javier De Las Rivas, Cancer Research Center (CiC-IBMCC), (Cancer Research Center IBMCC, from CSIC &amp; University of Salamanca, President of SOIBIO and Member of INB/ELIXIR-Spain)\r
		\r
		\r
			14:35 - 14:45\r
			AB3C (title to be confirmed).\r
				Marcelo Brandão, University Estadual de Campinas, Brazil\r
		\r
		\r
			14:45 - 14:55\r
			Creating paths for the development and application of bioinformatics in Mexico Irma Martínez-Flores or Shirley Alquicira-Hernández, Center for Genomic Sciences, Mexico\r
		\r
		\r
			14:55 - 15:05\r
			Bioinformatics in Argentina: The first 10+3 years of A2B2C\r
				Nicolás Palopoli, National Scientific and Technical Research Council, Argentina \r
		\r
		\r
			15:05 - 15:30\r
			Break\r
		\r
		\r
			15:30 - 15:45\r
			Frederik Coppens, ELIXIR Belgium\r
				Research data management (RDM) in ELIXIR and insight into the RDM Toolkit\r
		\r
		\r
			15:45 - 16:00\r
			ELIXIR Training activities and opportunities for engagement\r
				Katharina Heil, ELIXIR Communities Coordinator, Jessica Lindvall, ELIXIR Training Platform ExCo and Fotis Psomopoulos, ELIXIR Training Platform ExCo\r
		\r
		\r
			16:00 - 16:30\r
			Open Discussion\r
		\r
		\r
			16:30\r
			Close\r
		\r
	\r
""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2022-09-20 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Outreach webinar with Latin America - Data management and training: Opportunities for engagement" ;
    schema1:startDate "2022-09-20 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-outreach-webinar-latin-america-data-management-and-training-opportunities-engagement> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-rdm-community-meeting> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """The ELIXIR RDM Community meeting will take place from 12:00 CET on 4 December, to 14:00 CET on 6 December 2023. It will include the kick-off for the ELIXIR RDM Community Implementation Study, on the afternoon of 5 December and the morning of 6 December. This meeting is planned as a hybrid meeting, with the F2F component in Bergen, Norway. \r
\r
Meeting content\r
\r
The meeting will include presentations, workshops and participant engagement. An agenda will be shared closer to the event. \r
\r
After having finalised the RDM Community white paper and Implementation Study proposal, this meeting is an opportunity to come together in-person and start the joint work and community exchange.\r
\r
Participation\r
\r
This meeting has a limit of in-person attendees, with no-limit on virtual participant numbers. A number of selected invited participants will receive funding for F2F attendance of the meeting. Additionally, parts will need to be covered via (to be allocated) Implementation Study travel budget. Details regarding funding and reimbursement will be shared after registration. Please do not book any travel until after you have been notified. \r
\r
Travel and venue\r
\r
Once notified of your F2F attendance you will be expected to make your own travel and accommodation arrangements to the venue. Reimbursement information will be shared with invited attendees after their successful registration.\r
\r
The closest airport is BERGEN (BGO), while travel by plane is the fastest option, there is also the possibility to reach Bergen by train (optional overnight) from Oslo or by ferry from Denmark. \r
\r
The venue is centrally located in Bergen and easy to reach by tram (~45min, ~4€), bus (~30min, ~20€) and taxi (~25min, 80€) from Bergen airport. You can find the connection details on the page of the public transport provider.\r
\r
Recommended accommodation (please consider shared reimbursement rules)\r
\r
After registration, we will supply you with a booking code for Scandic Ornen, which is also the venue.\r
\r
Other hotels in 5-10 min walking distance  from venue:\r
\r
\r
	Zander K Hotel\r
	Grand Hotel Terminus \r
	Citybox Bergen City  (often most budget friendly hotel option)\r
	Hotel Park\r
	Various other options\r
\r
\r
Registration deadline: 6 November 2023 (F2F), 3 December 2023 (virtual)\r
\r
Contacts\r
\r
Clare Garrard (clare.garrard@elixir-europe.org), event related questions and logistics\r
\r
Katharina Heil (katharina.heil@elixir-europe.org), any other questions""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2023-12-06 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Norway" ;
                    schema1:addressLocality "Bergen" ] ;
            schema1:latitude "60.394306" ;
            schema1:longitude "5.325919" ] ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR RDM Community meeting" ;
    schema1:startDate "2023-12-04 12:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-rdm-community-meeting> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-romania-webinar> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """You are invited to join this webinar introducing the work of ELIXIR in anticipation of establishing the ELIXIR Romania Node. This is particularly intended for BioInformatics Community within Romania, ahead of a workshop in association with the Romanian Society of BioInformaticians in April, setting out the range of opportunities to participate in a range of European-wide Life Science activities. \r
\r
Speakers: \r
\r
\r
	\r
		\r
			\r
				Mihail Anton\r
\r
				Senior Science Officer\r
\r
				Chairing the Webinar\r
			\r
			\r
		\r
		\r
			\r
				Andy Smith \r
\r
				ELIXIR Director (Interim) \r
					&amp; Head of External Relations.         \r
\r
				Introducing ELIXIR\r
			\r
			 \r
		\r
		\r
			\r
				 \r
\r
				Peter Maccallum \r
\r
				ELIXIR Chief Technical Officer\r
\r
				ELIXIR Platforms \r
			\r
			 \r
				\r
			\r
		\r
		\r
			\r
				Clare Garrard\r
\r
				Scientific Officer \r
\r
				ELIXIR Communities\r
			\r
			\r
		\r
	\r
\r
\r
There will be an opportunity to pose questions both to this webinar and at the later Workshop. \r
\r
This event builds on a series of webinars in 2020 (link) """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2024-03-07 16:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Romania Webinar" ;
    schema1:startDate "2024-03-07 16:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-romania-webinar> .

