<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-single-cell-community-workshop-first-steps-in-building-the-community-and-white-paper> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """This workshop aims to consolidate key themes and challenges in the Single Cell Omics field, which the emerging ELIXIR Community will tackle.\r
\r
Everyone with an interest in the field of Single Cell Omics is welcome to join the workshop, which will be divided into three main parts: \r
\r
\r
	Introduction of the field and focus, with highlight presentations \r
	Joint discussion around the Community's themes and challenges\r
	Identification of key themes and planning of the white paper writing. \r
\r
\r
A more detailed agenda will be shared closer in time. """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2021-09-16 13:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Single-Cell Community workshop - First steps in building the Community and white paper" ;
    schema1:startDate "2021-09-16 10:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-single-cell-community-workshop-first-steps-building-community-and-white-paper> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-single-cell-omics-community-f2f-hybrid-meeting> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """The ELIXIR Single Cell Omics Community meeting takes place from 12:00 CET on Monday, December 5th to 14:00 CET on Tuesday,December 6th, 2022. This meeting is planned as a hybrid meeting, with the F2F component at SciLifeLab (Tomtebodavägen 23b, Gamma Building), Stockholm, Sweden.\r
\r
Following up the Single-Cell Omics Community white paper this meeting is an opportunity to come together in-person for the first time and start organising and planning the Community work including its Implementation Study (SCONE).\r
\r
The meeting will include presentations, workshops and participant engagement. \r
\r
The (preliminary) agenda can be found here.\r
\r
This meeting has a limit of in-person attendees, with no-limit on virtual participant numbers. A number of selected invited participants will receive funding to attend the meeting. These will be specifically informed regarding the reimbursement arrangements. \r
\r
Registration Deadline\r
\r
F2F attendance: Monday, November 14th, 2022\r
\r
Virtual attendance: Sunday, December 4th, 2022\r
\r
 \r
\r
Additional Registration information\r
\r
All registrants will be informed via email regarding their registration (including funded F2F, other F2F and virtual participants). Please do not book any travel till after you have been notified.  \r
\r
 \r
\r
Travel and venue\r
\r
Once notified of your F2F attendance you will be expected to make your own travel and accommodation arrangements to the venue, reimbursement information will be shared with invited attendees after their successful registration. Once this occurred, please: \r
\r
Book your flight to Stockholm Arlanda Airport (ARN)\r
\r
Take the Airport shuttle Flygbussarna (line to Liljeholmen): https://www.flygbussarna.se\r
\r
There will be a stop named “Karolinska Sjukhuset” (Karolinska Hospital) - remember to press the STOP button to let the driver know you will drop in the next stop (otherwise they just drive past it).\r
\r
\r
	 \r
\r
Recommended accommodation (please consider shared reimbursement rules):\r
\r
The closest and most convenient hotel is the Elite Carolina Tower.\r
	https://elite.se/sv/hotell/stockholm/hotel-carolina-tower/\r
\r
 """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2022-12-06 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Sweden" ;
                    schema1:addressLocality "Stockholm, Sweden" ;
                    schema1:streetAddress "SciLifeLab, Tomtebodavägen 23b, Gamma Building" ] ] ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Single-Cell Omics Community F2F/hybrid meeting" ;
    schema1:startDate "2022-12-05 12:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-single-cell-omics-community-f2fhybrid-meeting> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-single-cell-omics-community-f2f-hybrid-meeting-24129532-dd30-4a63-94c1-40d7a65d7667> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """This year, we are combining the annual community gathering with the FAIR Data Management Workshop. The annual meeting is scheduled for October 18th and will be hosted at the EMBL-EBI Campus in Hinxton, UK. Following that, the workshop will take place from October 19th to 20th, 2023.\r
\r
During the workshop, the focus will be on discussing and sharing practices related to FAIR data management. The agenda includes insights from members of the Single Cell Omics Community who will present their data production and analysis workflows. Challenges in reusing others' data and creating usable datasets will also be addressed. The aim is to establish best practices in managing research data and pinpoint key areas where the community requires improvements to enhance data FAIRness. The workshop is scheduled for a duration of two days, from morning to lunchtime.\r
\r
The current agenda (draft) can be found here.\r
\r
Seats for the in-person segment of the meeting are limited, whereas there is no cap on the number of virtual participants. Those who receive invitations to attend will be offered funding based on their participation in either one or both parts of the event, as well as their involvement in the implementation study. Detailed information about funding and reimbursement will be provided after registration. We kindly request that you refrain from making any travel arrangements until you have received a confirmation notification.\r
\r
Travel and venue\r
\r
Once notified of your F2F attendance you will be expected to make your own travel and accommodation arrangements to the venue, reimbursement information will be shared with invited attendees after their successful registration.  \r
\r
Recommended accommodation (please consider shared reimbursement rules):\r
\r
Hinxton Hall  \r
\r
To book, please click on this link: https://booking.hinxtonhall.org/. Online bookings can only be made up until 8 days prior to your arrival date (up until the 9th October 2023).\r
	1. Enter dates, number of rooms required and your bespoke Promo Code: KX26180-AK\r
	2. Please add any special requirements you may have in the booking notes section when you complete your personal details.\r
	3. Complete the Worldpay card payment steps fully in order to confirm your reservation.\r
\r
You will automatically receive confirmation from Hinxton Hall of your booking following successful payment. * If you do not receive a confirmation email please do not assume your booking is confirmed – please contact our Reception Team on +44 (0)1223 495000 or at conference.reception@hinxtonhall.org to check your booking has been processed fully.\r
\r
 \r
\r
Registration deadlines: \r
\r
F2F registration deadline: 27 September  2023\r
\r
Virtual registration deadline: 16 October 2023\r
\r
Contacts:\r
\r
Clare Garrard  clare.garrard@elixir-europe.org  \r
\r
Katharina Heil katharina.heil@elixir-europe.org \r
\r
 """ ;
