<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-software-carpentry-ljubljana> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_2269>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3071>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3316> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "PhD students" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Master students" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Beginners in statistics" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Life Science Researchers" ] ;
    schema1:description """**ELIXIR Software Carpentry - Ljubljana**\r
\r
**16-17 May 2019, Faculty of Medicine,** \r
**Vrazov trg 2, Ljubljana (Slovenia)**\r
\r
ELIXIR Software Carpentry is a workshop intended for all those \r
who would like to learn more about the basics of R - \r
software environment used in bioinformatics \r
for statistical computing and graphics. \r
The workshop will include a keynote lecture \r
about data management in ELIXIR-SI.\r
\r
The workshop will be in English.\r
\r
The course will take place in the computer classroom \r
at the Institute of Biostatistics and Medical Informatics (IBMI), \r
Faculty of Medicine, Vrazov trg 2, Ljubljana.\r
\r
**The course is free of charge. The limit of participants is 20.** \r
If the number of registered applicants exceeds this limit, \r
selection of participants will be made. \r
It will be based on the time of their registration and their affiliations, \r
as well as geographic distribution.\r
\r
Sessions will be intensive and hands-on, \r
and taught by experienced software carpentry instructors. \r
The course is recommended for anyone \r
who would like to learn more about using statistical computing and graphics \r
in the bioinformatics field, both for research or operational work.\r
\r
**Program topics:**\r
- Keynote lecture about ELIXIR-SI data management\r
- Introduction to Linux/Unix command line\r
- Git\r
- R\r
\r
**The course is organised by ELIXIR Slovenia \r
in collaboration with Data &amp; Software Carpentry.**\r
\r
More info about the course is available on the **[ELIXIR-SI eLearning Platform (EeLP)](https://elixir.mf.uni-lj.si/course/view.php?id=46)**.""" ;
