<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-tools-for-reproducible-research> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description "One of the key principles of proper scientific procedure is the act of repeating an experiment or analysis and being able to reach similar conclusions. Published research based on computational analysis, e.g. bioinformatics or computational biology, have often suffered from incomplete method descriptions (e.g. list of used software versions); unavailable raw data; and incomplete, undocumented and/or unavailable code. This essentially prevents any possibility of attempting to reproduce the results of such studies. The term “reproducible research” has been used to describe the idea that a scientific publication based on computational analysis should be distributed along with all the raw data and metadata used in the study, all the code and/or computational notebooks needed to produce results from the raw data, and the computational environment or a complete description thereof. Reproducible research not only leads to proper scientific conduct but also provides other researchers the access to build upon previous work. Most importantly, the person setting up a reproducible research project will quickly realize the immediate personal benefits: an organized and structured way of working. The person that most often has to reproduce your own analysis is your future self!" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "online" ;
            schema1:endDate "2021-11-19 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:maximumAttendeeCapacity 20 ;
            schema1:startDate "2021-11-15 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:inLanguage "en" ;
    schema1:name "Tools for Reproducible Research" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "NBIS" ;
            schema1:url <http://nbis.se> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://uppsala.instructure.com/courses/51980> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-tools-platform-f2f-hybrid-meeting> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """The ELIXIR Tools Platform meeting is confirmed to take place from Monday, 27 March (12:00 CET) to Wednesday, 29 March (17:00 CET) in Leiden. This will be a hybrid meeting but F2F participation  is encouraged. The meeting will include presentations and discussions in particular focussed on planning for the new ELIXIR Programme for 2024-28. \r
\r
Date\r
\r
Monday - Wednesday, 27-29 March 2023\r
\r
\r
	Day 1, 12:00 - 17:00 CET: Tools Platform meeting  (start after lunch)\r
	Day 2, 09:00 - 17:00 CET: Tools Platform  meeting (two breakout rooms after lunch)\r
	Day 3, 09:00 - 17:00 CET: Tools Platform meeting (two breakout rooms)\r
\r
\r
Location\r
\r
Fletcher Wellness-Hotel Leiden is located in the building LEVEL. This is a tall modern building next to station Leiden Centraal, on the side of LUMC. The reception of Fletcher Wellness-Hotel Leiden is located at centre C on the 12th level of the building. \r
\r
There is a direct train link from Schiphol Airport, Amsterdam and also a train link from Rotterdam to Leiden Centraal in 25-35 minutes.\r
\r
The venue offers rooms to stay. Alternatively, there are plenty of hotels around such as an Ibis hotel next to the Leiden Centraal.\r
\r
Agenda\r
\r
A tentative agenda for the meeting can be found here.\r
\r
Hub Contact\r
\r
Jonathan Tedds (Programme Manager for Scientific Computing; ELIXIR Compute Platform, Tools Platform &amp; EOSC Coordinator)\r
	jonathan.tedds@elixir-europe.org\r
\r
Manthos Pitoulias (ELIXIR Senior Scientific Officer; Bioinformatics - Tools &amp; Training Platforms)\r
	manthos.pitoulias@elixir-europe.org""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2023-03-29 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Netherlands" ;
                    schema1:addressLocality "Leiden, Netherlands" ;
                    schema1:postalCode "2333" ;
                    schema1:streetAddress "Fletcher Wellness Hotel Leiden, Bargelaan 180" ] ] ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Tools Platform F2F Hybrid Meeting" ;
    schema1:startDate "2023-03-27 12:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-tools-platform-f2f-hybrid-meeting> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-toxicology-community-f2f-hybrid-meeting> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """The aim of the meeting is to provide an update to the ELIXIR Toxicology Community on the implementation study, as it was submitted on 14 July,  and discuss collaboration with the Partnership for the Assessment of Risks from Chemicals (PARC, eu-parc.eu) and other toxicology projects, for leveraging the FAIRification of toxicology data and ELIXIR life sciences infrastructure for toxicology.\r
\r
The meeting will facilitate knowledge sharing, address concerns, gather input, and foster collaboration to achieve the project's objectives. It also aims to explore synergies between ELIXIR and PARC. Overall, the meeting aims to strengthen the ELIXIR Toxicology Community, advance the implementation study, and promote FAIR practices in toxicology data management.\r
\r
This meeting has a limit of in-person attendees, with no-limit on virtual participant numbers. \r
\r
Details regarding funding and reimbursement will be shared after registration. \r
\r
Please do not book any travel till after you have been notified.\r
\r
Additional Registration information\r
\r
Please note, if you have selected to attend the face to face meeting, this option is limited to first come first served basis. All registrants will be informed via email regarding their registration. Please do not book any travel till after you have been notified.  \r
\r
Travel and venue\r
\r
Venue: Campus Brussels, Maastricht University, Tervurenlaan 153, 1150, Sint-Pieters-Woluwe, Belgium, and online via Zoom (via ELIXIR Hub Zoom Account).\r
\r
Best is to travel to Brussel Central Station, then take metro line 1, to Montgomery metro station (direction Stockel), exit the metro station in south/south west ward direction.\r
\r
Public transportation by train: https://www.belgiantrain.be/en.\r
\r
Once notified of your F2F attendance you will be expected to make your own travel and accommodation arrangements to the venue, reimbursement information will be shared with invited attendees after their successful registration. \r
\r
F2F registration deadline: 1 September  \r
\r
Virtual registration deadline: 19 September\r
\r
Contacts: \r
\r
Clare Garrard  clare.garrard@elixir-europe.org \r
\r
Katharina Heil katharina.heil@elixir-europe.org\r
\r
 \r
\r
 """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2023-09-20 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Netherlands" ;
                    schema1:addressLocality "1150 Sint-Pieters-Woluwe" ;
                    schema1:postalCode "1150" ;
                    schema1:streetAddress "Campus Brussels, Maastricht University, Tervurenlaan 153" ] ] ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Toxicology Community F2F/hybrid meeting" ;
    schema1:startDate "2023-09-20 09:30:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-toxicology-community-f2fhybrid-meeting> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-toxicology-community-webinar-1> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Introduction and preparation of the ELIXIR workshop:\r
\r
				"Empowering Toxicology Research - Leveraging ELIXIR Data Solutions". \r
\r
				 \r
\r
				This webinar will provide insights into how two of the ELIXIR platforms (Data and Interoperability) can change toxicological data management, tackling challenges faced by toxicology research consortia like 'Partnership for the Assessment of Risks from Chemicals' (PARC), the 'Animal-free Safety assessment of chemicals: Project cluster for Implementation of novel Strategies' (ASPIS) and 'NanoSafety Cluster' (NSC). \r
			\r
		\r
	\r
\r
\r
Webinar Speakers: \r
\r
\r
	\r
		\r
			\r
				\r
			\r
			\r
			\r
			\r
			\r
		\r
		\r
			Marvin Martens\r
			Ulrike Wittig\r
			Susanna-Assunta Sansone\r
			Phillipe Rocca-Serra\r
			Allyson Lister\r
		\r
	\r
\r
\r
We will start the webinar with an introduction to the ELIXIR Data and Interoperability platforms, given by two of the leaders (Ulrike Wittig &amp; Susanna-Assunta Sansone) who reveal the powerful tools and resources they provide for data FAIRness, as well as then activities in the current programme of work. We then delve deeper into the application for the toxicology community, with the FAIRsharing Collection by the ELIXIR Toxicology Community, and discuss the pressing data challenges within PARC, ASPIS and NSC and specifically discuss and explore a.o. the use of ELIXIR resources for developing compact identifiers and FAIR-ification of Adverse Outcome Pathways\r
\r
This webinar serves as preparation for the free-of-charge 2-days hands-on workshop entitled "FAIR-ification of Toxicological Research Output: Leveraging ELIXIR Resources" to be held on 28-29 May 2024 in Utrecht, The Netherlands. This is the first of five workshops organized during 2024 -2025 by the ELIXIR Toxicology Community as part of their Implementation Study (INTOXICOM). Registration is now open. \r
	 \r
\r
Links to resources mentioned in the Webinar: \r
\r
\r
	Recommended Interoperability Resources\r
	RDMkit\r
	FAIRcookbook\r
	ELIXIR Toxicology Collection in FAIRsharing\r
	FAIRsharing Champions\r
\r
\r
\r
	\r
		\r
			 \r
			 """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2024-05-02 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Toxicology Community Webinar 1" ;
    schema1:startDate "2024-05-02 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-toxicology-community-webinar-1> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-toxicology-community-webinar-2> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """You are invited to jon a preparatory webinar ahead of the workshop entitled: \r
\r
"Enhancing Research Output: FAIR documentation and Tool Management for toxicology studies"\r
\r
During this one-hour meeting participants can introduce themselves. In a co-creation-style we will finalize the details of the programme based on the scheme below. A short summary of the first workshop will be presented.\r
\r
\r
	\r
		\r
			\r
				This workshop is a face-to-face, free-of-charge hands-on workshop, organised in the context of the first implementation study (INTOXICOM) of the ELIXIR Toxicology Community.  See the ELIXIR Toxicology Community Whitepaper for more in-depth information about the community's goals. This workshop will feature keynote lectures and hands-on sessions. This workshop will continue with the concept of the FAIR Cookbook recipe and focus on what is needed to submit the recipe. We will also address existing tools to manage research output. Specifically, we will write DS-Wizard templates and focus here on the use of ontologies like EDAM to annotate research output and registering of the output in the suitable ELIXIR platform.\r
					ELIXIR solutions we like to see adopted from the toxicology community include the DS-Wizard, EDAM ontology, and to continue to populate ELIXIR registries with toxicology resources, such as bio.tools, FAIRsharing, TeSS, and the FAIR Cookbook. This workshop will also feature hands-on lectures. Dr. Sara Morsy will give a hands-on lecture on How to make toxicology training materials FAIR. Expected outcomes include model templates for software, such as predictive toxicology solutions for EOSC and bio.tools and scientific models, such as AOPs, PBPK, and QSAR models.\r
					The location of the second workshop is the University of Basel, Petersplatz 1, 4001 Basel Switzerland, Main building, Kollegienhaus - lecture hall (Hörsaal) 120, get directions from maps.\r
			\r
			\r
				 \r
			\r
		\r
	\r
\r
\r
Webinar Speakers: \r
\r
\r
	\r
		\r
			\r
				\r
			\r
			\r
		\r
		\r
			 Egon Willighagen (NL)\r
			Sara Morsy (UK)\r
		\r
	\r
\r
\r
Intended participants:\r
\r
\r
	Toxicologists interested in using FAIR data resources for their research or making their data FAIR, as well as data managers and researchers working with AOPs.\r
	Toxicology lecturers /trainers who would like to invest in making trainings FAIR.\r
\r
\r
Registration is now open\r
\r
Workshop details\r
\r
\r
	27-28 November 2024\r
	University of Basel, Switzerland\r
\r
\r
Workshop Organisers: \r
\r
\r
	\r
		\r
			\r
				\r
			\r
			\r
			\r
			\r
		\r
		\r
			 Egon Willighagen (NL)\r
			Danyel Jennen (NL)\r
			Thomas Exner (UK)\r
			Nina Jeliazkova (BG)\r
		\r
	\r
\r
\r
Links to resources mentioned in the Webinar: \r
\r
\r
	Recommended Interoperability Resources\r
	RDMkit\r
	FAIRcookbook\r
	ELIXIR Toxicology Collection in FAIRsharing\r
	FAIRsharing Champions\r
\r
\r
\r
	\r
		\r
			 \r
			 """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2024-11-13 15:30:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Toxicology Community Webinar 2" ;
    schema1:startDate "2024-11-13 15:30:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-toxicology-community-webinar-2> .

