<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-ttr-course-basic-genomics-using-advanced-analysis-tools> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0622> ;
    schema1:alternateName "Genomic Data Science with Galaxy" ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "beginner bioinformaticians" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Postgraduate students" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "life scientists" ] ;
    schema1:description """**NEW DATE FOR THE COURSE HAS BEEN SET: Dec. 20-21**\r
\r
**ELIXIR TtR course: Basic genomics using advanced analysis tools\r
Genomic Data Science with Galaxy**\r
**December 20-21, 2018**, Faculty of Medicine, Vrazov trg 2, Ljubljana (Slovenia)\r
\r
Galaxy is an open source, web-based platform for data intensive biomedical research. The Galaxy Platform provides user friendly software for producing reproducible genomic pipelines for data analysis. This workshop will provide a 2 day introductory session to Galaxy software system.\r
\r
The course will be in English.\r
\r
The course will take place in the computer classroom at the Institute of Biostatistics and Medical Informatics (IBMI), Faculty of Medicine, Vrazov trg 2, Ljubljana.\r
\r
**The limit of participants is 20**.\r
\r
This course will focus on introducing the Galaxy user interface and how it can be used for basic genomic analyses. Sessions will be intensive and hands-on, and taught by experienced instructors from the Galaxy Community. We will cover the basic features of Galaxy, including where to find tools, how to import and use your data, and an introduction to workflows. This session is recommended for anyone who has not used, or only rarely uses Galaxy.\r
\r
**Program topics:**\r
Quick introduction to Galaxy UI (20.12. morning)\r
From peaks to genes (20.12. morning)\r
Reference-based RNA-seq - Quality control (20.12. afternoon)\r
Reference-based RNA-seq - Sequencing (21.12. morning)\r
Lecturers will be **Christophe Antoniewski** and **Olivier Inizan** from ELIXIR France.\r
\r
Course is organised by **ELIXIR Slovenia** in collaboration with **ELIXIR France**.\r
\r
ELIXIR is an European ESFRI priority research infrastructure for bioinformatics that provides databases, (software) tools, services and training (including training materials) for information, cloud storage and supercomputers in the area of life sciences. It coordinates, develops, integrates and sustains life science (bioinformatics) resources across Europe.\r
\r
**Prerequisites:**\r
Wi-Fi enabled laptop with a modern web browser. Latest versions of Google Chrome, Firefox, Safari and Opera will work best.\r
\r
**Location: Faculty of Medicine, University of Ljubljana**\r
\r
If you have any questions about this course, please contact ELIXIR-SI""" ;
