<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-de-nbi-cloud-integration-to-elixir-aai> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """The de.NBI cloud is a fully academic cloud infrastructure, free of charge for academic users, where currently five cloud centers provide compute and storage resources.\r
\r
During 2017, de.NBI was integrated into ELIXIR AAI which acts as a backbone for the connection of the five compute centers and allows users to manage cloud projects and access the cloud infrastructure using the authentication service of their home institutions.\r
\r
In this webinar, Peter Belmann (de.NBI cloud governance) will present how de.NBI makes use of ELIXIR AAI and demonstrate how a potential user logs in to the portal, applies for and manages his project, and finally starts using the assigned resources in the cloud.\r
\r
Michal Prochazka of ELIXIR-CZ will complement Peter’s presentation by describing how the integration was done on the ELIXIR AAI side.\r
	 """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2018-03-07 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: de.NBI Cloud Integration to ELIXIR AAI" ;
    schema1:startDate "2018-03-07 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-denbi-cloud-integration-elixir-aai> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-discovering-the-latest-ega-features-quality-control-and-data-submission-portal> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """\r
\r
What to expect\r
\r
The European Genome-phenome Archive (EGA) offers permanent archiving and sharing of all types of personally identifiable genetic and phenotypic data from research projects and healthcare studies.\r
\r
During this webinar, you will discover the latest features of the EGA:\r
\r
\r
	Quality control portal for checking BAM, VCFs and FastQ files\r
	New submitter portal, under development\r
\r
\r
You will learn how to submit data to the EGA directly from the experts at the Centre for Genomic Regulation (CRG). \r
\r
Who should attend\r
\r
\r
	Bioinformaticians\r
	Researchers submitting data to the EGA\r
	Experts interested in joining the Federated EGA in the near future or the long term\r
""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2021-06-16 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: Discovering the latest EGA features. Quality control and data submission portal" ;
    schema1:startDate "2021-06-16 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/discovering-latest-ega-features> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-elixir-beacon-beacon-network-as-a-service> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """This webinar will present the ELIXIR Beacon &amp; Beacon Network As A Service.  \r
\r
Beacons present an easy-to-implement strategy for determining whether an institution has genomic data in its data set that would be useful to share. Beacon networks consist of registries of multiple Beacons, in different locations, which can be queried through a common intercace or gateway protocol. The ELIXIR Beacon Network is a collection of Beacons from ELIXIR Nodes, which - among other features - implement controlled access options by leveraging the ELIXIR AAI.\r
\r
More information: https://beacon-project.io\r
\r
Note: If you are having technical issues connecting to the webinar session, please download and install the latest webex software on your computer from: https://www.webex.com/downloads.html.\r
\r
 """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2019-10-16 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: ELIXIR Beacon & Beacon Network As A Service" ;
    schema1:startDate "2019-10-16 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-elixir-beacon-beacon-network-service> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-elixir-operations> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description "The scientific direction of ELIXIR is laid out in the Scientific Programme 2019-23 and in annual Work Plans which describe the activities that take place in each year. To facilitate the delivery of the Scientific Programme, ELIXIR has a wealth of resources available to support the whole infrastructure to collaborate and achieve its goals. The Handbook of Operations provides a comprehensive overview of ELIXIR policies, guidelines, recommendations and related procedures that are available via the ELIXIR website and intranet. The Handbook is intended for use by the whole ELIXIR infrastructure, including all individuals in ELIXIR Nodes, ELIXIR Hub staff, ELIXIR Board members, and national funders." ;
    schema1:endDate "2022-06-16 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: ELIXIR Operations" ;
    schema1:startDate "2022-06-16 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-elixir-operations> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-elixir-sl-elearning-platform> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description "This ELIXIR Webinar will present the eLearning Platform developed and managed by ELIXIR Slovenia. More information will be available soon." ;
    schema1:endDate "2018-09-19 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: ELIXIR-SL eLearning Platform" ;
    schema1:startDate "2018-09-19 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-elixir-sl-elearning-platform> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-enabling-a-data-ecosystem-at-the-national-institutes-of-health-nih> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """ELIXIR is honoured to welcome two distinguished speakers from the US National Institutes of Health (NIH) as part of its Webinar Series:\r
\r
\r
	Susan Gregurick is the NIH Associate Director for Data Science and the Director of the Office Data Science Strategy leading the efforts to realise the vision set forth in the NIH Strategic Plan for Data Science.\r
\r
\r
\r
	Ishwar Chandramouliswaran is Program Director and technical lead for the strategy, planning, coordination and oversight of establishing a “FAIR” data and repository ecosystem.\r
\r
\r
Together, they will present on Enabling a Data Ecosystem at the National Institutes of Health:\r
\r
The complexity and volume of basic, translational, and clinical research data generated by NIH supported and conducted research continues to rapidly increase, even more so in the light of the COVID-19 pandemic. To take full advantage of these data, NIH must integrate the collection, storage, analysis, use, and sharing of these data to ensure they are discoverable, interoperable, and reusable according to FAIR practices.\r
\r
This talk will showcase some of the key activities led and coordinated by the Office of Data Science Strategy to realise the vision for a modernised and integrated biomedical data ecosystem including the development of a diverse data science workforce and building strategic partnerships in emerging technologies.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2022-03-24 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: Enabling a Data Ecosystem at the National Institutes of Health (NIH)" ;
    schema1:startDate "2022-03-24 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-enabling-data-ecosystem-national-institutes-health-nih> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-exploring-connected-data-ecosystem-with-scientific-literature> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """One of the main goals of the ELIXIR Data Platform is to build a comprehensive connected data ecosystem with deep links to scientific literature. In this webinar we will provide an overview on how links between biological data from various ELIXIR Data resources and scientific publications can be explored using services offered by Europe PMC.\r
\r
The webinar will be presented by Aravind Venkatesan, Senior Data Scientist in the Literature services team at EMBL-EBI.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2020-04-22 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: Exploring connected data ecosystem with scientific literature" ;
    schema1:startDate "2020-04-22 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/webinar-linking-data-literature> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-exploring-structural-and-functional-annotations-of-idps-with-disprot> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Outline the key features of a DisProt entry​\r
\r
\r
	DisProt entry key features:\r
		\r
			General info\r
			Feature viewer\r
			Annotations of disorder aspects (structural state, transitions, functions GO and functions IDPO)\r
		\r
	\r
	How to perform complex searches in DisProt \r
		\r
			Identify and describe protein functions with the Browse search functionalities:\r
			Customize columns to look for specific functions\r
			Finding the IDPO terms\r
			Describe and analyze thematic datasets\r
		\r
	\r
	How to download the output of a search in DisProt\r
\r
\r
This is the second webinar in the series, "An introduction to DisProt" is available here """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2022-08-23 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: Exploring structural and functional annotations of IDPs with DisProt" ;
    schema1:startDate "2022-08-23 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-exploring-structural-and-functional-annotations-idps-disprot> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-fairification-of-genomic-tracks> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """This ELIXIR webinar will present the ELIXIR Implementation study FAIRification of Genomic Tracks which focused on “FAIRifying” all metadata related to genomic annotation track files.\r
\r
The study modelled a comprehensive JSON Schema that structures the most important metadata of genomic tracks. Taking a highly practical approach to interoperability, the project developed a (1) proof-of-concept of the full interoperability chain from end to end, supporting deposit of track metadata in the TrackHub registry; (2) advanced search capabilities through the newly developed TrackFind service (Web based tool/REST API); as well as  (3) metadata search/data import through clients in end-user analysis tools (GSuite HyperBrowser, EPICO).""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2019-11-06 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: FAIRification of Genomic Tracks" ;
    schema1:startDate "2019-11-06 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-fairification-genomic-tracks> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-fairness-of-the-current-elixir-core-resources> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Postponed! This webinar will not be taking place today (4 Wednesday at 15.00). The new date will be announced here shortly.\r
\r
This webinar will present the outcomes of the ELIXIR Implementation study FAIRness of the current ELIXIR Core resources.\r
\r
The goal of the Implementation study was to apply newly available FAIR metrics/FAIR evaluation software to ELIXIR Core Data Resources (CDRs) and propose steps that would increase the​ their ​FAIRness. The webinar will present the outcomes of the evaluation of the CDR as well as evaluation platform developed within the study.\r
\r
See also the presentation of the Implementation study at the ELIXIR All Hands meeting in Lisbon in June 2019.\r
\r
 """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2019-09-04 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: FAIRness of the current ELIXIR Core Data Resources" ;
    schema1:startDate "2019-09-04 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/webinar-fairness-core-data-resources> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-genetic-discrimination-observatory> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """\r
\r
The Genetic Discrimination Observatory (GDO) is a unique network of researchers and other stakeholders dedicated to researching and preventing discrimination based on genomic and other omic data worldwide.\r
\r
Yann Joly is the Research Director of the Centre of Genomics and Policy, based in the Bioethics Unit, at McGill University, a member of the Canadian Commission for UNESCO and Co-Lead the regulatory and ethics work stream of the Global Alliance for Genomics and Health (GA4GH).\r
\r
Register\r
\r
 \r
\r
 """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2021-04-29 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: Genetic Discrimination Observatory" ;
    schema1:startDate "2021-04-29 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-genetic-discrimination-observatory> .

