<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-improvements-to-ensembl> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Paul Kersey (EMBL-EBI) will present a webinar on the development of a distributed model for Ensembl.  This will enable multiple ELIXIR Nodes  to use a common infrastructure and provide an integrated service to users, each focusing on their own areas of interest and expertise.\r
\r
The work is the outcome of the Ensembl Implementation Study.\r
\r
ELIXIR Webinars usually take place every third Wednesday of the month 15.00 CET and are open for anyone to join. Upcoming webinars.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2017-12-20 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: Improvements to Ensembl" ;
    schema1:startDate "2017-12-20 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-improvements-ensembl> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-increasing-interoperability-between-elixir-protein-structure-and-sequence-resources> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """The webinar presented the outcomes of the ELIXIR Implementation Study 'Increasing Interoperability between ELIXIR Protein Structure and Sequence Resources (CATH, SWISS-MODEL, PDBe and InterPro) and Expanding these Resources with 3D-Models of CATH Domains, built by SWISS-MODEL'.\r
\r
The original aims of the Implementation Study were to increase interoperability between four ELIXIR resources (CATH, SWISS-MODEL, InterPro and PDBe), by building APIs that facilitate the import and export of data between them. The ultimate goal is to improve provision of 3D-Models for protein domain sequences via CATH, SWISS-MODEL and InterPro. This pipeline has been built and deployed and the results are already available in InterPro.\r
\r
The webinar demonstrated the results of this pipeline and explained the overall approach of the project to developing and deploying a collaborative pipeline connecting large resources according to best practices. This includes technical decisions on considerations such as: API design, authentication, web application, worker queues, testing, containerisation, etc. but also data analysis and setting up reliable and repeatable benchmarks.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2019-09-18 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: Increasing Interoperability between ELIXIR Protein Structure and Sequence Resources" ;
    schema1:startDate "2019-09-18 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/webinar-interoperability-protein-structure-sequence-resources> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-mapping-the-landscape-of-biocuration-in-elixir> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """The webinar will present the results of the ELIXIR Implementation Study "Mapping the landscape of Biocuration in ELIXIR" run from December 2018 until May 2020.\r
	\r
	The Implementation study aimed at:\r
\r
\r
	Reviewing and mapping the type of curation work being done, for which databases across ELIXIR, and in which life science/health domains;\r
	Identifying the tools curators are currently using for curation tasks;\r
	Assessing the capacity requirements for new curators and training provision available;\r
\r
\r
The goal was to produce an initial map of (1) biocurators, (2) manually curated knowledgebases and data repositories, (3) curation tools and resources. \r
\r
More information about the content of the webinar and the speaker will be available closer to the webinar date.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2020-11-25 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: Mapping the landscape of Biocuration in ELIXIR" ;
    schema1:startDate "2020-11-25 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/webinar-biocuration> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-mobidb-a-database-of-protein-disorder-and-mobility-annotations> a schema1:Event ;
