<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-on-sustainability-implementation-study> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Representatives from ELIXIR Switzerland will present the outcomes of the ELIXIR Sustainability Implementation Study, focused on reviewing sustainable funding models for knowledge bases, with UniprotKB/Swiss-Prot as a specific use case.\r
\r
Chiara Gabella will present the recent paper published on ELIXIR F1000R channel Funding knowledgebases: Towards a sustainable funding model for the UniProt use case which explored twelve funding models for data resources and applied them on the Universal Protein Resource (UniProt), a key resource for protein sequences and functional information knowledge. The paper shows that most of the models present inconsistencies with open access or equity policies, and that while some models do not allow to cover the total costs, they could potentially be used as a complementary income source.\r
\r
The webinar will also present a new model developed as part of the Implementation Study whereby funding agencies would set aside a fixed percentage of their research grant volumes, which would subsequently be redistributed to core data resources according to well-defined selection criteria. Under this model, compatible with the principles of open science, less than 1% of the total amount dedicated to research grants in the life sciences would be sufficient to cover the costs of the core data resources worldwide, including both knowledgebases and deposition databases.\r
\r
 """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2018-05-16 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar on the Sustainability Implementation Study" ;
    schema1:startDate "2018-05-16 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-sustainability-implementation-study> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-on-the-equal-opportunities-policy> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Catherine Gater (European Bioinformatics Institute (EMBL-EBI)) will present the newly created Equal Opportunities Policy for ELIXIR.\r
\r
The Policy is designed to form part of the Handbook of Operations. It covers recommendations on equal opportunities for the ELIXIR Hub and Nodes, and also ELIXIR’s advisory and governance committees, trainers, events, tools and services and Communities of Practice. The Equal Opportunity Policy for ELIXIR outlines the data and metrics that the Hub and Nodes are recommended to collect relating to equality and diversity. The Policy covers the cycle for data collection, monitoring and feeding this back into practice. Finally, the Equal Opportunities Policy describes strategies for establishing an ELIXIR Equal Opportunities Toolkit and collaborations with other networks and projects.\r
\r
ELIXIR Webinars usually take place every third Wednesday of the month 15.00 CET and are open for anyone to join. Upcoming webinars.\r
\r
 """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2018-03-14 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar on the Equal Opportunities Policy" ;
    schema1:startDate "2018-03-14 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-equal-opportunities-policy> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-on-the-equal-opportunities-strategy> a schema1:Event ;
