<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-on-the-systems-biology-implementation-study> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Alan Bridge (ELIXIR Switzerland) will present outcomes from the Systems Biology Implementation Study which looks at the requirements for a European bioinformatics resource for microbial metabolism. This will include a practical demonstration of how existing ELIXIR partner resources (HAMAP, Rhea, MicroScope and Ensembl) can be integrated with ELIXIR Core Data Resources (UniProt and ChEBI) using RDF and SPARQL to support typical requirements such as the construction of draft genome scale metabolic networks.\r
\r
The webinar will take place on Wendesday 13 June 2018 at 14.00 BST.\r
\r
ELIXIR Webinars usually take place every third Wednesday of the month 15.00 CET and are open for anyone to join. Upcoming webinars.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2018-06-13 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar on the Systems Biology Implementation Study" ;
    schema1:startDate "2018-06-13 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-systems-biology-implementation-study> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-overview-of-a-suite-of-tools-and-training-material-for-implementing-fair-data-principles> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description "There is global endorsement of principles to make data findable, accessible, interoperable and reusable (FAIR) by humans and computers.  Marco Roos (ELIXIR-NL), will present standards-based tools, architecture, and training material that help communities implement FAIR principles for their data sources.  FAIR can be applied in areas ranging from rare diseases to plant breeding." ;
    schema1:endDate "2017-10-18 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: Overview of a suite of tools and training material for implementing FAIR data principles" ;
    schema1:startDate "2017-10-18 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-overview-suite-tools-and-training-material-implementing-fair-data-principles> .

