<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-referencing-of-data-using-identifiers> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Identifiers.org enables the referencing of data for the life sciences community. It handles persistent identifiers in the form of Uniform Resource Identifier (URI), a string of characters used to identify a resource eg http://identifiers.org/pdb/2gc4 and Compact URIs (CURIEs) a generic, abbreviated syntax eg pdb:2gc4. This allows the referencing of data in both a location-independent and resource-dependent manner. Provision of resolvable identifiers fits well with the Semantic Web vision, and the Linked Data initiative.\r
\r
Sarala Wimalaratne (EMBL-EBI) will present the outcomes from the Identifiers Implementation Study, which aims to establish ldentifiers.org as a stable ELIXIR system for uniform identifier resolution of major bioinformatics resources (with a focus on ELIXIR reference resources).\r
\r
ELIXIR Webinars usually take place every third Wednesday of the month 15.00 CET and are open for anyone to join. Upcoming webinars.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2017-11-15 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar:  Referencing of Data Using Identifiers" ;
    schema1:startDate "2017-11-15 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-referencing-data-using-identifiers> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-reproducibility-in-systems-biology-modelling-sometimes> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """A webinar by Henning Hermjakob (Team Leader Molecular Networks, EMBL-EBI).\r
\r
\r
\r
In the context of BioModels, we have systematically attempted to reproduce 455 kinetic models of biological processes published in peer-reviewed research articles from 152 journals. About half (49%) of the models could not be reproduced using the information provided in the published manuscripts.\r
\r
With further effort, an additional 12% of the models could be reproduced either by empirical correction or support from authors. We will describe the study and discuss suggestions for improvement at individual and community level.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2020-09-11 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: Reproducibility in Systems Biology Modelling — Sometimes" ;
    schema1:startDate "2020-09-11 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/reproducibiity-systems-biology> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-requirements-in-data-protection-law-and-the-upcoming-general-data-protection-regulation-gdpr-implementation> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Regina Becker (ELIXIR Luxembourg) will give an introduction into the upcoming General Data Protection Legislation (GDPR) that will come into force on 25 May 2018. The new regulation has considerable consequences for managing and storing personal data, imposing more responsibility on the data controllers and data processors.\r
\r
During the webinar, relevant parts of the legislation for research and data sharing will be highlighted. Practical consequences for research institutions and in particular ELIXIR Nodes will be explained, and measures outlined that should be implemented for compliance. In addition, challenges and open questions will be addressed and suggestions made on how to jointly tackle these challenges in ELIXIR.\r
\r
This webinar is of interest for data stewards, Technical Coordinators, and everyone interested in the requirements for processing data for research under the GDPR.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2018-02-07 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: Requirements in data protection law and the upcoming General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) implementation" ;
    schema1:startDate "2018-02-07 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/webinar-gdpr> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-research-data-management-kit-rdmkit> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """This webinar will present the Research Data Management Kit (RDMKit) ahead of the public release at the end of March. \r
\r
This is a web-based resource for research data management, a flagship of ELIXIR-CONVERGE, built with contributions from every ELIXIR Node. It has been designed to guide life scientists in their efforts to better manage their research data following the FAIR Principles as well as help researchers be more productive for themselves and their collaborators. \r
\r
\r
\r
	Slide deck \r
\r
	\r
\r
""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2021-03-01 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: Research Data Management Kit (RDMKit)" ;
    schema1:startDate "2021-03-01 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-research-data-management-kit-rdmkit> .

