<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-the-transfer-of-large-volume-electronic-confidential-human-data> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """In the webinar, the ELIXIR Compute platform a showcase how ELIXIR supports transfer of large volumes of confidential, electronic, human data, while maintaining appropriate access rights. It will give an overview of an improved support to researchers in accessing and processing sensitive data from European Genome-Phenome Archive (EGA).\r
\r
The demonstration will present a scenario where a researcher first discovers data through the central EGA website. The resarchers is then directed to use ELIXIR Authentication and Authorisation Infrastructure (ELIXIR AAI) to apply for the data access. The application is communicated to the appropriate Data Access Committee (DAC), and access is granted.\r
\r
To store and analyse the data, the researcher can use local storage and computing resources made available  from a distributed ELIXIR cloud service: The researcher requests the ELIXIR Node offering the cloud service to transfer the dataset from the EGA data resource to the cloud service. Transferred data are then validated and moved to a secure location accessible to the cloud virtual machines. The ELIXIR cloud service notifies the researcher when the data are ready to be used. The researcher will then gain access to the data by authenticating with ELIXIR AAI, which links information that a valid DAC approval is associated with the researchers electronic identity.\r
\r
This is a demonstrator of the ELIXIR Compute Platform and a deliverable under ELIXIR EXCELERATE.\r
\r
ELIXIR Webinars are open for anyone to join. Upcoming webinars.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2017-11-13 14:30:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "ELIXIR Webinar: The transfer of large volume, electronic, confidential, human data" ;
    schema1:startDate "2017-11-13 14:30:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-transfer-large-volume-data> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/elixir-webinar-towards-professionalising-data-stewardship> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """As part of the National Programme Open Science (NPOS), the "Professionalising data stewardship in the Netherlands" report was recently published.\r
\r
This report provides arguments for urgent decisions and activities to ensure adequate data steward capacity in the Netherlands, in order to realise the ambitions for Open Science.\r
\r
In this webinar we will present the outcomes and recommendations of the project. Furthermore, we will indicate how this work, in particular the Data Stewardship Competency Framework, is contributing to activities in several Work Packages of ELIXIR-CONVERGE. \r
\r
Register\r
\r
\r
\r
Slides are available via Zenodo\r
\r
References\r
\r
\r
	Mijke Jetten, Marjan Grootveld, Annemie Mordant, Mascha Jansen, Margreet Bloemers, Margriet Miedema, &amp; Celia W.G. van Gelder. (2021). Professionalising data stewardship in the Netherlands. Competences, training and education. Dutch roadmap towards national implementation of FAIR data stewardship. Zenodo\r
	NPOS/ELIXIR Data Stewardship competency framework: https://competency.ebi.ac.uk\r
""" ;
