<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/eosc-life-de-nbi-cloud-workshop-how-to-deploy-your-webservice-in-the-cloud> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Jakob Mathis, Martin Braun (HD-HuB)\r
\r
Date: \r
27.07 9am-1pm\r
\r
Location:\r
Online\r
\r
Content:\r
In our EOSC Life / de.NBI workshop, we will focus on how to containerize an application and deploy the application as a web service in the de.NBI cloud infrastructure. We will cover basics in the usage of container technology, configure an reverse proxy together and use "Let's encrypt" to secure your website. We will show you key mechanisms and practices how you can deploy your own webservices in our cloud infrastructure.\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
Browser\r
\r
Keywords:\r
Cloud Computing, Linux, EOSC Life, Webservice\r
\r
Tools:\r
Bash, Docker, Docker Compose, Nginx""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2023-07-27 13:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:event_types "meetings_and_conferences" ;
    schema1:name "EOSC-Life & de.NBI Cloud workshop - How to deploy your webservice in the cloud?" ;
    schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "de.NBI / ELIXIR-DE" ] ;
    schema1:startDate "2023-07-27 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.denbi.de/training/1587-eosc-life-de-nbi-cloud-workshop-how-to-deploy-your-webservice-in-the-cloud> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/eosc-life-de-nbi-cloud-workshop-weskit-a-user-friendly-workflow-execution-service> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Valentin Schneier-Lunitz, Martin Braun (HD-HuB)\r
\r
Date: \r
21.07.2023 1pm-5pm\r
\r
Location:\r
Online\r
\r
Content:\r
In this EOSC Life workshop, we are going to use the open-source software WESkit that helps researchers to execute Nextflow and Snakemake workflows locally or remote in HPC or cloud environments. WESkit provides extensive logging capabilities, and a user management system, and supports high data throughput, stability, and security. Participants will be encouraged to set up their own WESkit instance and use it to submit both Nextflow and Snakemake workflows.\r
\r
Prerequisites\r
Browser\r
\r
Keywords:\r
Cloud Computing, Linux, EOSC Life\r
\r
Tools:\r
Bash, Conda /mamba, Docker\r
\r
Contact:\r
martin.braun@charite.de""" ;
