<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/eoscpilot-data-interoperability-technical-workshop> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """The European Open Science Cloud (EOSC) aims to provide by 2020 a virtual repository to access data from publicly funded research. The EOSCpilot is a two year project to support the first phase of development of EOSC. The EOSCpilot data interoperability task aims to establish principles, propose recommendations and demonstrate how FAIR data hosted by domain specific data repositories can be exposed to EOSC to be used and reused by EOSC services and users. This work relies on EOSCpilot use cases, data resources from domain specific research infrastructures and requirements from e-infrastructures services. In this workshop we will review data models used to describe datasets and data catalogues as well as requirements of infrastructure services dependent on datasets. The workshop will be focus on understanding, testing and evaluating existing technologies to expose and facilitate the integration of dataset metadata.\r
	\r
	Objectives\r
\r
Day 1\r
\r
\r
	Get an update of the EOSCpilot project and the work of the data interoperability task\r
	Review use cases and metadata models describing dataset catalogues and datasets\r
	Review e-infrastructure requirements for services working with datasets\r
	Propose key minimum properties to expose and find dataset metadata\r
\r
\r
Day 2\r
\r
\r
	Evaluate methods and technologies to expose data catalogues and datasets metadata\r
\r
\r
Meeting is limited to 35 attandees. Registration is on first come first serve basis.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2017-10-05 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "United Kingdom" ;
                            schema1:streetAddress "Wellcome Genome Campus" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "52.078533" ;
                    schema1:longitude "0.186135" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2017-10-04 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:name "EOSCpilot data interoperability technical workshop" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "ELIXIR" ;
            schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/eoscpilot-data-interoperability-technical-workshop> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/ep-permed-trainining-in-data-management-in-personalised-medicine> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3071> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Clinicians" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Lab managers" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Healthcare providers" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Researchers" ] ;
    schema1:description """EP PerMed is organising a two-day, hands-on training course on research data management (RDM) on 5 and 6 February 2026 in Paris, France. The application process will start at the beginning of September 2025.\r
\r
## General aim of the Training in Data Management\r
\r
The overall purpose of the Training in Data Management is to enable a responsible and effective use of data, by endowing researchers, clinicians, and data professionals with the knowledge, skills, and best practices necessary to manage, share, and interpret complex biomedical data in a way that supports personalised healthcare solutions. The training is made in collaboration with the Portuguese and Norwegian nodes of ELIXIR, the research infrastructure on life science data.\r
Specific aims of the Training\r
\r
Two-day hands-on Intensive Research Data Management (RDM) Course, guiding participants across the data lifecycle, highlighting the key challenges and questions to address at each stage, and showcasing tools and resources that researchers can use to aid them. The course will feature theoretical sessions that promote group discussions, intertwined with practical sessions consisting of exercises in small groups, that allow participants to both get acquainted with the tools and get involved in key RDM challenges. Key objectives:\r
\r
- Enhance Data Literacy and Competency;\r
- Promote FAIR Data Principles;\r
- Facilitate Regulatory and Ethical Compliance;\r
- Improve Research Efficiency and Reproducibility;\r
- Accelerate Translational Research and Innovation.\r
\r
## Target audience\r
\r
The training is specifically tailored to the personalised medicine scientific community (researchers, clinicians, healthcare providers, lab managers), applying to EP PerMed (and other) potential funding schemes.\r
\r
##  Logistics and Communication\r
\r
### Format\r
Two-half day physical event.\r
In person training, with theoretical sessions followed by practical exercises adapted to PM research community, with a focus on handling human genomic data.\r
\r
### Target groups\r
PM scientific community (researchers, clinicians, healthcare providers, lab managers)\r
\r
### Expected number of participants\r
30 physical trainees\r
\r
### Date\r
05-06 February 2026\r
\r
### Location\r
Paris (France), back-to-back with the ERA PerMed JTC 2022 Midterm Seminar (on invitation only)\r
\r
### Selection of participants\r
Candidates will apply on a platform (Microsoft Forms), providing curricular information, such as: Professional Experience and Achievements (PM related), publications and motivation to be selected for the Training.\r
\r
The application process will start at the beginning of September 2025.""" ;
