<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/european-conference-on-computational-biology-eccb-2018> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """On 8-12 September 2018 the Hellenic Society for Computational Biology and Bioinformatics is organising the 17th edition of the European Conference on Computational Biology in association with the ELIXIR.\r
\r
ECCB 2018 will take place in the historic city of Athens in Greece. It is the main computational biology event in Europe and will welcome scientists working in a variety of disciplines, including bioinformatics, computational biology, biology, medicine, and systems biology. Participating in ECCB 2018 will be the perfect opportunity to keep pace with cutting edge research, and to network with members of ECCB community.\r
\r
ELIXIR will be the main organising sponsor of the 17th ECCB. \r
\r
As part of the ELIXIR-ECCB 2018 partnership, the programme of the conference will feature a dedicated ELIXIR Application Track to showcase ELIXIR activities and services and ELIXIR Poster session.\r
	 \r
	The submission is now closed. \r
\r
ELIXIR track programme\r
\r
\r
	\r
		\r
			Sunday 9 September\r
		\r
	\r
	\r
		\r
			Morning session\r
		\r
		\r
			\r
				Application talks​\r
\r
				(No talks in this session.)\r
			\r
			\r
				Workshops \r
\r
				ELIXIR TeSS Usability Study\r
					(12:30-15:30)\r
					Niall Beard\r
					Agenda (Google Doc)\r
\r
				Beacons\r
					(15:30-17:00)\r
					Sabela de la Torre\r
					Agenda (Google Doc)\r
			\r
		\r
	\r
\r
\r
\r
	\r
		\r
			Monday 10 September\r
		\r
	\r
	\r
		\r
			Morning session\r
		\r
		\r
			\r
				Application talks​\r
\r
				ELIXIR Beacon - A Driver Project for the Global Alliance for Genomics and Health\r
\r
				EGA - new and future functionality\r
\r
				Secure e-infrastructure services supporting cross-border genomic and register studies\r
			\r
			\r
				Workshops\r
\r
				Bioschemas\r
					(12:30-14:00)\r
					Leyla Garcia, Alasdair Gray\r
					Agenda (on the Bioschemas website)\r
			\r
		\r
		\r
			Afternoon session\r
		\r
		\r
			\r
				Application talks​\r
\r
				Help yourself, and your community. Software reproducibility with BioContainers \r
\r
				Galaxy integration with DIANA-tools \r
\r
				Automated workflow composition in mass spectrometry based proteomics \r
			\r
			\r
				Workshops\r
\r
				Galaxy\r
					(17:30-19:00)\r
					Bjoern Gruening\r
					Agenda (Google Doc)\r
			\r
		\r
	\r
\r
\r
\r
	\r
		\r
			Tuesday 11 September\r
		\r
	\r
	\r
		\r
			Morning session\r
		\r
		\r
			\r
				Application talks​\r
\r
				cpPredictor: Webserver for template-based prediction of RNA secondary structure\r
\r
				neXtProt, a FAIR human protein resource working with the scientific community: Two use cases\r
\r
				3DBIONOTES crossing genomics, proteomics and interactomics\r
			\r
			\r
				Workshops\r
\r
				OpenEbench and Bio.tools \r
					(12:30-14:00)\r
					Salvador Capella Gutierrez\r
					Agenda (Google Doc)\r
\r
				Research under the GDPR \r
					(12:30-14:00)\r
					Regina Becker\r
					Agenda (Google Doc)\r
			\r
		\r
		\r
			Afternoon session\r
		\r
		\r
			\r
				Application talks​\r
\r
				GA4GH Compatible Analysis Platform &amp; Reference Dataset Distribution Services\r
\r
				Training as a service - empowering scientists to provide high quality training\r
\r
				The role of public bioinformatics infrastructures in supporting innovation in the life sciences\r
			\r
			\r
				Workshops\r
\r
				Implementation of DMPs and Data Stewardship in practice\r
					(17:30-19:00)\r
					Roland Krause, Brane Leskosek, Celia van Gelder\r
					Agenda (Google Doc)\r
\r
				Secure access to your services using ELIXIR AAI\r
					(17:30-19:00)\r
					Michal Procházka, František Dominik Bučík\r
					Agenda (Google Doc)\r
			\r
		\r
	\r
\r
\r
*Please note, the exact ECCB schedule with Application Track timings will be published 30 days in advance.\r
	\r
	For more details, please visit the ECCB main page""" ;
