    schema1:description """Do you want to understand more about genetic variation? Are you aware of the resources available for finding, viewing and exploring variant data? Are you trying to link variant data to phenotypes?

This three-day workshop will demonstrate resources and bioinformatics tools available at EMBL-EBI and the Wellcome Sanger Institute that will aid understanding of human genetic variation.

Participants will learn via a mix of lectures, trainer Q&amp;A sessions, and hands-on training. Practical experience will be developed through group activities and trainer-led exercises. Live sessions will be delivered using [Zoom](https://zoom.us/) with additional support and communication via [Slack](https://slack.com/intl/en-gb/). 

This course will take place over three non-consecutive days: 16, 18, and 20 May 2022.

Selected participants will be sent materials prior to the course. These might include pre-recorded talks and required reading or online training that will be essential to fully understand the course.

Participants will need to be available between the hours of 09:00 - 17:30 BST each day of the course. Trainers will be available to assist, answer questions, and further explain the analysis during these times.

 """ ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "online" ;
            schema1:endDate "2022-05-20 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:maximumAttendeeCapacity 30 ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "European Bioinformatics Institute (EBI)" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2022-05-16 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:keywords "Ensembl",
        "European Mouse Mutation Archive",
        "European Variation Archive",
        "NHGRI-EBI GWAS Catalog",
        "UniProt: The Universal Protein Resource" ;
    schema1:name "Exploring human genetic variation" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "European Bioinformatics Institute (EBI)" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.ebi.ac.uk> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/training/events/exploring-genetic-variation-2022> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/exploring-macromolecular-assemblies-in-complex-portal> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0602> ;
    schema1:description "This webinar will introduce the [Complex Portal](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/complexportal/home), which is a manually curated resource of molecular complexes. We will address how we define protein complexes, how they are different from molecular interactions, and what are their curation priorities and coverage. We will also explore how to search complexes using a variety of accession numbers, keywords and how to use the organism specific search. Further, we will also demonstrate examples of complex details pages that include visualisation tools and link-outs to related databases" ;
    schema1:endDate "2023-11-15 00:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:keywords "Complex Portal",
        "Molecular building blocks of life",
        "Proteins (proteins)",
        "macromolecular assembly" ;
    schema1:maximumAttendeeCapacity 1000 ;
    schema1:name "Exploring macromolecular assemblies in Complex Portal" ;
    schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "European Bioinformatics Institute (EBI)" ] ;
    schema1:startDate "2023-11-15 00:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/training/events/exploring-macromolecular-assemblies-complex-portal> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/exploring-macromolecular-protein-assemblies-and-their-visualisation-with-complex-portal> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/data_2877>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_0128> ;
    schema1:description """Protein complexes play a crucial role in driving biological functions and processes, making it important to gain insights into proteins and their higher-order assemblies.

[Complex Portal](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/complexportal/home) is a curated resource designed to offer insights into proteins and their higher-level complexes. In this webinar we will introduce the portal, address how we define protein complexes, demonstrate how to search complexes using accession numbers, or keywords specific search, perform organism-specific searches, explore examples of complex details pages including the Complex Viewer and link-outs to related databases. We will also look at the new ‘star-rating’ given to complexes, use the Complex Navigator to compare orthologous and paralogous complexes and introduce the predicted human complexes from huMAP3.0 and MuSIC maps.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "online" ;
            schema1:endDate "2025-07-09 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:streetAddress ", " ] ] ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "European Bioinformatics Institute (EBI)" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2025-07-09 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:keywords "Complex Portal",
        "protein" ;
    schema1:name "Exploring macromolecular protein assemblies and their visualisation with Complex Portal" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "European Bioinformatics Institute (EBI)" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.ebi.ac.uk> ],
        [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "EMBL-EBI" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/training> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/training/events/exploring-macromolecular-protein-assemblies-and-their-visualisation-complex-portal> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/exploring-metabolite-metabolism-using-the-enzyme-portal> a schema1:Event ;
