<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/fair-data-management-in-life-sciences-2022-course-1st-edition-by-elixir-norway> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3071> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "All postgraduates" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Life sciences" ] ;
    schema1:description """# FAIR Data Management in Life Sciences - 2022 Course, 1st Edition by ELIXIR Norway\r
\r
## 14.-16. June, Virtual \r
\r
### About\r
\r
The course aims to cover topics covering the whole data life cycle (as shown in the [Research Data Management kit by ELIXIR Europe](https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/)) with a specific focus on the implementation of [the FAIR data principles](https://www.go-fair.org/fair-principles/). The goal is to teach the key concepts on how to make life sciences data Findable, Accessible, Interoperable, and Reusable for your research management. For queries, check out [Frequently Asked Questions](https://github.com/elixir-oslo/fair-dm-2022-course/blob/main/faqs.md) and/or you can send mail to contact@bioinfo.no.\r
\r
### Learning Objectives\r
\r
- To walk through data life cycle steps with an introduction to tools relevant to life sciences research, including in a context of computational analysis for life sciences.\r
- To understand FAIR principles in the context of each data cycle step\r
- To understand the data curation processes that enable data reuse and repurposing\r
- To know the different RDM guidelines and practices used by the various RIs and institutions in Norway. \r
\r
### Learning Outcomes:\r
\r
- To be able to define and connect RDM tasks within a domain of interest.\r
- To be able to determine different tools that are available, globally and in Norway, to carry out RDM tasks.  \r
- To be able to identify metadata standards and to associate relevant deposition repositories\r
- To be able to analyse and evaluate FAIRness of Data (and Management Plan)\r
\r
### Learning Activities:\r
\r
Each session will include time for a short discussion including questions and answers. We plan to have a group activity on last day of the course that will involve reviewing and discussing how to create a FAIR DMP. In addition, we plan to include a short quiz relevant to each session; learners are recommended to take a quiz during or after the course to help revise and understand the content learned throughout the course.\r
\r
### 👥 Target Audience\r
\r
The course is aimed at current and future life scientists in Norway. The target audience includes master’s students, PhD candidates, postdoctoral fellows, early-career researchers, and technical staff involved in scientific research in the life sciences in Norway. The course is particularly relevant for users and/or collaborators of the research infrastructures listed below:\r
\r
- [NorSeq: National consortium for sequencing and personalised medicine](https://www.norseq.org/)\r
- [NOR-Openscreen: Consortium for chemical biology and early drug discovery](http://www.openscreen.no/)\r
- [NORMOLIM: Norwegian Molecular Imaging Infrastructure](https://normolim.w.uib.no/)\r
- [NALMIN: Norwegian Advanced Light Microscopy Imaging Network](https://nalmin.no/) \r
- [NORCRYST: Norwegian Macromolecular Crystallography Consortium]( https://site.uit.no/norcryst/) \r
- [BBMRI-NO: National research infrastructure for clinical and population-based biobanks](https://bbmri.no/)\r
- [MoBa Genetics: Norwegian Mother, Father and Child Cohort Study](https://www.fhi.no/en/studies/moba/)\r
- [GBIF Norway: The Norwegian node of the Global Biodiversity Information Facility](https://www.gbif.org/country/NO/summary)\r
\r
### Course Schedule and Registration\r
🗓 [Click here to read the course schedule](https://github.com/elixir-oslo/fair-dm-2022-course/blob/main/schedule.md) \r
➡️ [Click here to register](https://nettskjema.no/a/fair-dm-2022)\r
\r
### Organisers\r
- Nazeefa Fatima, Centre for Bioinformatics, University of Oslo\r
- Korbinian Bösl, University of Bergen\r
- Federico Bianchini, Centre for Bioinformatics, University of Oslo\r
\r
### Important Links\r
- [ELIXIR-Norway website](https://elixir.no/)\r
- [Read more about BioMedData](https://elixir.no/organization/biomeddata)\r
- [ELIXIR-Norway Data Stewardship Wizard](https://elixir-no.ds-wizard.org/)\r
- [End-User Course on FAIR Data Management for Life Sciences Research in Norway](https://zenodo.org/record/6104400#.YmFyjZNBxqs) - Deliverable report, available on Zenodo\r
\r
## For queries, check out [Frequently Asked Questions](https://github.com/elixir-oslo/fair-dm-2022-course/blob/main/faqs.md) and/or you can send mail to the organisers at contact@bioinfo.no (use the course title as e-mail subject).""" ;
