<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/fairplus-webinar-discovering-the-fair-cookbook> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """\r
\r
What to expect\r
\r
You will discover the FAIRplus flagship product developed by and for life science researchers and data stewards — the FAIR Cookbook.\r
\r
Combining the expertise of industry experts and academia, this web resource includes a framework and real-life examples of datasets to make your data Findable, Accessible, Interoperable and Reusable (FAIR).\r
\r
Delivered by the resource’s developers and project coordinator, you will hear about the FAIR Cookbook recipes, the challenges and the key required capabilities and skills required.\r
\r
Who should attend\r
\r
\r
	Data scientists\r
	Data stewards\r
	Curators\r
	Staff supporting and training researchers to make data FAIR\r
	Policymakers recommending useful FAIR-enabling resources and training materials to their community.\r
	FAIR experts interested in contributing\r
\r
\r
Whether you are looking for a resource to start your FAIRification journey or want to contribute to this community-driven effort, we invite you to join this short webinar to discover the potential of the Cookbook.\r
\r
Speakers\r
\r
\r
	Serena Scollen (ELIXIR-Hub)\r
	Herman Van Vlijmen (Janssen)\r
	Philippe Rocca-Serra (University of Oxford)\r
	Wei Gu (University of Luxembourg)\r
	Tony Burdett (EMBL-EBI)\r
	Andrea Splendiani (Novartis AG)\r
	Susanna-Assunta Sansone (University of Oxford)\r
	Robert Giessmann (Bayer AG)\r
\r
\r
\r
The FAIRplus project has received funding from the Innovative Medicines Initiative Joint Undertaking under grant agreement No 802750. This Joint Undertaking receives support from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme and EFPIA Companies. This communication reflects the views of the authors and neither IMI nor the European Union, EFPIA or any Associated Partners are liable for any use that may be made of the information contained herein.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2021-05-26 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "FAIRplus Webinar. Discovering the FAIR Cookbook" ;
    schema1:startDate "2021-05-26 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/fairplus-webinar-discovering-fair-cookbook> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/fairplus-webinar-what-is-the-value-of-fair-data> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Using real life examples and use cases, this online event will showcase the value of FAIR data in pharmaceutical research and make case for policy changes in relation to research data management and research funding.\r
\r
The webinar is organised by the FAIRplus project, which develops guidelines and tools to facilitate the application of FAIR principles to data selected from participating Innovative Medicines Initiative (IMI) projects and pharmaceutical companies. It is supported by by IMI and coordinated jointly by ELIXIR and Janssen.\r
\r
More information is available on the FAIRplus website.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2020-12-09 10:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "FAIRplus webinar: What is the value of FAIR data?" ;
    schema1:startDate "2020-12-09 10:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/fairplus-webinar-what-value-fair-data> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/fairymags-hybrid-hackathon-2025-optimising-metagenomics-assembled-genomes-building> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Paul Zierep (RBC), Bérénice Batut (ELIXIR-FR)\r
\r
Date:\r
October 6-9th, 2025\r
\r
Location:\r
Georges-Koehler-Allee 079, D-79110 Freiburg, Germany &amp; Online\r
\r
Contents:\r
Metagenomics Assembled Genomes building workflows are both technically and scientifically challenging, yet they are essential tools for reducing microbial dark matter, as most microbes cannot be cultivated.\r
\r
As part of the FAIRyMAGs project within the ELIXIR BFSP Programme, we are organizing a 4-day hackathon (October 6-9th)and 1-day for an optional social event (October 10th). We warmly invite the community to join us either in person in Freiburg or online. This event is an opportunity to collaborate, discuss, and improve MAGs workflows together!\r
\r
FAIRyMAGs is led by Paul Zierep (ELIXIR-DE) and Bérénice Batut (ELIXIR-FR) in collaboration with Giuseppe Defazio (ELIXIR-IT), Bruno Fosso (ELIXIR-IT), Martin Beracochea (EMBL-EBI), Santiago Sanchez (EMBL-EBI), that will be participating the hackathon.\r
\r
Learning goals:\r
The learning goals of this 4-day scientific and technical hackathon are to optimize Metagenomics Assembled Genomes building by:\r
\r
🚀 Enhancing FAIR MAGs building Workflows\r
Optimizing assembly strategies: Individual assembly vs. co-assembly vs. grouped-assembly, Automating decision-making for assembly selection\r
Bin refinement improvements: Where do we go beyond MetaWrap? Should we integrate more binning tools for better results?\r
📚Developing user-friendly training materials\r
\r
Advancing workflow evaluation methods (using CAMI infrastructure &amp; real data)\r
Have metagenomic WGS samples? Want to create MAGs? This is your chance!\r
⚙️ Building intelligent computational resource estimation tools\r
Whether you're using Nextflow, Snakemake, or Galaxy, resource allocation is key. Over-provisioning wastes resources; under-provisioning leads to failed jobs. Let’s design workflow-agnostic tools that optimize resource usage, reducing computational waste and environmental impact!\r
Prerequisites:\r
Only for experts in Metagenomics and Bioinformatics! Basic knowledge of Galaxy is also helpful. \r
\r
Keywords: \r
Galaxy, Metagenomics\r
\r
Tools:\r
Galaxy""" ;
