        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3489> ;
    schema1:description """This Q&amp;A (question and answer) webinar will provide an opportunity for anyone who has completed ‘[Finding and using publicly available data: A curated set of online courses](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/training/online/courses/finding-using-public-data/)’ to join some of EMBL-EBI's experts and ask their own questions. This session will focus on biocuration, open data, and accessing publicly available data.

The questions covered during the Q&amp;A webinar will depend on those asked by attendees, however we will likely cover topics such as:

- Data sharing and submission
- Restricted access to genetic, phenotypic, and clinical data
- Data management of biological data and open data
- Finding the right EMBL-EBI resource for accessing data""" ;
