<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/gentle-hands-on-introduction-to-python-programming-in-person-482d69f5-b65b-447c-9f9b-5da38d2fe1c2> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description "This is a course that gently introduces programming to new programmers over a 4 meetings with the trainers in class, and the afternoon for self-paced extra activities and doubts , afternoons interactions are optional but encouraged. There are plenty of opportunities to practice what you learn and ask questions in a safe place. Furthermore, surprise yourself by building a substantial project.Each week there are some OPTIONAL interactive afternoons \"lab\" sessions for you to do exercises and ask questions . The lab sessions will be after the morning course, but more may be scheduled with our trainers at different times or in-person depending on your needs.Contact Bruna Piereck or James Collier if you have any questions regarding the course, see e-mails below. This is a online course that gently introduces programming to new programmers over a self-paced 2-month period combined with Q&amp;A (\"lab\" sessions).You will receive an email before the course starts, this email will contain all the information you need to begin the course.Important: You are required to follow at least 75% of this course in order to receive your certificate of successful completion." ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
