<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/gentle-hands-on-introduction-to-python-programming-online> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description "This is an online self-paced course that gently introduces programming to new programmers over a  2 months course combined with Q&amp;A \"LAB\" sessions.During the 2-month course, there are scheduled optional afternoon “lab” sessions for Q&amp;A and problem solving. The lab sessions will be in Ghent and online, but more/other may be scheduled with our trainers at different times (online or in-person) based on your personal needs and availability. There are plenty of opportunities to practice what you learn and ask questions in a safe place. Furthermore, surprise yourself by building a substantial project.Contact Bruna Piereck or James Collier if you have any questions regarding the course, see e-mails below.   You will receive an email before the course opens, this email will contain all the information you need to begin the course.Important: You are required to follow at least 75% of this self-paced course in order to receive your certificate of successful completion.  02/Sep we have kickoff and release, and to 03/Sep \"Lab\" sessions (Q&amp;A) starts  " ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
