<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/gentle-hands-on-introduction-to-python-programming-online-94c2ba79-3507-4cc9-8d98-f604921526db> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description "This is an online course that gently introduces programming to new programmers over a  2 months course combined with afternoon practical sessions combined with self-paced exercises.During the 2-month course, there are scheduled afternoons to with trainers for problem solving practice moment. The online session will complemente the self-paced activities increasing the depth of learning and understand of application of Python programming language basics. If during the self-pace exercises you encounter challenges you can scheduled dedicated call with our trainers at different times based on your personal needs. There are plenty of opportunities to practice what you learn and ask questions in a safe place. Furthermore, surprise yourself by building a substantial project during the guided sessions.Contact Bruna Piereck or James Collier if you have any questions regarding the course, see e-mails below.  You will receive an email before the course opens, this email will contain all the information you need to begin the course.Important: You are required to follow at least 75% of this self-paced course in order to receive your certificate of successful completion. On 29 Apr, we have kickoff and release, and to 13th of May the content classes start." ;
