<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/ghga-summer-school-on-gene-set-enrichment-analysis-with-r> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:coursePrerequisites "some previous knowledge on R" ;
    schema1:description """GHGA is organising a summer school on Gene Set Enrichment Analysis with R\r
\r
Instructors: Zuguang Gu (DKFZ) and Kübra Narci (GHGA)\r
\r
Content:\r
\r
Gene Set Enrichment Analysis (GSEA) is a fundamental technique in biological data analysis. It is commonly used to associate biological functions with a list of genes, offering valuable insights into the biological context of experimental results. This workshop will provide a comprehensive introduction to GSEA methods with hands-on practice using R and Bioconductor packages. The following topics will be covered: \r
\r
1) accessing and utilizing gene set resources with Bioconductor packages;\r
\r
2) ORA and GSEA, \r
\r
3) applications of GSEA in genomics; \r
\r
4) pathway-based GSEA approaches;\r
\r
5) single-sample GSEA approaches, and \r
\r
6) visualization of GSEA results.\r
\r
Recommended audience: master students, PhD and postdoc with R skills""" ;
