<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/how-to-recognize-stress-and-prevent-burnout-in-depth-sessions> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """These sessions are part of a learning path. You first need to participate in the introductory session before you can attend these in-depth sessions. More information on the introductory session can be found here.

Session 1: Training your brain to get into relaxation status and tackle stress in daily life

You can automate the methods of getting into deep relaxation so that you can drop in your brain frequency in shorter and shorter periods of time. By doing these exercises, you learn to drop to low alpha and thêta, the levels of relaxation where you have much more self-control and you can recondition your brain itself in about 2 minutes. 

In this session we will also learn several short methods that can be used at any time of the day. These methods help to drop slightly in brain frequency. So if you use them quickly enough (before you are completely stressed), they will help you calm down quickly in acute moments and keep your self-control. By using these methods you also prevent the stress from building up and leaving you exhausted and tired in the evening. Thanks to the application of these methods you can prevent accumulation of stress.

Session 2: The power of beliefs, the missing link to achieve lasting change

Our beliefs are the way we look at the world. We think it is the only truth and, as a result, we come into conflict with ourselves and those around us. After all, a belief is only a partial truth. Working first and then playing (= relaxing) is a good thought in itself, but limiting if you have been raised with it. If I relax first then I will work more efficiently afterwards is equally correct and thus complementary. It is AND - AND. When both beliefs are imprinted 100% in your brain, then you have choice and can adapt according to the situation and need. We are not aware of which beliefs we have and which ones we lack. This is 80-90% the cause of our stress in all areas of life. In this module you will reflect on your own thoughts, why you think this way and what complementary thoughts you need to reduce your stress.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2024-03-29 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Belgium" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Leuven" ;
                            schema1:postalCode "3000" ;
                            schema1:streetAddress "Leuven - Campus Gasthuisberg, Herestraat 49" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "50.879202" ;
                    schema1:longitude "4.701168" ] ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "VIB" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2024-03-13 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:inLanguage "en" ;
    schema1:keywords "wellbeing" ;
    schema1:name "How to Recognize Stress and Prevent Burnout: In-depth Sessions" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "VIB Training" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/all-trainings/how-recognize-stress-and-prevent-burnout-depth-sessions> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/how-to-recognize-stress-and-prevent-burnout-in-depth-sessions-26a88b78-a7be-4e4a-ae2d-a74b3ef79350> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description "These sessions are part of a learning path. You first need to participate in the introductory session before you can attend these in-depth sessions. More information on the introductory session can be found here.Session 1: Training your brain to get into relaxation status and tackle stress in daily lifeYou can automate the methods of getting into deep relaxation so that you can drop in your brain frequency in shorter and shorter periods of time. By doing these exercises, you learn to drop to low alpha and thêta, the levels of relaxation where you have much more self-control and you can recondition your brain itself in about 2 minutes. In this session, we will also learn several short methods that can be used at any time of the day. These methods help to drop slightly in brain frequency. So if you use them quickly enough (before you are completely stressed), they will help you calm down quickly in acute moments and keep your self-control. By using these methods you also prevent the stress from building up and leaving you exhausted and tired in the evening. Thanks to the application of these methods you can prevent accumulation of stress.Session 2: The power of beliefs, the missing link to achieve lasting changeOur beliefs are the way we look at the world. We think it is the only truth, and as a result, we come into conflict with ourselves and those around us. After all, a belief is only a partial truth. Working first and then playing (= relaxing) is a good thought in itself, but limiting if you have been raised with it. If I relax first then I will work more efficiently afterwards is equally correct and thus complementary. It is AND - AND. When both beliefs are imprinted 100% in your brain, then you have a choice and can adapt according to the situation and need. We are not aware of which beliefs we have and which ones we lack. This is 80-90% of the cause of our stress in all areas of life. In this module you will reflect on your own thoughts, why you think this way and what complementary thoughts you need to reduce your stress." ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
