<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/illumina-rna-library-preparation-lab-course> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Note, to ensure a high quality of training for everyone, we will be limiting places for those with no/limited lab experience to 2 for this course." ] ;
    schema1:description "In this course you will learn how to produce sequencing libraries using the new RNA ligation library preparation kits from Illumina, which provide a quick and simple work-flow for library production. You will get to work on both a high-quality training sample and have the opportunity to bring your own RNA sample for library preparation and sequencing. This course assumes you have a basic level of laboratory experience in a molecular biology lab, although experienced demonstrators will always be on hand to guide you. If you have limited lab experience, please indicate this on the registration form and we will try to accommodate you." ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2024-10-24 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "Edinburgh Genomics" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2024-10-23 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:keywords "Illumina",
        "Library",
        "Molecular biology",
        "RNA",
        "Sequencing" ;
    schema1:name "Illumina RNA Library Preparation Lab Course" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "Edinburgh Genomics" ;
            schema1:url <https://genomics.ed.ac.uk> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://genomics.ed.ac.uk/event/illumina-rna-library-preparation-lab-course/> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/image-ethics-poster-design> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """In this training course, we want to teach the basic ethic aspects of image editing and design appealing and modern scientific posters.

The image ethics part handles on the theoretical aspects of image manipulation, the mistakes people make and how to avoid image fraud. VIB has guidelines for acceptable scientific image manipulations. Not all manipulations are scientifically correct. There are manipulations that fall within the scope of scientific misconduct, because they result in misrepresentation of the data. Such misrepresentation makes it impossible for others to interpret the data correctly, or worse, leads to conclusions that are not correct.

The second part of this course deals with poster design. Scientific posters are a resume of a piece or timespan of research on one square meter of paper. They are best compared to slides for oral presentations, not a written document. Posters can’t convey detailed evidence like scientific articles, it must visualize a message on its own. When standing a meter away from a poster you hardly feel like reading much text, especially when the author/designer stands next to it. A poster must bring that message without requiring oral explanation, but with as little text as possible.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2019-06-27 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Belgium" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Leuven" ;
                            schema1:postalCode "3010" ;
                            schema1:streetAddress "Leuven - Park Inn by Radisson, Martelarenlaan 36" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "50.881367" ;
                    schema1:longitude "4.717319" ] ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "VIB" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2019-06-27 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:inLanguage "en" ;
    schema1:name "Image Ethics & Poster Design" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "VIB Training" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/all-trainings/image-ethics-poster-design> .

