<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/innate-immunity-in-host-pathogen-interactions-871c32b2-052f-4d9c-bd6c-699708a07a20> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3301> ;
    schema1:description """This symposium focuses on bringing together innate immunity and microbiology to obtain a global view of host-pathogen interactions. A better understanding of infectious disease will come through the simultaneous analysis of microbial and host variables, and open new avenues for treatment and prevention strategies. 
The talks will center around common processes, rather than a particular infectious agent or host cell, and the strategies of all types of pathogens, commensals and different host cells will be analysed.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2016-06-29 00:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Germany" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Heidelberg" ;
                            schema1:streetAddress "EMBL" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "49.398752" ;
                    schema1:longitude "8.672434" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2016-06-26 00:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:name "Innate Immunity in Host-Pathogen Interactions" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "iAnn" ;
            schema1:url <http://iann.pro> ] ;
    schema1:url <http://www.embl.de/training/events/stay-informed/newsletter/2016/march/immunity/?utm_source=eventmailing&utm_medium=E-Mail&utm_content=EES16-05_01_survey&utm_campaign=EES16-05> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/innovation-and-sme-forum-building-the-learning-ecosystem-of-health-from-data-tracking-to-preventive-medicine> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """\r
\r
What to expect\r
\r
You will dive deep into the world of data-driven innovation with a mix of high-level keynote presentations and hands-on sessions to discuss and interact with other companies, academics and ELIXIR partners. All this with an interactive virtual platform to offer you an immersive online experience\r
\r
Who should attend\r
\r
\r
	Researchers in academia and industry\r
	Large and small companies that develop services for data management and analysis\r
	Policymakers and funders\r
	Anyone interested in the data-driven life sciences sector\r
""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2021-09-13 00:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Switzerland" ] ;
            schema1:latitude "46.798562" ;
            schema1:longitude "8.231974" ] ;
    schema1:name "Innovation and SME Forum: Building the learning ecosystem of health: from data tracking to preventive medicine" ;
    schema1:startDate "2021-09-13 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/innovation-and-sme-forum-building-learning-ecosystem-health-data-tracking-preventive-medicine> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/innovation-and-sme-forum-building-the-learning-ecosystem-of-health-from-data-tracking-to-preventive-medicine-53eb72ef-a93d-489f-9b79-9f0b78721733> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Take part in the ELIXIR Innovation and SME Forum at [BC]2, to share solutions for preventive medicine and the whole learning ecosystem of health\r
\r
The [BC]2 Basel Computational Biology Conference, organised by the SIB - Swiss Institute of Bioinformatics, will host a one-day ELIXIR Innovation and SME Forum entitled “Building the learning ecosystem of health: from data tracking to preventive medicine” on 13 September. The day aims to foster knowledge sharing and collaborations between academia and industry around the technologies, data science and learning implementation related to preventive medicine and follow-up treatment. The forum will include talks from high-profile speakers, interactive panel discussions, and selected talks from across the biomedical research and healthcare ecosystem.\r
\r
\r
\r
What to expect\r
\r
The ELIXIR Innovation and SME Forum day will explore solutions to understand better the different components of the learning ecosystem of health and preventive medicine. From technologies (hardware, software) to data management, data integration or analysis.\r
\r
What are the missing pieces of the puzzle to develop knowledge and preventive medicine? Which are the technologies, methods, processes, standards needed to advance learnings about health and increase benefits for citizens? What is promising? Which contributions are necessary?\r
	These are some of the questions which will be addressed during the day, through invited talks, selected presentations as well as panel discussions.\r
\r
The programme includes a discussion on solutions connecting the different components of the learning ecosystem of health, from industry (start-ups and SMEs, and large companies) and academia in areas related to:\r
\r
\r
	Health data collection technologies (hardware and software) focusing on healthy citizens and/or patients in the post-treatment phase\r
	Data management\r
	Research or data integration and analysis\r
	Converting learnings into healthcare guidelines/policies.\r
\r
\r
Who should attend\r
\r
\r
	Researchers in academia and industry\r
	Large and small companies that develop services for data management and analysis\r
	Policymakers and funders\r
	Anyone interested in the data-driven life sciences sector or preventive medicine\r
""" ;
