<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/inspirational-leadership-getting-things-done-with-a-team> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """People quit their bosses, not their jobs. The main driver of people quitting their job, having a low job satisfaction or low performance is because of their manager. A large study at Google has shown that the most effective teams, that outperform all other teams have only one thing in common: trust. Trust in each‐other and trust in their team‐leader.

 
How can you build a team from loose individuals? How do you grow trust? How can you inspire the people around you to performing at their best?


In this training we will cover how you can motivate and inspire people, how you build effective teams. You  will  learn  how  our  minds  work  and  how  you  need  to  adapt  as  a  leader.  We  will  put  these theoretical insights into action by leveraging several tools into a plan for you and your team. At the end you will learn how to follow‐up, provide feedback and evaluate performance. Finally we will cover a number of easy wins on how to build your relationships while still having enough spare time for your own work. 

Content

How to go from group to team  


	What motivates others? 
	Define the team purpose. 
	Define the team values. 
	Define the objectives. 
	Building trust with transparency and clarity. 


How the human brain works  


	You go towards your focus. 
	Questions trigger the mind. 
	The mind cannot avoid a don’t. 
	The mind can only focus on one thought at a time. 
	The power of beliefs. 


Providing direction 


	Getting to know your direct reports. 
	Comfort, Stretch, Stress zones for development. 
	Manager’s role in setting priorities. 
	Strengths based leadership. 
	Annual action plan. 
	Setting individual objectives and success measures. 
	Communicating expectations 
	1on1 leadership 


Providing feedback 


	Regular Employee‐Manager Touch Points 
	Effective listening 
	Giving and Receiving Feedback 
	Feedback Delivery Techniques 
	Planning a feedback meeting 
	Rose of Leary 
	Handling Resistance to Feedback 
	Evaluating Contributions 
	The Action Plan – Performance Evaluation 


Reward and recognition 


	How to stimulate wanted behaviours 
	Individual versus group rewards 
	The power of Moments 
	
		Achievement 
		Transition 
		Relationships """ ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2022-09-14 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Belgium" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Leuven" ;
                            schema1:postalCode "3010" ;
                            schema1:streetAddress "Leuven - Park Inn by Radisson, Martelarenlaan 36" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "50.879202" ;
                    schema1:longitude "4.701168" ] ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "VIB" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2022-09-12 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:inLanguage "en" ;
    schema1:keywords "leadership & management" ;
    schema1:name "Inspirational Leadership – Getting things done with a team" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "VIB Training" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/all-trainings/inspirational-leadership-getting-things-done-team> .

