<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/integrative-structural-biology-course> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_1317> ;
    schema1:alternateName "The course will be held in Sweden, on site (Lund, Gothenburg, Stockholm), on 3 different occassions between Aug 22 and Sept 2nd" ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "The course is open to scientists of all age from academia, health care and industry. Level approximately corresponding to PhD student or postdoc depending on experience. Applicants welcome from Sweden, the Nordics, and other countries." ] ;
    schema1:description """Deadline for application: 23rd of May: https://www.lyyti.fi/reg/Integrative_Structural_Biology_Course_3770 \r
\r
\r
The two week course is a joint effort between the three large-scale research infrastructures SciLifeLab, MAX IV and ESS and additional related platforms. The aim is to give an overview of the structural biology available at the research infrastructures in Sweden. The course will focus on understanding the sample requirements, the nature of structural information that can be obtained and how data from multiple structural biology methods can be combined using e.g. computational chemistry techniques. The course consists of lectures, key note speakers, modelling practicals and facility visits. In addition events allowing time for networking within the group of students, the teachers and other infrastructure personnel, contributing to an expanded professional network.\r
\r
Technologies/methods:\r
\r
    * Macromolecular X-ray and neutron crystallography\r
    * Small angle X-ray and neutron scattering \r
    * Cryo-electron microscopy\r
    * Macromolecular nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy\r
    * Structural mass spectrometry\r
    * Modelling and Computational methods \r
    * Biophysical characterization\r
\r
Keynote speakers:\r
\r
We proudly present a number of exciting keynote speakers that will present scientific examples of how integrative structural biology techniques can be used to solve intriguing questions.\r
\r
    Professor Poul Nissen, Aarhus University\r
    Professor Carmen Domene, University of Bath\r
    Postdoctoral researcher Hanna Barriga, Karolinska university\r
\r
Also we will be able to join in on the SciLifeLab “Annual lecture on Structural Biology” where Demis Hassabis will talk on using AI to accelerate scientific discovery.\r
\r
Lessons on modelling/computational methods:\r
\r
We will have several lectures on modelling and computational techniques for structural biology.\r
\r
Associate professor Lucie Delemotte, Integrating physics-based and evolutionary modelling to investigate the conformational dynamics of membrane proteins\r
\r
Professor Gunnar von Heijne, Different approaches to the study of cotranslational protein folding\r
\r
Professor Erik Lindahl, titel tbd\r
\r
Principal Research Engineer Claudio Mirabello, The protein structure prediction problem: from Anfinsen to AlphaFold.\r
\r
""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2022-10-02 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:funder [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "This InfraLife integrative structural biology course is organized with funding support from the Swedish research council, Lif, Excillum, NBIS, Xenocs, SwedNMR, Bruker and CryoNET." ] ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Sweden" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Lund, Gothenburg, Stockholm" ;
                            schema1:addressRegion "Sweden" ;
                            schema1:postalCode "Sweden" ;
                            schema1:streetAddress """Onsite on three different locations across Sweden where the Swedish national Research Infrastructures, MaxIV, SciLifeLab and ESS are coming together to deliver a course on structural biology. \r
The course will be held in Sweden, on site, between Aug 22 and Sept 2nd 2022.\r
\r
    *Lund, 22 to 25 Aug\r
    *Gothenburg, 26 Aug\r
    *Stockholm, 29 Aug to 2 Sep""" ] ] ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "Infralife" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2022-08-22 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:keywords "Structural biology",
        "Technology",
        "bioinformatics",
        "computational methods" ;
    schema1:name "Integrative structural biology course" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "ELIXIR Sweden" ;
            schema1:url <file:///home/runner/work/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/> ],
        [ a schema1:Organization ;
