<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/introduction-to-ega-and-its-ecosystem-of-tools> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0091>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_0622> ;
    schema1:description """**About the workshop**\r
\r
The [European Genome-phenome Archive (EGA)](https://ega-archive.org/) is a resource for archiving of all types of potentially identifiable genetic, phenotypic, and clinical data resulting from biomedical research projects. Its mission is to foster hosted data reuse, enable reproducibility, and accelerate biomedical and translational research.\r
\r
To promote the use and interaction with professionals in research and education, we invite you to attend our first online workshop on the EGA and its ecosystem of tools. The goal of this training would be to present EGA repositories and tools so that they can be incorporated into your research or teaching. This online course is aimed at teachers, professors and trainers interested in incorporating these concepts and tools in their curriculums.\r
\r
Register in this [online form](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfnyIscGgN961IvO6AcbL-cHk-A9zRezzLbGUHTf8ZJKI0YGQ/viewform) (open until Wednesday, September 14).\r
\r
**Content**\r
\r
- Part 1: The EGA and introduction to human data and sharing sensitive data.\r
- Part 2: Tools for exploring data: EGA has a number of tools in relation to GA4GH, such as Beacon or protocol htsget, which will be presented. There will also be introduction to other repositories for exploring sensitive human data, including [GPAP: the RD-Connect Genome-Phenome Analysis Platform](https://rd-connect.eu/what-we-do/omics/gpap/) for diagnosis and gene discovery in rare disease research and [DisGeNET](https://www.disgenet.org/): a discovery platform designed to address a variety of questions concerning the genetic underpinning of human diseases.\r
\r
During the workshop, live demonstrations of the tools will be performed. The organisers will also provide direct access to materials for learning and training. The agenda is available on the [VEIS website](https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/workshop-tools-and-techniques-to-make-sensitive-data-discoverable).\r
\r
This course is supported by the [VEIS](https://veis.bsc.es/en/) project: Value of the EGA for Industry and Society.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2022-09-19 13:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:funder [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "VEIS" ] ;
    schema1:keywords "Genomics",
        "bioinformatics",
        "e-learning" ;
    schema1:name "Introduction to EGA and its Ecosystem of Tools" ;
    schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "European Genome-Phenome Archive (EGA)" ] ;
    schema1:startDate "2022-09-19 10:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://veis.bsc.es/en/events/ega-crg-introduction-to-ega-and-its-ecosystem-of-tools/> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/introduction-to-elabjournal-getting-started-with-the-electronic-lab-notebook-eln> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description "Efficient documentation and collaboration are essential in any research environment. The eLabJournal serves as the central platform for managing experimental workflows, samples, and team communication. This introductory training offers a practical overview of how to use the Electronic Lab Notebook (ELN) to streamline daily lab operations.Participants will explore the platform’s core features — from documenting experiments and organizing samples to facilitating collaboration across research teams. The training is hands-on and designed to help users quickly become confident in navigating the system, improving productivity while ensuring compliance with research standards (e.g. FAIR principles)." ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2025-10-07 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Belgium" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Antwerpen" ;
                            schema1:postalCode "2610" ;
                            schema1:streetAddress "Antwerp - Campus Drie Eiken UAntwerpen, Universiteitsplein 1" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "51.22111" ;
                    schema1:longitude "4.399708" ] ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "VIB" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2025-10-07 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:inLanguage "en" ;
    schema1:keywords "ELN",
        "hands-on",
        "personal effectiveness" ;
    schema1:name "Introduction to eLabJournal: getting started with the Electronic Lab Notebook (ELN)" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "VIB Training" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches "“Configure inventory settings including sample types and storage units”",
        "“Create and edit protocols within the platform”",
        "“Create and organize experiments and experiment templates”",
        "“Develop a unified naming structure for samples projects studies and experiments”",
        "“Differentiate the three core components of eLabJournal: inventory protocols and journal”",
        "“Explain the importance of the ELNs in research projects”",
        "“List the benefits of using eLabJournal in scientific workflows”",
        "“Search and retrieve inventory and journal entries efficiently”",
        "“Track samples supplies and equipment bookings”",
        "“Use collaborative features such as sharing experiments and adding collaborators”" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/all-trainings/introduction-elabjournal-getting-started-electronic-lab-notebook-eln-1> .

