<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/introduction-to-git-github> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Get you started with Git from zero (note that if you already use Git, this workshop will be too basic for you). We'll look into git on a command-line level &amp; GitHub online version.\r
\r
\r
	Introduction, set-up &amp; configurations\r
	Working locally: Create a repository, clone, edit, staging commits, commit &amp; push\r
	Working with your history, logs and diffs (including undo changes)\r
	Working in a project: Forking, branching, pull requests, fetch, merge, pull &amp; push\r
\r
\r
In the most likely case, we have time left:\r
\r
\r
	Resolving common problems\r
	Collaborating tactics\r
	Gitignore files\r
""" ;
