<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/introduction-to-protein-structure-analysis-and-alphafold> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """This two-day training session will provide the basics of protein structure determination and how this information is stored in databases. 

We will explore and search in online databases containing protein structure information including models from AlphaFoldDB. With the aid of the Yasara View program, we will visualize protein structures on the first day. Different hands-on exercises will allow you to compare the structure of homologues. We will use (online) tools to quantify various interactions in the structures.


On the second day, we will use AlphaFold2 via the HPC cluster at the VSC UGhent to predict structural models of proteins. We will also investigate how to find homologous structures via 3D searches. In the afternoon, the second day is dedicated to your own research question you might want to address via structural predictions using AlphaFold2.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2022-04-29 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Belgium" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Zwijnaarde" ;
                            schema1:postalCode "9052" ;
                            schema1:streetAddress "Ghent - VIB/UGent FSVM II, Technologiepark 75" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "51.033713" ;
                    schema1:longitude "3.706543" ] ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "VIB" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2022-04-28 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:inLanguage "en" ;
    schema1:keywords "basic bioinformatics" ;
    schema1:name "Introduction to Protein Structure Analysis and AlphaFold" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "VIB Training" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/all-trainings/introduction-protein-structure-analysis-and-alphafold> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/introduction-to-protein-structure-analysis-and-prediction> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description "Understanding protein structure is essential for researchers in molecular biology, bioinformatics, and structural biology, as it underpins insights into function, interaction, and disease mechanisms. This two-day training is designed for early-career researchers, PhD students, and postdocs who are new to protein structure analysis. Participants will gain hands-on experience with key tools and databases, including ChimeraX, AlphaFoldDB, MutateX, and PROSS. They will use these tools to visualize, explore, and compare protein structures, and to design new ones. The course also introduces structure prediction methods using both online platforms (AlphaFold3, Chai-1) and our local VSC infrastructure (AlphaFold2, Boltz-1). Furthermore, we will use AlphaPulldown, a Python package that streamlines protein-protein interaction screens. On the second day, participants will apply these tools to their research questions, with guided support. By the end of the training, attendees will be equipped to independently access, analyze, and interpret protein structural data using state-of-the-art resources." ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2025-09-09 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:funder [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "Vlaams Supercomputer Centrum" ] ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Belgium" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Zwijnaarde" ;
                            schema1:postalCode "9052" ;
                            schema1:streetAddress "Ghent - VIB/UGent FSVM II, Technologiepark 75" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "51.033713" ;
                    schema1:longitude "3.71677" ] ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "VIB" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2025-09-08 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:inLanguage "en" ;
    schema1:keywords "advanced bioinformatics" ;
    schema1:name "Introduction to protein structure analysis and prediction" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "VIB Training" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches "Apply AlphaPulldown to conduct protein-protein interaction screens and interpret the predicted complexes",
        "Formulate a research question involving structural prediction and select appropriate tools (e.g. AlphaFold3 Boltz-1 Chai-1) to address it",
        "Predict 3D protein structures using AlphaFold2 on the VSC HPC and analyze the quality of the resulting models",
        "Search for structurally similar proteins using FoldSeek and evaluate the relevance of retrieved models",
        "Set up and execute in silico site-directed mutagenesis experiments on the VSC HPC using tools like MutateX or PROSS",
        "Visualize protein structures and compare homologous proteins using ChimeraX to interpret structural similarities and differences" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/all-trainings/introduction-protein-structure-analysis-and-prediction> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/introduction-to-protein-structure-analysis-and-prediction-september-2023> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """This two-day training session will provide the basics of protein structure analysis and how this information is stored in databases.

On the two days, we will explore and search in online databases containing protein structure information including models from AlphaFoldDB. Furthermore, we will visualize protein structures using Chimera. Different hands-on exercises will allow you to compare the structure of homologues. We will use (online) tools to quantify various interactions in the structures.

We will use AlphaFold2 via the HPC cluster at the VSC UGhent to predict structural models of proteins. An overview of different protein folding predictors is discussed, such as ESMFold, OpenFold and RoseTTaFold.

In the afternoon, the second day is dedicated to your own research question you might want to address via structural predictions using AlphaFold2. Additionally, we will learn to use AlphaPulldown, a Python package that streamlines protein-protein interaction screens.""" ;
