<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/introduction-to-r-data-manipulation-and-visualization> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Renato Alves, Jakob Wirbel, Mike Smith (HD-HuB), Nicolas Descostes (EMBL Rome Bioinformatics Services, Italy)\r
\r
Date:\r
February 23-26, 2021 (10:00 -13:00)\r
\r
Location:\r
Online training\r
\r
Contents:\r
In this course you will learn how to read and manipulate data using basic R and tidyverse packages followed by data visualization with ggplot2.\r
\r
- Basic information about syntax for the R programming language\r
- The RStudio interface\r
- Importing CSV files\r
- Structure of data frame objects, categorical variables (i.e. factors), basic data manipulation (adding/removing rows and columns)\r
- Calculating summary statistics\r
- Introduction to plotting\r
\r
Learning goals:\r
Introduction to the R – Data manipulation and visualization\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
This is an introduction to R designed for participants with no programming experience\r
\r
Keywords:\r
R\r
\r
Tools:\r
R""" ;
