<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/label-free-proteomics-data-analysis-in-galaxy> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """At the beginning of the course we will introduce you to the Galaxy platform and teach you how to perform basic tasks such as importing data, running tools, working with histories, creating workflows, and sharing your work. \r
\r
Then, we will dive into proteomic analyses which are split up into two parts.\r
\r
First, we will use MaxQuant to analyze classical proteomic shotgun (label-free data dependent acquisition = DDA) data. MaxQuant is a standalone tool that enables peptide and protein identification as well as quantification. \r
\r
In the second part we will perform a complete analysis workflow for data independent acquisition (DIA) data using a variety of open-source tools (including diapysef, OpenSwath, Pyprophet, MSstats). This includes generating a peptide library, refining the library and utilizing the library to identify and quantify peptides in DIA data. """ ;
    schema1:endDate "2020-12-04 00:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Belgium" ;
                    schema1:addressLocality "Ghent" ;
                    schema1:postalCode "9000" ;
                    schema1:streetAddress "Clemenspoort Gent" ] ;
            schema1:latitude "51.033713" ;
            schema1:longitude "3.706543" ] ;
    schema1:name "DDA and DIA proteomic analysis in Galaxy" ;
    schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "VIB Bioinformatics Core" ] ;
    schema1:startDate "2020-12-03 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/product/230> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/label-free-quantification-with-openms-nettab-bbcc> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Oliver Kohlbacher, Julianus Pfeuffer and Timo Sachsenberg (CIBI)\r
\r
Date:\r
11.11.2019\r
\r
Location:\r
NETTAB/BBCC 2019\r
Salerno, Italy\r
\r
Contents:\r
Computational mass spectrometry provides important tools and bioinformatic solutions for the analysis of proteomics data. Different methods for label-free quantification have been developed in recent years and were successfully applied in a wide range of studies. Non-targeted methods have shown great potential in unbiased discovery studies.\r
This de.NBI training event introduces key concepts of label-free analysis using workflow-based processing of real-life data sets. We will introduce several open-source software tools for proteomics, primarily focusing on OpenMS (http://www.OpenMS.org/).\r
In a hands-on session, we will demonstrate how to combine these tools into complex data analysis workflows including visualization of the results. Participants will have the opportunity to bring their own data and design custom analysis workflows together with instructors.\r
For participants interested in developing their own algorithms and methods within the OpenMS framework, we provide a brief introduction to pyOpenMS – the python interface to the OpenMS development library.\r
Training material and handouts will be prepared for both users that want to design proteomic workflows, as well as training material for algorithm and tool developers.\r
The participants should bring their own laptop computers. Installer versions of required software will be made available. Bringing own data is possible, but not necessary.\r
\r
Software Requirements:\r
The participants should bring their own laptop computers. Installer versions of required software will be made available.\r
\r
Keywords:\r
LC-MS based proteomics, OpenMS, workflows, KNIME, data analysis\r
\r
Tools:\r
OpenMS/OpenSWATH, KNIME""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2019-11-11 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:event_types "meetings_and_conferences" ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Italy" ;
                    schema1:addressLocality "Salerno" ;
                    schema1:addressRegion "Salerno" ;
                    schema1:streetAddress "Salerno" ] ;
            schema1:latitude "40.682441" ;
            schema1:longitude "14.768096" ] ;
    schema1:name "Label-free quantification with OpenMS - NETTAB/BBCC" ;
    schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "de.NBI" ] ;
    schema1:startDate "2019-11-11 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.denbi.de/training/693-label-free-quantification-with-openms> .

