    schema1:name "Life Science Data Management: Planning workshop" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "Centre for Digital Life Norway" ;
            schema1:url <https://www.digitallifenorway.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """Workshop participants will:\r
\r
* Understand data management requirements from the Research Council of Norway and the universities\r
* Be aware of the various national offerings for storage and understand which one is preferable, also considering data sensitivity\r
* Understand the importance of using (meta)data standards and the role of persistent identifiers in this context.\r
* Understand the key ethical and legal requirements related to their research\r
* Be aware of the various options for publishing their data and the role of licenses\r
* Create a data management plan using the Data Stewardship Wizard""" ;
    schema1:url <https://www.digitallifenorway.org/events/dmp-workshop-for-life-science-10.html> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/life-science-data-management-planning-workshop-322f024b-69fe-4a8a-b914-0fde3de6ba77> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0219>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3071>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_4012> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "PhD candidate" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "PIsSenior scientist/ Principal investigator" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Post Docs" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Life Scientists" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Researchers" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "All postgraduates" ] ;
    schema1:coursePrerequisites " Join us online and bring your project proposal . You will get the opportunity to set up a data management plan for your project with help of the Data Stewardship Wizard tool using a structured and detailed questionnaire with references to relevant resources." ;
    schema1:description """We are pleased to announce the Data Management planning workshop for Life Scientists in Norway by ELIXIR Norway and Digital Life Norway.\r
\r
All Norwegian universities require a DMP for all projects. All projects that receive funding from the Norwegian RCN are required to submit a data management plan as soon as possible after the contract with the RCN has been signed. This workshop focuses on how-to generate a data management plan for a Life Science research project that will meet both requirements.\r
\r
We would like to invite researchers (PhD candidates, Post Doctoral Fellows, Researchers, Associate Professors and Professors) in existing and upcoming Life Science projects to develop their DMP in this workshop.\r
\r
Maximum number of participants: 45\r
\r
The workshop will take place if there is at least 10 participants\r
05.06.2024\r
\r
0830 - 0900 Login support\r
\r
0900 - 0915 Introduction\r
\r
0915 - 0930 Requirements from the RCN\r
\r
0930 - 1000 Parallel session: Local recommendations &amp; storage infrastructures Institutional DMP guidelines\r
\r
1000 - 1015 Short break\r
\r
1015 - 1100 Introduction DSW\r
\r
1100 - 1120 Information on national storage infrastructures\r
\r
 *  NeLS/StoreBioInfo\r
 *  NIRD\r
 *  TSD\r
\r
1120 - 1135 Short break\r
\r
1135 - 1230 Persistent identifiers, Controlled Vocabularies &amp; Ontologies\r
\r
 \r
06.06.2024\r
\r
0900 - 1000 Key legal and ethical requirements for research in the GDPR and Health Research Act\r
\r
   * Personal Data Act\r
   * Health Research Act\r
\r
1000 - 1010 Short break\r
\r
1010 - 1050 Relevant deposition repositories/ data archives\r
\r
   * domain-specific archives (ELIXIR/EMBL-EBI, NCBI)\r
   * Dataverse NO\r
   * EGA\r
   * NIRD archive\r
   * NSD\r
\r
1050 - 1100 Short break\r
\r
1100 - 1115 Licensing of data, biological material and software\r
\r
1115 - 1230 Hands-on training and assistance to generate a data management plan\r
\r
Requirements: Join us online and bring your project proposal. You will get the opportunity to set up a data management plan for your project with the help of the Data Stewardship Wizard tool using a structured and detailed questionnaire with references to relevant resources.\r
\r
We are looking forward to seeing you at the workshop.\r
\r
Register [here](https://nettskjema.no/a/dmp-ws-24-06)  by 25 May 2024""" ;
