    schema1:description """We are pleased to announce the Data Management Planning Workshop for Life Scientists in Norway by ELIXIR Norway \r
\r
All Norwegian universities require a DMP for all projects. Projects receiving funding from the Research Council of Norway (RCN) must submit a data management plan. This workshop focuses on how to generate a data management plan (DMP) for a Life Science research project and how to use the national instance of the Data Stewardship Wizard (DSW) for this scope.\r
\r
We invite researchers (PhD candidates, Post Doctoral Fellows, Researchers, Associate Professors and Professors) in existing and upcoming Life Science projects to develop their DMP in this workshop.\r
\r
0900 - 0915 Welcome and introduction\r
\r
0915 - 0945 Requirements from the RCN\r
\r
0945 - 1030 Data Storage\r
\r
1030 - 1045 Break\r
\r
1045 - 1115 Repositories\r
\r
11015- 1145 Metadata standards and semantic interoperability\r
\r
1145 - 1200 Licensing\r
\r
1200 - 1230 Lunch\r
\r
12:30 - 1245 DSW: login and technical support\r
\r
1245 - 1315 DSW: live demonstration\r
\r
1315 - 1500 Hands-on: create a DMP for your project""" ;
