<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/lipidomics-ms-data-processing-identification-quantification-lipidomics-forum-2019> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Jacobo Miranda Ackermann, Nils Hoffmann (BioInfra.Prot / LIFS)\r
\r
Date:\r
November 10th, 2019\r
\r
Location:\r
Forschungszentrum Borstel, Borstel, Germany (as part of Lipidomics Forum 2019)\r
\r
Contents:\r
In this course, we will work through a typical use-case for bioinformatics processing lipidomics data following MS acquisition. The first part of the course will start with PeakStrainer and LipidXplorer for filtering, identification and quantification of lipid signals from shotgun lipidomics. The second part of the course will work through an example for targeted LC-MS lipidomics with LipidCreator and Skyline. The course will consist of a short theory and background overview of the employed programs complemented by the application of the tools to a provided data set.\r
\r
10:00 - 10:45 Common Introduction\r
10:45 - 12:30 LipidXplorer Shotgun Lipidomics\r
12:30 - 13:30 Lunch break\r
13:30 - 16:30 LipidCreator &amp; Skyline Targeted LC-MS lipidomics\r
\r
Learning goals:\r
Participants will be able to understand and explain the shotgun MS and targeted LC-MS workflows for lipidomics. They will learn the fundamentals of the software tools used and how to choose parameters for them. They will learn to understand and interpret the results of each step of the pipeline.\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
Basic knowledge of lipidomics, analytical workflows in lipidomics and basic familiarity with web-based and desktop applications. Participants are required to bring their own laptop in order to work on the hands-on exercises.\r
\r
Keywords:\r
Lipidomics, Shotgun, Targeted, LC-MS\r
\r
Tools:\r
PeakStrainer and LipidXplorer, LipidCreator, Skyline""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2019-11-10 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
