<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/maximizing-the-potential-of-microbial-research-data-strategies-for-effective-management-and-utilization> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
de.NBI: Helena Schnitzer, Daniel Wibberg (CAU)\r
NFDI4Microbiota: Justine Vandendorpe (ZB MED - Information Centre for Life Sciences)\r
\r
Date:\r
18th February, 2025 - 09:00 a.m. to 12:00 p.m.\r
\r
Location:\r
Online\r
\r
Contents:\r
Have you ever wondered what Research Data Management (RDM) entails? Why is it so crucial? What sets the management of microbial research data apart? If so, de.NBI and NFDI4Microbiota have designed the ideal interactive training session for you, blending informative presentations with hands-on exercises!\r
\r
With increasing pressure from funders to publish and archive research data, understanding RDM is more essential than ever. In just three hours, you will acquire foundational knowledge tailored to the management of microbial data. Guided by data management experts, you will explore the essentials of RDM, including best practices, common pitfalls, and strategies to enhance the management of data in microbial research projects.\r
\r
The course include:\r
\r
Kick off with a brief introduction to the research data lifecycle\r
Learn about the FAIR data principles\r
Dive deeper into the intricacies of effective data management\r
Gain insights from data management experts\r
Explore best practices and avoid common pitfalls\r
Focus on microbial research data management\r
This workshop is for anyone working with microbial data, interested in active learning, and gaining skills in RDM.\r
\r
If you find this intriguing, you'll be also interested in this training course\r
\r
Learning goals:\r
- Know the research data life cycle.\r
- Know the FAIR principles and understand their importance.\r
- Know the advantages of RDM.\r
- Apply generic RDM concepts to microbiology.\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
- A computer with internet connection, a webcam, a microphone and a browser.\r
- No additional prerequisites required.\r
\r
Keywords:\r
Research data management, research data life cycle, FAIR, microbial data\r
\r
Tools:\r
RDMkit, DSW, RDMO4Life""" ;
