<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/metabolomics-data-clinic-october-2019> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3172> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Peters / Neumann / Meier / Treutler (CIBI / MASH)\r
\r
Date:\r
2019/10/11 @ 10:00 - 11:00 CEST (UMT+2h)\r
\r
Location:\r
Online Meeting (DFNconf service, connection details after registration)\r
\r
Workshop goals:\r
We want to invite to the next edition of our online Metabolomics Data Clinic. The Data Clinic is a web-based video help desk which addresses (not only) beginners in the field of metabolomics and associated data analyses. We want to help people with their first steps in the exciting and multifaceted field of metabolomics, to facilitate the (sometimes) steep learning curve, and raise awareness of advanced data analysis options.\r
\r
In this Metabolomics Data Clinic we will focus in particular on:\r
- Data Sharing and data standards (MetaboLights Data Repository)\r
- Metabolite identification (MassBank, MetFrag, MetFamily)\r
- Other metabolomics-related topics\r
\r
Mode of action:\r
Our Metabolomics Data Clinic is not a webinar, you can rather think of the coffee break during a conference, where oftentimes valuable suggestions are exchanged. We usually won’t have slides, and don’t prepare a lecture.\r
\r
You are interested and have a question? We will try to answer them or tell you who might be the expert to ask. If you mail your questions to denbi-mash@ipb-halle.de a few days before the data clinic we can prepare and improve our response.\r
\r
Looking forward to see you,\r
Yours,\r
The de.NBI Data Clinic Team\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
None.\r
\r
Keywords:\r
Metabolomics, mass spectrometry, R, Bioconductor, data processing, metabolite annotation, metabolite identification""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
