<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/metatranscriptomics-analysis-using-microbiome-rna-seq-data-in-galaxy-9ba7230f-42c8-43ef-975d-36a1e0726a30> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Metatranscriptomics analysis examines how the microbiome responds to the environment by studying the taxonomic composition and functional analysis of genes expressed by the microbiome, using microbial community RNASeq data and subsequent metatranscriptomics workflows. This workshop will introduce researchers to the basic concepts and tools from the ASaiM-MT workflow. ASaiM-MT provides a curated collection of tools to explore and visualize taxonomic and functional information from metatranscriptomic sequences.

The workshop trainers will update attendees on the latest developments in Galaxy tools and workflows for functional microbiome and multi-omics analysis.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2021-05-25 00:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:funder [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "ELIXIR Belgium" ] ;
    schema1:keywords "ELIXIR",
        "advanced bioinformatics",
        "basic bioinformatics",
        "omics",
        "online" ;
    schema1:name "Metatranscriptomics analysis using microbiome RNA-seq data in Galaxy" ;
    schema1:startDate "2021-05-25 00:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://training.vib.be/all-trainings/metatranscriptomics-analysis-using-microbiome-rna-seq-data-galaxy> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/methods-for-exploring-newly-annotated-species-in-ensembl-rapid-release> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Newly sequenced genomes, including those produced by the Darwin Tree of Life project, are all added to Ensembl Rapid Release. These genomes have minimal annotation, with genes mapped onto the genome, protein domain analysis and homologue predictions. 

This webinar will guide you through the data available for newly-annotated species in the Ensembl Rapid Release site and how to cross-reference against more fully-annotated genomes in the main Ensembl genome browser.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
