<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/microbial-shotgun-metagenomics> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Microbial Shotgun Metagenomics - 5&amp;7 April 2022\r
There are many unknown and unculturable microbes found in a vast array of different environments. Shotgun metagenomics is an approach to capture all the genetic information in a sample, providing the taxonomic and metabolic information of all present organisms. In this course we will analyse shotgun metagenomic sequencing data from stool samples to compare western and Korean diets. At the end of the course you will be able to quantify the taxonomic composition with Kraken2 &amp; Bracken, and determine the metabolic profile with the bioBakery suite of tools.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2022-04-07 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "Microbial shotgun metagenomics " ;
    schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "NEOF" ] ;
    schema1:startDate "2022-04-05 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfB5V4HBkSaF6-xXdgpyYLYl0v1yrpWJesHgiy7WCYfXXk9Uw/viewform> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/microbiome-data-analysis-workshop> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Life Science Researchers" ] ;
    schema1:description """We cordially invite you to our first Microbiome Data Analyses Workshop!\r
This event will be held April, 20-23 2020, at Hasselt University.    \r
\r
The international workshop is organised jointly by the\r
Data Sciences Institute and Center for Environmental Sciences. \r
\r
The MDAW brings leading scientists to UHasselt to discuss their newest developments, statistical tools, \r
and latest findings in the rapidly expanding field of microbiome data analyses and high-throughput sequencing.\r
This event is held to encourage PhD students and Postdocs dealing with large and complicated, highly\r
dimensional microbiome datasets, to get an overview of the current state-of-the art in amplicon\r
sequence data analyses, teached in lectures and hands-on sessions.\r
Additionally, this workshop aims to promote scientific networking and\r
potential research collaborations at both national and international levels.\r
\r
For more details and registration, please read further below.\r
\r
We are looking forward to meeting you at the 1st Microbiome Data Analyses Workshop!\r
\r
On behalf of the organizing committee,\r
Professor Dr. Olivier Thas, dr. Sofie Thijs, dr. Stefanie Kerkhofs""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2020-04-23 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
