<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/multiple-sequence-alignment-with-jalview-and-protein-structure-and-function> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:alternateName "Jalview hands-on workshop" ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Life Science Researchers" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "PhD students" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "principle investigators" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "postdoctoral researchers" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "bioinformaticians" ] ;
    schema1:description """Date: Monday 14th to Tuesday 15th May 2018\r
Time: 9.00 to 17.00\r
Location: MSTC, Sherrington Building, University of Liverpool, L69 3BX\r
\r
Overview\r
This two day hands-on training course is aimed at students and researchers who want to gain practical understanding of the tools and approaches for protein sequence, structure and function prediction and analysis.\r
\r
In day 1, participants will be introduced to Jalview - a free desktop application for the visualisation and comparative analysis of protein, DNA and RNA sequences. Jalview can integrate data from Ensembl, Uniprot, PDBe, Rfam and Pfam, and can access a range of tools for multiple sequence alignment, conservation analysis and secondary structure and disorder prediction, including the widely used JPred4.\r
\r
On the second day, participants will learn to use Jalview’s 3D structure visualisation capabilities in conjunction with UCSF Chimera, and take a whistle-stop tour of the methodologies and tools for prediction and analysis of Protein 3D structure and function. Participants are encouraged to bring their own protein analysis problems and time will be reserved at the end of day 2 for discussion.\r
\r
Register using the link on the Jalview website:  http://www.jalview.org/training/training-courses/Multiple-Sequence-Alignment-with-Jalview-and-Protein-Structure-and\r
\r
Day 1: Multiple Sequence Alignment and Analysis with Jalview\r
Workshop trainers: Dr Jim Procter and Dr Suzanne Duce\r
9    9.15    Introduction to the Workshop\r
9.15    10.30    Session 1.Loading sequences, structures and alignments with Jalview\r
Coffee break\r
11    12.30    Session 2. Multiple alignment Creation and Alignment Reliability\r
Lunch\r
1.30    3pm    Session 3. Phylogenetic trees and subfamily analysis of Proteins and CDS\r
Coffee break\r
3.30    5pm    Session 4. Protein secondary structure and disorder prediction, and working with annotation\r
\r
Day 2: Protein Structure Analysis and Modelling\r
Workshop trainers: Dr Jim Procter and Dr Dan Rigden\r
9    9.15    Introduction to Workshop Day 2\r
9.15    9.30    Introduction to Protein 3D Structure\r
9.30    10    Viewing and Comparing 3D structures with Jalview and UCSF Chimera\r
10    10.30    Mapping sequence conservation to Biological Assemblies with Jalview\r
Coffee Break\r
11    12.30    Functional analysis of Protein Structures\r
Lunch\r
1.30    2.30    Homology modelling and model quality evaluation\r
2.30    3.15    Ab initio models and searching for fold matches\r
3.15    3.30    Wrap up: Function Analysis and 3D models\r
Coffee Break\r
4pm    5pm    Analyse your own protein sequences and structures.\r
""" ;
