    schema1:inLanguage "en" ;
    schema1:name "NEOF - Introduction to sequencing data and quality control" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "ELIXIR UK" ;
            schema1:url <https://elixiruknode.org/activities/training> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """At the end of this book learners will be able to:\r
\r
- Explain how sequencing by synthesis works.\r
- Understand where common Illumina errors come from.\r
- Quality check Illumina fastq files with fastQC and multiQC.\r
- Quality control Illumina fastq files by trimming and filtering.\r
- Explain how ONT & PacBio sequencing works.\r
- Understand the advantages and disadvantages of both technologies.\r
- Quality check ONT data with NanoPlot.\r
- Remove ONT adaptors with Porechop.\r
- Filter ONT reads by length and quality with Chopper.\r
- Filter adapters from PacBio data with HiFiAdapterFilt.\r
- Convert PacBio BAM files to fastq.\r
- Quality check PacBio CCS reads with RabbitQCPlus.""" ;
    schema1:url <https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfzx8jGo0sFdosabS4MEubjBWRjoMEK_FK-qjSfu_f2PaoV6A/viewform> .

