<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/nfdi4microbiota-annual-conference> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3071>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3301> ;
    schema1:description """# Join the NFDI4Microbiota Conference 2025 in Cologne!\r
\r
The **NFDI4Microbiota** consortium brings together researchers from across disciplines to improve microbiome research through better data practices, infrastructure, and community support. Our goal is to make microbiome data **FAIR** — *Findable, Accessible, Interoperable, and Reusable* — and to empower scientists with tools and standards for high-quality, reproducible research.\r
\r
Under the motto **“From Lab to Publication – Bridging the Gap with Best Practices”**, this year’s conference will take place from **30 September to 2 October 2025** at **ZB MED – Information Centre for Life Sciences in Cologne**.\r
\r
 **What to expect:**\r
- Hands-on workshops where you can learn to apply NFDI4Microbiota services  \r
- The opportunity to test your skills on a small training dataset  \r
- Inspiring keynote talks and interactive poster sessions  \r
- Community exchange and best practices for microbiome research  \r
\r
\r
## Workshop Topics Summary\r
\r
### Track: From Bench to Browser – Microbiome Analysis Without Coding Skills\r
\r
- **Workshop 1:** Introduction to Qiita for 16S amplicon data analysis\r
- **Workshop 2:** Cloud-based metagenomics workflows using CloWM\r
\r
### Track: From Lab Bench to Data Bench – Practical Research Data Management\r
\r
- **Workshop 3:** Metadata standards from the Genomic Standards Consortium (GSC)\r
- **Workshop 4:** Implementing Electronic Lab Notebooks (ELNs) with eLabFTW\r
- **Workshop 5:** Basics of research data management and data management plans (DMPs)\r
- **Workshop 6:** Accessing virus metadata and sequences via VirJenDB\r
\r
### Track: From Pipelines to Portals – Next-Generation Tools for Microbiome Analysis\r
\r
- **Workshop 7:** Extracting and resolving strain identifiers using StrainInfo\r
- **Workshop 8:** Federated FAIR data infrastructure with Aruna v3\r
- **Workshop 9:** Benchmarking metagenomics tools with the CAMI portal\r
\r
👉 **Workshop sign-up is available during conference registration.**\r
\r
\r
We look forward to welcoming you to Cologne!""" ;
