<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/non-targeted-label-free-proteomics-gcb-2021> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Timo Sachsenberg (CIBI)\r
\r
Date:\r
09.09.2019\r
\r
Location:\r
GCB 2021 - Online\r
\r
Contents:\r
The course introduces key concepts of non-targeted label-free proteomics. Non-targeted methods are ideal for unbiased discovery studies and scale well for large-scale studies (e.g., clinical proteomics). Based on example datasets we will then introduce several open-source software tools for proteomics primarily focusing on OpenMS (www.openms.org). We will demonstrate how these tools can be combined into complex data analysis workflows including visualization of results. Participants will have the opportunity to design custom analysis workflows together with instructors.\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
Target audience are computational scientists interested in working with raw mass spectrometric data.\r
\r
Learning goals:\r
- Introduction to computational mass spectrometry proteomics\r
- OpenMS and the integration platform KNIME\r
- Hands-on: Identification and Quantification workflow for Label-free quantitative proteomics\r
- Optional: Developing tools with the OpenMS library\r
- Optional: Large scale data processing with OpenMS (nextflow or galaxy)\r
\r
Software Requirements:\r
Installer versions of required software will be made available.\r
\r
Keywords:\r
LC-MS based proteomics, OpenMS, workflows, KNIME, data analysis\r
\r
Tools:\r
OpenMS/pyOpenMS, KNIME""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2021-09-09 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:event_types "meetings_and_conferences" ;
    schema1:name "Non-targeted label-free Proteomics - GCB 2021" ;
    schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "de.NBI" ] ;
    schema1:startDate "2021-09-09 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.denbi.de/training/1273-non-targeted-label-free-proteomics-gcb-2021> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/nordic-elixir-goblet-train-the-trainer> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:alternateName "Nordic ELIXIR-GOBLET Train-the-Trainer" ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Training Designers" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Trainers" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "PhD Scholars, Graduates and Post Graduates, Professors, Associate Professors, Assistant Professors, Bio instruments Professionals, Bio-informatics Professionals, Directors, CEO’s of Organizations, Supply Chain companies, Manufacturing Companies, Software development companies, Research Institutes and members" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Educators" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Training instructors" ] ;
    schema1:description """This course offers guidance, ideas and tips for designing training/teaching, development and delivery on training activities, all based on research-driven educational principles. This course will cover 4 main topics:\r
\r
1. Learning principles and how they apply to training and teaching\r
2. Design and plan session, course, materials\r
3. Teaching techniques to enhance learner engagement and participation\r
4. Assessment and feedback in training and teaching\r
\r
Note! The course is highly interactive and hence it is important that you, as a participant, actively contribute to all sessions and elements of the course\r
\r
This course will be delivered through Canvas learning management system.\r
\r
**Register at: [bit.ly/register-nordic-ttt](https://bit.ly/register-nordic-ttt)**\r
\r
Deadline for applying to the course is 3rd of April. You will receive notification regarding acceptance to the course or if you are on the reserve list no later than one week after the closing of the registration.\r
\r
**Course fee** \r
\r
There is no course attendance fee.\r
\r
Note! If you are accepted and decide not to attend without communicating the reason for the no-show with us, we will invoice a no-show-fee of 200 Euros.\r
\r
The invoicing information needs to be included in the registration in order to guarantee your spot in the training event, if you are to be accepted. By giving the invoice information you hereby confirm that the group leader/PI/manager has given a consent regarding your possible participation in the Training event. NOTE – Uppsala University cannot invoice individuals.\r
\r
**Course content**\r
\r
Learning Objectives:\r
\r
- To get acquainted with Learning principles and how they apply to training\r
- To be able to select and use training techniques that can help enhance learner engagement and participation\r
- To learn how to use assessment and feedback in training\r
- To learn about session, course, and materials design\r
\r
Learning Outcome:\r
\r
By the end of this course, learners will be able to:\r
\r
- Name learning principles that a good teacher/instructor should have in mind\r
- Describe at least three training techniques, drawing on learning principles\r
- Design a training session and a course\r
- Develop assessment questionnaires\r
- Enumerate types of materials needed for each part of a training session or course\r
\r
**Target audience**\r
\r
Whoever is interested in becoming a trainer/instructor, or improving your training skills. If you have questions like the following ones, this course may be very helpful to you.\r
\r
- How learning works?\r
- How do I use learning principles and theories to improve my teaching/training?\r
- How do I make my teaching/training more engaging and effective?\r
- How should I adjust my teaching/training to different types of learners?\r
- How do I ensure learning progress?\r
- How can I assess whether my students are actually understanding my lessons? Are they actually learning?\r
- What is the best balance between theory and practice?\r
- How can I best assess whether learning is occurring and/or has occurred?\r
- What works in a classroom and what doesn’t?\r
\r
**Selection criteria**\r
We will accept a maximum of 20 participants. Priority will be given to applicants from institutes and organisations across the Nordic research community and to participants from Nordic ELIXIR nodes.\r
\r
**Course Team**\r
\r
Instructors:\r
- Jessica Lindvall (ELIXIR-SE Training Coordinator, NBIS, Sweden\r
- Nina Norgren (ELIXIR-SE, Training Coordinator, NBIS, Sweden)\r
- Nazeefa Fatima (ELIXIR-NO, Data Steward, UiO, Norway)\r
- Erik Hjerde (ELIXIR-NO, Training Coordinator, UiT, Norway)\r
- Priit Adler (ELIXIR-EE, Trainer, UT, Estonia)\r
- Allegra Via (ELIXIR-IT, Training Coordinator, IBPM-CNR, IT)\r
- Patricia Palagi (ELIXIR-CH, Training coordinator, SIB)\r
\r
Organisers: ELIXIR-SE, ELIXIR-NO, ELIXIR-FI, and ELIXIR-EE""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "online" ;
            schema1:endDate "2022-05-13 16:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:maximumAttendeeCapacity 20 ;
            schema1:startDate "2022-05-10 12:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:keywords "Curriculum development, course design, learning outcomes, Bloom's Taxonomy, assessment, course evaluation, training trainers, training material",
        "ELIXIR Training Platform",
        "Education",
        "GOBLET",
        "Online learning",
        "Teaching",
        "Train the trainer",
        "Train trainer",
        "Trainer skills",
        "Training technique",
