<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/nucleic-acids-model-building-workshop> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0077>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_0097>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_1317> ;
    schema1:description """Workshop will concentrate on using the dinucleotide conformers (NtC) as a tool\r
enabling more reliable solution of crystal and cryo-EM structures of nucleic acids. The current\r
version of the dnatco.org web server as well as the development version introducing a\r
universal (for both DNA and RNA) set of NtC classes will be demonstrated.\r
\r
We will show prototype of the procedure(s) to fit our library of the dinucleotide\r
conformers to electron density, as well as method of building NA models with the user\r
specified NtC sequence, and morphing between two NA structures. All that by using\r
MacroMoleculeBuilder (MMB) by Samuel Flores. Sam will be present to show these new\r
functions.\r
\r
Importantly, we also work with Paul Emsley on new Coot features. We currently\r
concentrate on initial model building by fitting into experimental electron density and validation\r
using the NtC. Paul is unavailable for the meeting but we shall be able to present and discuss\r
all new and planned Coot features concentrating on the synergy between different tools.\r
Your presence would be extremely important to be able to look at the initial model\r
building and validation from user's perspective and suggest improvements of an early phase\r
of building a truly useful tool. It will be great if you bring your own problem to test the\r
emerging system.\r
\r
We will try to cover two nights (Nov 15-16 and 16-17) in a hotel including breakfast\r
( www.hotel-ilf.cz ). There is also no registration fee for the workshop thanks to the support\r
provided by the ELIXIR-CZ.\r
\r
For more details contact Jiří Černý ( jiri.cerny@ibt.cas.cz ), ideally till November 7.\r
""" ;
