<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/omics-analyses-pathways-networks-and-biomarkers> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0091>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_0092>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3474>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3678> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Experimental Researchers" ] ;
    schema1:description """A CBF three-day face-to-face intense course for experimental biologists and clinicians\r
\r
Demystify computational biology and come to learn:\r
-Functional &amp; pathway enrichment\r
-In-silico biomarker discovery using multivariate methods and machine learning\r
-Identification of transcriptional hubs &amp; master regulators via network analysis\r
-Best experimental design practices  \r
-Dedicated time to talk about your data and experiments\r
\r
Theory and practice sessions. 1-1 support.  \r
\r
Requirements\r
All materials have been built using relevant life sciences/clinical examples. The course has been designed for delegates with some R experience (basics). A refresher of R from beginner level is included and all relevant code will be provided such as delegates will only have to run specific scripts. \r
\r
Administrative details\r
A significantly reduced access fee of £225 is available to all academic delegates. Other delegates will be quoted upon request. \r
""" ;
