<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/openms-developer-conference> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Timo Sachsenberg, Kyowon Jeong\r
\r
Date:\r
10-16 MARCH 2024\r
\r
Location:\r
NEAR MALAGA, SPAIN\r
\r
Contents:\r
The OpenMS developer conference brings bioinformaticians working in computational mass spectrometry together to shape the future development of OpenMS. It is targeted to core developers, new developers, and potential future contributors. Short talks, developer tutorials, and code sprints will be intertwined. Participants will have the opportunity to design custom tools and workflows together with instructors. External users are welcome to bring their own ideas and will receive detailed feedback as well as help getting started in OpenMS development. Progress will be tracked on our GitHub page with a resume of each day.\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
Target audience: This developer conference is targeted to core, new and potential future developers of the OpenMS library and its tools.\r
\r
Learning goals:\r
* Developing algorithms and tools with the OpenMS library and pyOpenMS\r
* Working with OpenMS, its build system, and its datastructures\r
* Deeper insights into new and established algorithms of the library\r
* Learning the GitHub workflow of OpenMS\r
\r
Keywords:\r
LC-MS-based proteomics and metabolomics, OpenMS, C++, algorithms for mass spectrometry, software engineering/design\r
\r
Tools:\r
OpenMS, git, cmake, C++ gcc / clang toolchain\r
\r
Audience: This developer conference is targeted to core, new and potential future developers of the OpenMS library and its tools.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2024-03-16 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
