<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/openms-user-meeting-2024> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Sam Wein, Kyowon Jeong, Matteo Pilz, Axel Walter, Joshua Charkow (CIBI)\r
\r
Date:\r
17 – 18 October 2024\r
\r
Location:\r
KNIME GmbH, Körtestr. 10, 10967 Berlin, Germany\r
\r
Contents:\r
We are pleased to announce the 2024 OpenMS User Meeting, hosted by KNIME GmbH in Berlin, Germany. The meeting will provide a comprehensive introduction to data analysis with OpenMS, alongside specialized tutorials led by experts in the field. This event aims to equip application users and expert data analysts with the latest tools and techniques for omics data analysis.\r
\r
Learning Goals:\r
- Comprehensive understanding of OpenMS tools and services\r
- Application areas in genome informatics and workflows\r
- Advanced techniques in proteomics and metabolomics\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
None\r
\r
Keywords:\r
Workflows, Proteomics, Metabolomics\r
\r
Tools:\r
OpenMS""" ;
