<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/pangaea-community-workshop-may-2026-finding-and-retrieving-data-from-pangaea> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
PANGAEA Training team (BioData)\r
\r
Date:\r
14.05.2026 10:30 – 12:30\r
15.05.2026 10:30 – 12:30\r
\r
Location:\r
Online\r
\r
Contents:\r
Embark on a comprehensive, 2-day, 4-hour journey to master the art of discovering and leveraging PANGAEA's vast repository of published Earth &amp; Environment and Biodiversity research datasets. Through a carefully crafted blend of theoretical foundations and hands-on exercises, participants will gain a deep understanding of how to systematically find, utilize, and integrate relevant datasets into their own work and unlock new insights. Including (but not limited to) Python-based workflows, leveraging the power of virtual research environments like Jupyter notebooks to streamline data analysis.\r
\r
More Information can be found here.\r
\r
Learning goals:\r
By the end of the workshop, participants will be able to use targeted and advanced search methods to sifting through the large spectrum of earth, biodiversity and environmental data published at PANGAEA, and to integrate these search results into typical analytical and data science workflows mainly using the Python scripting language. They will further be introduced to a powerful (and unique) feature, the Data Warehouse, which allows to conveniently perform meta-studies of PANGAEA's manually curated and extensively harmonized data content on a parameter/variable level by methods, geo-location or time slice.\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
non\r
\r
Keywords:\r
PANGAEA, Workflows\r
\r
Tools:\r
PANGAEA, Python, Jupyter Notebook""" ;
