<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/practical-data-and-software-skills-for-reproducible-research-workshops> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Investigators and researchers working in all areas of the life sciences." ] ;
    schema1:description """Two one-day introductory workshops on the skills and technologies you need for publishable and reproducible data-driven science. People can register for one or both workshops.\r
\r
Practical Data Skills Workshop: 2-3 October, 2019\r
Practical Software Skills Workshop: 3-4 October, 2019\r
\r
Working with “Big data” is challenging for most researchers and the barriers to publication can be difficult. These workshops introduce free open-source approaches that reduce these challenges and help you deliver research that is more impactful, open, and reproducible.\r
\r
Training will focus on solutions developed by publicly funded cyberinfrastructure developed in the US (CyVerse) and Europe (CyVerse UK, ELIXIR, EOSC, and others). Lessons learned will prepare you with skills you can apply no matter which computing platforms you use.""" ;
