<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/ready-for-biodata-management-day-2-day-data-management> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:alternateName "Day 2 Day Data Management" ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Life Science Researchers" ] ;
    schema1:contact "info[at]biodata.pt" ;
    schema1:description """This is a one-day, introductory, hands-on course aimed at Life Sciences researchers (with at least PhD frequency level) and lab managers.\r
\r
It focuses on the day-to-day data management aspects of research activities, like planning, annotation, deposit, aiming to empower researchers and lab managers to improve the efficiency of data management throughout the life cycle of the data and enable reproducibility and reusability.\r
\r
The course features an introduction to topics such as The FAIR Principles and Open Science best practices, Data Management Plans, metadata standard and ontologies, an overview of online data management resources, and practical components centred on data documentation using Electronic Lab Notebooks and data sharing using DataVerse.\r
\r
This Face-to-face course was delivered in four Portuguese R&amp;I institutions in January 2023.\r
\r
If you would like to host such a course, please contact us by email via info[at]biodata.pt, using Ready for BioData Management Course as a Subject.""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2023-01-31 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:funder [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "elixir" ],
        [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "impact implementation study" ],
        [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "elixir-converge" ] ;
    schema1:hostInstitution "BioData.pt" ;
    schema1:keywords "Data management",
        "electronic lab notebook",
        "research data management" ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Portugal" ;
                    schema1:addressLocality "Lisbon" ] ;
            schema1:latitude "38.707751" ;
            schema1:longitude "-9.136592" ] ;
    schema1:name "\"Ready for BioData Management?\" Day 2 Day Data Management" ;
    schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "BioData.pt" ] ;
    schema1:startDate "2023-01-13 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <http://ready4biodatamanagement.biodata.pt/courses.html#day2day> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/ready-for-biodata-management-dmp-double-course-83906c14-665f-4a18-89c4-bf4913994695> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """“Ready for BioData Management? | DMP Double Course”. A complete course that gathers the “Introduction to Data Management Plans” and “Advanced Data Management Plans” courses.\r
\r
Introduction to Data Management Plans is an introductory course aiming at disseminating Data Management best practices and teaching the basics of making and using Data Management Plans (DMP) in the context of research activities.\r
\r
The course features two introductory lectures on Research Data Management and DMPs.\r
\r
Advanced Data Management Plans" is a one-day hands-on course where participants will be guided through the process of preparing a real DMP for a real research project, according to the H2020 DMP template.\r
\r
The course assumes participants have basic notions of DMPs. It will feature a lecture introducing the DMPOnline platform that the participants will be using, and another lecture overviewing the H2020 DMP template, but the majority of the course will be a hands-on session where participants prepare a DMP in the platform, in pairs.\r
\r
Participants are encouraged to bring their own research project or project plan, in the interest of producing a DMP that is relevant for them.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2021-10-13 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:funder [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "ELIXIR-CONVERGE" ] ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Portugal" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Lisbon" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "38.707751" ;
                    schema1:longitude "-9.136592" ] ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "BioData.pt" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2021-10-12 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:name "“Ready for BioData Management? | DMP Double Course”." ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "ELIXIR Portugal" ;
            schema1:url <https://elixir-portugal.org> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://github.com/BioData-PT/Ready4BioDataManagement> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/ready-for-biodata-management-dmp-double-course-a7ebe51a-b0b0-483c-91e3-d4539c8e1afb> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """## Registration\r
\r
After registration, they will be required to pay a registration fee as listed in the table below.\r
\r
| Modality | Regular registration | BioData.pt members |\r
| One day | €40 | €20 |\r
| Both days | €60 | €30 |\r
\r
* * *\r
\r
## Course Description\r
\r
**Day 1:**"Introduction to Data Management Plans" is an introductory course aiming at disseminating Data Management best practices and teaching the basics of making and using Data Management Plans (DMPs) in the context of research activities. It features two introductory lectures on Research Data Management and DMPs, followed by a hands-on DMP exercise where participants will form groups to fill in a DMP for a mock research project, using Google Spreadsheets. The produced DMPs will then be reviewed and discussed.\r
\r
**Day 2:**"Advanced Data Management Plans" is a follow-up course aiming to empower participants to make their own real Data Management Plan according to the Science Europe DMP Template (adopted by FCT) on an online platform. It features three lectures covering advanced concepts in data management, the Science Europe DMP Template, and Data Stewardship Wizard (the DMP creation tool that participants will use), followed by a hands-on session where participants create their DMP, either alone or in pairs, with assistance from the teachers. Participants are encouraged to bring their own research projects to be the object of their DMP.\r
\r
Both courses will be delivered online, in real time, via Zoom.\r
\r
* * *\r
\r
## Target Audience\r
\r
Researchers, Lab Managers, PhD and Master Students, other science professionals.  \r
No prior knowledge required for day 1.  \r
Basic knowledge of data management or participation in day 1 expected for day 2.\r
\r
* * *\r
\r
## Trainers\r
\r
João Cardoso (BioData.pt/INESC-ID)  \r
Daniel Faria (BioData.pt/INESC-ID)\r
\r
* * *\r
\r
## Agenda\r
\r
**Day 1**  \r
9:30 Check-in  \r
9:35 Introduction to Research Data Management (Daniel Faria)  \r
10:45 Break  \r
11:00 Demystifying Data Management Plans (João Cardoso)  \r
11:25 Introduction to the Hands-On DMP Exercise (João Cardoso &amp; Daniel Faria)  \r
11:40 Hands-On DMP Session (steps 1 and 2)  \r
13:00 Lunch break  \r
14:00 Hands-On DMP Session (steps 3, 4 and 5)  \r
16:00 Final discussion  \r
16:30 End  \r
  \r
**Day 2**  \r
9:30 Check-in  \r
9:35 The Science Europe DMP Template (João Cardoso)  \r
9:55 Advanced Data Management Topics (Daniel Faria)  \r
10:30 The Data Stewardship Wizard (João Cardoso)  \r
10:45 Break  \r
11:00 Hands-On DMP Creation Exercise (Part 1)  \r
13:00 Lunch break  \r
14:00 Hands-On DMP Creation Exercise (Part 2)  \r
16:30 End""" ;
