<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/reproducibility-in-practice> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description "This course is part of a micro-credential track, a micro-credential has the added value of being like a mini-diploma. When following the full track you will become able to improve the reproducibility of your research. Check this opportunity : Reproducible Data Analysis: an Essential Capability in Modern Science.Join us in to brainstorm the challenges and solutions of data analysis reproducibility. You will have the chance to brainstorm, discuss and use your creativity to solve real life projects with a group of people. No matter your background and level of expertise this is a great opportunity of exchange, improving critical thinking, problem solving and exchange with experts.After a morning of exchange you will have the chance to hear the how the experts have tackled each challenge and to ask questions to discover more about their thinking process. It will be a fun activity with opportunities for networking and to think of your own challenges while taking the chance to expand your creativity and talking to people that have been navigating this water for a little longer." ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2025-02-28 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:funder [ a schema1:Organization ;
