<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/reproducible-research-2023> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """The following topics and tools are covered in the course:\r
\r
    Data management\r
    Project organisation\r
    Git\r
    Conda\r
    Snakemake\r
    Nextflow\r
    R Markdown\r
    Jupyter\r
    Docker\r
    Singularity\r
\r
At the end of the course, students should be able to:\r
\r
    Use good practices for data analysis and management\r
    Clearly organise their bioinformatic projects\r
    Use the version control system Git to track and collaborate on code\r
    Use the package and environment manager Conda\r
    Use and develop workflows with Snakemake and Nextflow\r
    Use R Markdown and Jupyter Notebooks to document and generate automated reports for their analyses\r
    Use Docker and Singularity to distribute containerized computational environments""" ;
