<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/sib-phd-training-network-annual-retreat-0e547bfb-2bb1-466d-8ca4-2961223dcdd9> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """**This course is exclusively reserved to the members of the [SIB PhD Training Network](https://www.sib.swiss/training/for-sib-phd-students).**

# Overview
The SIB PhD Training Network retreat is an annual informal and interactive event offering the opportunity to their members (students of the Swiss Schools of Higher Education registered as SIB members) to meet their peers and present their PhD project (or possibly their master project for students who have just started). This year, the event will focus on career paths by inviting alumni of the Training Network.

# Objectives of the event

* have a better overview of the various career paths.
* get to know the profile of the institutions and companies presented by the invited speakers.
* interact with other students and with the invited speakers and possibly get in contact for career opportunities

# Program


**22 June**
*Morning Session (10h00 - 12h30) – Careers in Academia*
*Afternoon Session (14h00 - 16h30) – Careers in large Biopharma companies*
 
**23 June**
*Morning Session (9h00 - 12h00) – Careers in startups &amp; small companies*
*Afternoon Session (13h45 - 16h00) – Careers in various fields*

# Application
Registration is free and open, but is **strictly reserved for members of the SIB PhD Training Network.**

You will be informed by email of your registration confirmation.

# Venue
University of Bern. More information will be provided to the participants.


For more information, please contact [Gregoire Rossier](mailto:gregoire.rossier@sib.swiss).""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2023-06-23 00:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:keywords "career",
        "community",
        "industry" ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Switzerland" ;
                    schema1:addressLocality "Bern" ] ;
            schema1:latitude "46.948271" ;
            schema1:longitude "7.451451" ] ;
