<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/single-cell-rnaseq-data-analysis-2022> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:alternateName "This course provides an introduction to single-cell genomics, for researchers who have basic experience of bioinformatics and who are planning a single-cell project." ;
    schema1:contact "training@earlham.ac.uk" ;
    schema1:description """This course provides an introduction to single-cell genomics, for researchers who have basic experience of bioinformatics and who are planning a single-cell project. \r
\r
The course will consist of a mixture of conceptual and methodological lectures and hands-on bioinformatics sessions, including best practice and tips as learned first-hand by Earlham Institute’s faculty. Participants will gain first-hand experience by learning how to assess data quality with the guidance of the faculty, troubleshoot small problems, and review the results. Hands-on sessions will be using data generated using both Smartseq2 and 10X protocols.\r
\r
There will be plenty of opportunities to ask questions, and an optional group discussion with other participants and the course trainers.\r
\r
This course will be delivered in-person at the Earlham Institute, with the option to join remotely via Zoom.\r
\r
What will I learn?\r
Understand the different data generated in scRNAseq experiments and analyses\r
Learn how to assess data quality\r
Introduction and hands-on experience in available tools and resources for analysing and visualising single-cell data\r
Introduction to cell type identification and pseudotime analyses \r
Introduction to long read sequencing with application to transcript annotation and quantification in single cell research""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2022-11-10 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "United Kingdom" ;
                    schema1:addressRegion "Norfolk" ;
                    schema1:streetAddress "Earlham Institute (EI), Colney Lane" ] ;
            schema1:latitude "52.621792" ;
            schema1:longitude "1.219034" ] ;
    schema1:name "Single-Cell RNAseq Data Analysis 2022" ;
    schema1:startDate "2022-11-07 10:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.earlham.ac.uk/events/single-cell-rnaseq-data-analysis-2022> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/single-cell-rnaseq-data-analysis-47ce1199-7e9a-4e2d-a3f9-7109ddc94f08> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Graduates, postgraduates, and PIs, who are using, or planning to use, single cell RNA-seq technology in their research and want to learn how to process and analyse single cell RNA-seq data." ] ;
    schema1:description "Single cell RNA-Seq offers many advantages over bulk RNA-Seq, but the richer data produced requires a more complex analysis. In this course we will learn about the advantages of single cell sequencing, and when it may be an appropriate choice, how to perform common types of data analysis, and to spot and deal with potential problems.  We will analyse 10X genomics data with the R package Seurat." ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
