<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/single-cell-transcriptomics-summer-school> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description "Registration deadline: 15th of August 2024The kick-off day on 9 September is open to everyone and free. It features a comprehensive overview of single cell transcriptomics, designed for those looking to understand the basics, get started with single cell omics, and navigate the latest advancements in the field.In the next three days, we will go through the entire workflow from data acquisition to data analysis.  At the end of the course, attendees will better understand the dos and don’ts in single cell transcriptomics and they will be able to set up and analyze their own experiments. The summer school is organized with the support of 10x Genomics and Element Biosciences." ;
