<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/sis-containers-data-access-movement-and-management-workshop> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Accessing, moving and managing data can be a difficult task for our users across ELIXIR. Datasets grow ever larger and more numerous, and simple HTTP becomes less adequate. Some challenges are:\r
\r
\r
	How do you give your users download options that won’t overwhelm them with complexity?\r
	What do you do when they want to process data on a public cloud, but it’s sitting on their local storage?\r
	How do you give them a uniform way of accessing data?\r
	How do you make it easier for them to upload their field data to management systems for processing in a secure manner?\r
\r
\r
These are just a few of the questions that we’ll explore in this workshop. After each presentation there will be a short period for Q&amp;A and a longer discussion session at the end.\r
\r
Duration: 09:30-12:30 CET.\r
\r
Chairs:  Justin Clark-Casey (EMBL-EBI), Frederik Coppens (ELIXIR Belgium)""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2022-03-31 09:30:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:name "SIS Containers: Data Access, Movement and Management Workshop" ;
    schema1:startDate "2022-03-31 09:30:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.elixir-europe.org/events/sis-containers-workshop> .

