<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/software-carpentry-course-university-of-bergen> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0605>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3372> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Researchers" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "PhD candidates" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Post-docs" ] ;
    schema1:contact "illimar.rekand@uib.no" ;
    schema1:description """This course will provide researchers with computational tools to address their research questions in new or more efficient and reproducible ways. The course is aimed at novices and no previous programming knowledge is required. The course follows the [Software Carpentry teaching concept and lessons](https://software-carpentry.org/).\r
\r
The course is hosted by the [Centre for Digital Life Norway,](https://www.digitallifenorway.org/) [ELIXIR-Norway,](https://elixir.no/) [NRIS](https://www.sigma2.no/nris) and [the University of Bergen Library Digital Lab](https://www.uib.no/en/digitallab). It is open to all PhD students, postdocs and researchers. Participants connected to one of the hosting initatives will be given priority.\r
\r
# Course content\r
Software Carpentry aims to help researchers get their work done in less time and with less pain by teaching them basic research computing skills. This course will cover the following lessons: Unix Shell, R for reproducible scientific analysis, Version Control with Git. Participants will be encouraged to help one another and to apply what they have learned to their own research problems.\r
\r
For a more detailed program, please [visit the GitHub event page](https://kjemist.github.io/2024-04-22-UiB-SWC/)\r
See also the [UiB event page](https://www.uib.no/en/ub/168267/software-carpentry-course-research-computing-skills-shell-r-and-python-reproducible)\r
\r
# Registration\r
Please sign up [using the registration link](https://skjemaker.app.uib.no/view.php?id=16467907) and include a short statement why you wish to participate in the Software Carpentry course. Participants connected to one of the hosting initatives will be given priority, beyond this participants will be accepted based on the order of sign-up. You will need to actively confirm you participation after the signup period, elsewise your spot will be offered to someone on the waiting list.\r
\r
Participants are expected to attend all course days and install software in advance. Participation in the installation help session is strongly recommended.\r
\r
The course will take place physically at the [University of Bergen Library Digital Lab.](https://www.uib.no/en/digitallab)\r
\r
# Contact\r
For questions or other inquiries, please contact: illimar.rekand@uib.no""" ;
