<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/software-faster-from-months-to-minutes> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:contact "Daniel Vaughan" ;
    schema1:description "Software Faster brings software delivery principles into the 21st century. You will learn new techniques that both enhance and replace existing agile practices, some of which are counter-intuitive and many which are completely counter to current “best practise”.  The speaker, Dan North, is the originator of Behaviour-Driven Development, an agile approach to software development that encourages teams to deliver the software that matters by emphasising the interactions between stakeholders. He is a popular keynote and session speaker at international technology conferences on a range of diverse topics." ;
    schema1:endDate "2016-09-20 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:keywords "HDRUK" ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "United Kingdom" ;
                    schema1:addressLocality "Cambridge" ;
                    schema1:postalCode "CB10 1SD" ;
                    schema1:streetAddress "European Bioinformatics Institute (EMBL-EBI), Wellcome Genome Campus" ] ;
            schema1:latitude "52.080033" ;
            schema1:longitude "0.186338" ] ;
    schema1:name "Software faster: From months to minutes" ;
    schema1:startDate "2016-09-20 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/training/events/2016/software-faster-months-minutes> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/software-sustainability-why-and-how-to-do-it> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:alternateName "BioExcel/SSI webinar by Steve Crouch" ;
    schema1:contact "Register at https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/3718052847120092173" ;
    schema1:description """This is a BioExcel webinar by Steve Crouch from [Software Sustainability Institute](https://software.ac.uk/) (SSI).\r
\r
We’ll explore the importance of **research software**, and the practices we can employ to develop it to help ensure its **sustainability** in the short, medium, and long term. We’ll also look at the different and emerging styles of _Management Plans_ for software, and how _software evaluation_ can identify areas for improvement and assist in the shaping of future development goals, and the potential for automation to allow evaluation to be conducted at scale.\r
\r
Software has a crucial role in the research process across many disciplines. As it continues to underpin our science and help push the boundaries of what is achievable, it becomes increasingly important that the sustainability of our software is given sufficient attention to ensure it can continue to evolve and grow to meet ever-changing research goals.""" ;
    schema1:eligibility "registration_of_interest" ;
    schema1:endDate "2019-11-21 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:keywords "Webinar",
        "research software",
        "software development",
        "sustainability" ;
    schema1:name "Software Sustainability – Why and How to do it" ;
    schema1:startDate "2019-11-21 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://bioexcel.eu/webinar-software-sustainability-why-and-how-to-do-it-2019-11-21/> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/soumission-de-donnees-et-metadonnees-a-biosample-et-ena-2025> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:alternateName "FAIR Data EBI 2025" ;
    schema1:description "Nous vous proposons une formation en ligne sur le processus et les outils mis en place dans le cadre des projets AgroDiv et BReIF pour soumettre des données à ENA (EMBL-EBI) associées à des descriptions riches des échantillons séquencés dans BioSamples. Le webinaire abordera une explication approfondie des fichiers d'entrée requis pour la soumission, des champs demandés dans les template ainsi qu'une démonstration de l'utilisation des scripts développés pour automatiser la soumission des données et simplifier le processus." ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2025-11-06 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Online" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "43.590472" ;
                    schema1:longitude "3.859513" ] ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "INRAE (https://www.inrae.fr/), URGI (https://urgi.versailles.inrae.fr/), URGI - US1164 (https://urgi.versailles.inrae.fr/)" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2025-11-06 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:name "Soumission de données et métadonnées à BioSample et ENA - 2025" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "IFB French Institute of Bioinformatics" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.france-bioinformatique.fr> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://moodle.france-bioinformatique.fr/course/view.php?id=44> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/soumission-de-donnees-et-metadonnees-a-embl-ebi-2024> a schema1:Course ;
