01.00 - 05.00 pm\r
\r
Concluding symposium and discussion\r
\r
05.00 - 05.30 pm\r
\r
Wrap-up and departure\r
\r
Learning goals:\r
Participants will gain hands-on experience in interpretable machine learning for multimodal biomedical data, developing the skills to collaboratively design and implement (publication-ready) bioinformatic analysesthat drive insight and impact in translational research.\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
You are a passionate PhD student or postdoctoral researcher eager to work at the intersection of cutting-edge data science and biomedical discovery?\r
\r
We welcome applicants from two complementary backgrounds:\r
\r
Bioinformatics, machine learning, or data science, with a keen interest and some hands-on experience in analyzing biological or medical data.\r
Experimental biologyor translational medicine, with a strong track record of performing your own data analyses using bioinformatics or machine learning methods.\r
If you’re excited about bridging disciplines and unlocking insights from complex biomedical data, and you have solid programming skills in Python, we’d love to have you on board.\r
\r
You must bring a modern laptop with WLAN and Python development capabilities\r
\r
Keywords:\r
Interpretable AI, ML in life sciences, multimodal data, translational research, AI in biomedical research, data integration\r
\r
Tools:\r
Python""" ;
