<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/systems-medicine-virtual-spring-seminar-series-2020> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3396>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3577> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Physicians" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "bioinformaticians" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Life Science Researchers" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Clinicians" ] ;
    schema1:description """ELIXIR Slovenia will organize a **Virtual Spring Seminar Series 2020** where experts from all over the world will share their experiences with systems medicine. \r
\r
Systems medicine is a field that will enable the translation of recent technological and scientific advances into the clinical practice. With systems medicine we will boost our understanding of disease mechanisms and the efficacy of treatments. Ultimately, systems medicine will bring a more personalised approach to healthcare, which may radically change the interaction between patients, doctors and other healthcare professionals. New healthcare approaches are an urging need, even accelerated in the Covid-19 era. \r
\r
The webinars will be hosted by **Prof. Dr. Damjana Rozman, Faculty of Medicine, University of Ljubljana, Slovenia**. You can join the webinars on **Zoom** by [following this link](https://us02web.zoom.us/j/89751733107?pwd=REJ5ak1DUllyU2xvMHFpR2ZPNWhZdz09).\r
\r
**Programme:**\r
\r
**Wednesday, 29 April 2020, 16h – 17h CEST**\r
Prof. Dr. Sona Vasudevan, Georgetown University, Washington D.C, USA\r
Title: Systems Medicine with Three-dimensional Insights \r
\r
**Thursday, 30 April 2020, 16h – 18h CEST**\r
Henning Hermjakob, EMBL-EBI, Cambridge, UK\r
Johannes Griss, Medical University of Vienna, Austria\r
Title: Reactome Pathway Analysis and Visualization\r
\r
**Thursday, 7 May 2020, 16h – 17h CEST**\r
Prof. Dr. Josep Roca, University of Barcelona, Spain\r
Title: Digital Health for Enhanced Understanding and Management of Health Events: COPD and COVID-19 as Use Cases\r
\r
**Wednesday, 13 May 2020, 16h – 17h CEST**\r
Prof. Dr. Anke-Hilse Maitland-van der Zee, Amsterdam UMC, the Netherlands\r
Title: Precision Medicine in Respiratory Medicine, Translation into Clinical Practice\r
\r
**Wednesday, 20 May 2020, 16h – 17h CEST**\r
Prof. Dr. Kristel van Steen, KU Leuven, Belgium Title: TBA\r
\r
**Wednesday, 27 May 2020, 16h – 17h CEST**\r
TBA""" ;
