<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/tools-platform-and-single-cell-omics-bring-your-workflow-to-workflowhub> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Diana Chiang Jurado (RBC), Armin Dadras (University of Göttingen)\r
\r
Date:\r
May 13th, 2025\r
\r
Location:\r
Online\r
\r
Contents:\r
This interactive session will highlight how to make your workflows more FAIR (Findable, Accessible, Interoperable, and Reusable) and citable, enhancing reproducibility and collaboration across the life sciences. In this event you will:\r
\r
Learn how FAIR principles improve workflow quality and usability.\r
Watch a step-by-step demonstration of workflow registration using single cell data analysis pipelines.\r
Bring your own workflows and get personalized guidance on how to register and share them in WorkflowHub.\r
\r
Agenda\r
-Welcome and Introduction\r
-How to make your computational workflows findable and citable\r
-Open Q\\&amp;A and discussion\r
-Demo: Registering workflows in WorkflowHub\r
-Breakout rooms for hands-on support\r
\r
Learning goals: \r
Workflow registration with WorkflowHub \r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
Whether you're a beginner or experienced developer, this event offers practical insights into improving the visibility and impact of your workflows.\r
\r
Keywords: \r
WorkflowHub\r
\r
Tools:\r
WorkflowHub""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2025-05-13 13:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
            schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                    schema1:addressCountry "Germany" ;
                    schema1:streetAddress "Deutschland" ] ;
            schema1:latitude "51.165691" ;
            schema1:longitude "10.451526" ] ;
    schema1:name "Tools Platform and Single Cell Omics: 'Bring Your Workflow' to WorkflowHub" ;
    schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "de.NBI / ELIXIR-DE" ] ;
    schema1:startDate "2025-05-13 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.denbi.de/training-courses-2025/1885-tools-platform-and-single-cell-omics-bring-your-workflow-to-workflowhub> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/tools-platform-and-single-cell-omics-bring-your-workflow-to-workflowhub-181c8645-137d-4046-8235-179b2524b68d> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """We are excited to invite you to an online event focused on enabling computational workflow best practices with the use of WorkflowHub. We will make use of exemplar workflows for the Single Cell Omics community to present and explore concepts and functions that are broadly applicable to computational workflows.\r
\r
## Event Highlights:\r
Gain insights from experts on the importance of FAIR principles in computational workflows and how they can enhance reproducibility, collaboration, and findability.\r
\r
Watch a live demonstration of workflow registration in WorkflowHub. Using computational workflows for handling and processing Single Cell data as examples, you will see how workflows can be easily registered, discovered, and shared within the scientific community.\r
\r
Participate in an interactive session where you can bring your own workflows and learn how to register and manage them in WorkflowHub. \r
\r
## Programme:\r
- Welcome and Introduction\r
- Make your computational workflows findable and citable\r
- Discussion and questions\r
- Demo workflow registration with WorkflowHub\r
- Hands-on “bring your own workflow” in breakout rooms""" ;
