<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/training-clinic-april-2025> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Daniel Wibberg (CAU / ELIXIR Germany), Nazeefa Fatima (ELIXIR-NO), Jill Jaworski (ELIXIR-SE), Patricia Palagi (ELIXIR-CH)\r
\r
Date:\r
15 April - 14:00-15:00\r
\r
Location:\r
Online\r
\r
Contents:\r
The main objective of this new course format - Training Clinic - is to provide participants with new knowledge and skills in the field of training in order to conduct training courses more effectively and create better training material. We invite trainers and scientists interested in training to take part! The content of the training clinic is specifically designed for current and aspiring trainers seeking to enhance their expertise and effectiveness in their field.\r
\r
The session also grants the possibility to exchange experiences between trainers and help connecting trainers. The course will be divided into different modules to facilitate the learning process. It will include a combination of lectures, practical exercises and case studies. This provides participants with both theoretical knowledge and practical experience. However, the focus should be on the exchange of problem-solving treatments. \r
\r
In the fifth edition, we will delve into "Handling Difficult Situations in Training Courses." Discover effective strategies and proven techniques to navigate and manage challenges that arise during training sessions. Whether you're an instructor facing unexpected obstacles or a participant aiming to contribute positively, mastering these skills can greatly enhance the overall training experience. Don't miss this opportunity to learn how to maintain a constructive and supportive environment, ensuring a smooth and successful learning journey for everyone involved!\r
\r
Learning goals:\r
- Improving training / teaching skills\r
- Trainer Networking\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
Interest in Training\r
\r
Keywords:\r
Training Clinic""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "online" ;
            schema1:endDate "2025-04-15 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:location [ a schema1:Place ;
                    schema1:address [ a schema1:PostalAddress ;
                            schema1:addressCountry "Germany" ;
                            schema1:addressLocality "Online" ] ;
                    schema1:latitude "50.56912" ;
                    schema1:longitude "10.449144" ] ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "de.NBI / ELIXIR-DE" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2025-04-15 14:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:name "Training Clinic - April 2025" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "de.NBI" ;
            schema1:url <https://www.denbi.de> ],
        [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "ELIXIR Germany" ;
            schema1:url <file:///home/runner/work/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://www.denbi.de/training-courses-2025/1874-training-clinic-april-2025> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/training-clinic-july-2025> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Educators:\r
Daniel Wibberg (CAU / ELIXIR Germany), Nazeefa Fatima (ELIXIR-NO), Jill Jaworski (ELIXIR-SE), Patricia Palagi (ELIXIR-CH)\r
\r
Date:\r
3 July - 13:00-14:00\r
\r
Location:\r
Online\r
\r
Contents:\r
The main objective of this new course format - Training Clinic - is to provide participants with new knowledge and skills in the field of training in order to conduct training courses more effectively and create better training material. We invite trainers and scientists interested in training to take part! The content of the training clinic is specifically designed for current and aspiring trainers seeking to enhance their expertise and effectiveness in their field.\r
The session also grants the possibility to exchange experiences between trainers and help connecting trainers. The course will be divided into different modules to facilitate the learning process. It will include a combination of lectures, practical exercises and case studies. This provides participants with both theoretical knowledge and practical experience. However, the focus should be on the exchange of problem-solving treatments. \r
Join us for the next Training Clinic, where we will explore the theme of E-Learning and Challenges. In the sixth edition, we will examine the unique difficulties that can arise in using learning management systems and provide you with effective strategies to address them. Whether you are an instructor managing technical issues or a participant seeking to enhance your experience, this session will equip you with the skills necessary to transform challenges into opportunities. Discover how to foster engagement, maintain motivation, and create a supportive atmosphere in learning management systems. Don’t miss this chance to enhance your e-learning expertise and contribute to a more effective and enriching online training experience for all!\r
\r
Learning goals: \r
- Improving training / teaching skills \r
- Trainer Networking\r
\r
Prerequisites: \r
Interest in Training\r
\r
Keywords: \r
Training Clinic """ ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
