<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/translational-immunology> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0804>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3342> ;
    schema1:alternateName "A VIB Science conference" ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Industry" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "PhD Students" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Physicians" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Academics" ] ;
    schema1:contact "conferences@vib.be" ;
    schema1:description """The organizing committee is looking forward to organize the postponed edition of this event on 22 - 23 November 2021 in Ghent, Belgium.\r
\r
The aim of this conference is to bridge the translational gap in immunopathology, bringing together clinicians, research scientists and industry partners to discuss prominent advances from the bench to the clinic.\r
\r
Internationally renowned speakers will present their latest findings during 5 plenary sessions:\r
\r
Making the most of your antibodies\r
T Cell activation and exhaustion\r
Bugs and drugs in immunology\r
From drug to market\r
Tissue immunity\r
Information for poster submissions\r
\r
The format for your poster should be: A0 (841 x 1189 mm / 33.1 x 46.8 in), portrait orientation. The best three abstracts were given a short talk slot in the plenary program. The 2 best posters will win the Poster prize sponsored by Elsevier's journal "Cellular Immunology"!\r
\r
Travel grants\r
\r
We offer 5 travel grants to international attendees, which will reimburse travel costs up to 400 Euros. Are you interested in attending Translational Immunology and want to have a chance on a travel grant? Submit your motivation below by clicking on the 'Apply for a grant' button before 30 August 2021. The organizing committee will notify you of your travel grant acceptance by the end of March.""" ;
    schema1:eligibility "first_come_first_served" ;
    schema1:endDate "2021-11-23 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
