<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/translational-immunology-fe17b83a-fab1-413f-94c3-9c6a1ecac893> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0804>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_2830>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3656> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "PhD students" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "PhD" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "industry" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Academics" ] ;
    schema1:description """Translational Immunology\r
\r
8-9 DECEMBER 2020, GHENT, BELGIUM\r
\r
Due to the Coronavirus, Translational Immunology and the satellite BIS meeting were postponed from 26-27 March 2020 to the end of the year. We are happy to confirm the new date: 8-9 December 2020.\r
\r
The aim of this conference is to bridge the translational gap in immunopathology, bringing together clinicians, research scientists and industry partners to discuss prominent advances from the bench to the clinic. The different sessions will have a particular focus on precision medicine in general, starting from disease-oriented cases and lessons learned. Innovative and alternative therapeutic strategies in immune-mediated disorders will be presented, besides the regulatory challenges that companies and researchers are dealing with.\r
\r
Deadlines:\r
-	Abstract submission: 5 October 2020\r
-	Early Bird deadline: 27 October 2020\r
-	Late Registration deadline: 24 November 2020\r
\r
Speakers:\r
Rosa Bacchetta	Stanford Medicine, US\r
Dirk Elewaut	VIB-UGent Center for Inflammation Research, BE\r
Alain Fischer	Assistance publique – Hôpitaux de Paris, FR\r
Martin Guilliams	VIB-UGent Center for Inflammation Research, BE\r
Pleun Hombrink	Sanquin, NL\r
Bengt Hoepken	Clinical Program Director, UCB Pharma, DE\r
Isabelle Huys	KU Leuven, BE\r
Christophe Lahorte	National Innovation Office &amp; Scientific-Technical Advice Unit - (Famhp), BE\r
Bart Lambrecht	VIB-UGent Center for Inflammation Research, BE\r
Antonio Lanzavecchia	Institute for Research in Biomedicine, CH\r
Sophie Lucas	de Duve Institute, UCLouvain, BE\r
Bénédicte Machiels	FARAH Center, ULiège, BE\r
Melanie Matheu	CEO, Founder at Prellis Biologics, Inc., US\r
Massimiliano Mazzone	VIB-KU Leuven Center for Cancer Biology, BE\r
Kathy McCoy 	University of Calgary, CA\r
Eoin McKinney	University of Cambridge, UK\r
Fiona Powrie	Kennedy Institute of Rheumatology, University of Oxford, UK\r
Federica Sallusto 	Institute for Research in Biomedicine, CH\r
Georg Schett	Friedrich-Alexander University Erlangen-Nürnberg, DE\r
Marvin van Luijn	Erasmus MC, University Medical Center Rotterdam MS Center ErasMS, NL\r
\r
\r
Location: De Bijloke, Jozef Kluyskensstraat 2, 9000 Gent\r
\r
Hashtag: #TransImmu20\r
""" ;
