<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/uniprot-for-proteomics-scientists-3015ec41-3b3e-459a-82e2-cb6d9f476bab> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/data_2976>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_0078>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_0121> ;
    schema1:description """[UniProt](https://www.uniprot.org/) is a comprehensive, expert-led, publicly available database of protein sequence, function, and variation information.

This webinar will give a brief introduction to the UniProt website and then highlight resources available that proteomics scientists or users with large protein datasets may find useful in analysing their data. This will encompass our proteomes service, how to convert and retrieve ID mappings, how to carry out a peptide search and how to visualise new large scale proteomics-derived PTM data.

The webinar will then go on to introduce the UniProt Proteins API which allows researchers to access and download UniProt data alongside large-scale genomic, proteomics and variation data without needing prior in-depth knowledge of programmatic languages. Data is available for download and querying in a range of formats, including XML, FASTA, and PEFF. The API multi-query search functions will be demonstrated and useful features such as searching the database by peptide, finding proteomic evidence of post translational modifications and accessing a protein entry to find its peptides will be explained.

The UniProt Proteins API is available at [//www.ebi.ac.uk/proteins/api/doc](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/proteins/api/doc)""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "online" ;
            schema1:endDate "2024-02-29 17:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
            schema1:maximumAttendeeCapacity 1000 ;
            schema1:organizer [ a schema1:Organization ;
                    schema1:name "European Bioinformatics Institute (EBI)" ] ;
            schema1:startDate "2024-02-29 09:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ] ;
    schema1:keywords "Proteins (proteins)",
        "UniProt: The Universal Protein Resource" ;
    schema1:name "UniProt for proteomics scientists" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "EMBL-EBI" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/training> ],
        [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "European Bioinformatics Institute (EBI)" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.ebi.ac.uk> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/training/events/uniprot-proteomics-scientists-2024> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/uniprot-for-proteomics-scientists-afd081aa-f2dd-40a6-8ec6-c1d0a721029a> a schema1:Event ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Event/0.2-DRAFT-2019_06_14> ;
    schema1:contact "Anna Swan - webinars@ebi.ac.uk" ;
    schema1:description """UniProt is a comprehensive, expert-led, publicly available database of protein sequence, function and variation information.

This webinar will give a brief introduction to the new UniProt website and then highlight resources available that proteomics scientists or users with large protein datasets may find useful in analysing their data. This will encompass our proteomes service, how to convert and retrieve ID mappings, and how to carry out a peptide search.

The webinar will then go on to introduce the UniProt Proteins API which allows researchers to access and download UniProt data alongside large-scale genomic, proteomics and variation data without needing prior in-depth knowledge of programmatic languages. Data is available for download and querying in a range of formats; including XML, FASTA and PEFF. The API multi-query search functions will be demonstrated and useful features such as searching entries by peptide, and the new functionality of searching for proteomic peptides and modifications will be explained.

The UniProt Proteins API is available at [//www.ebi.ac.uk/proteins/api/doc](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/proteins/api/doc)

 

""" ;
    schema1:endDate "2022-04-07 16:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:hostInstitution "EMBL-EBI" ;
    schema1:keywords "Proteins (proteins)",
        "UniProt: The Universal Protein Resource (173807)" ;
    schema1:maximumAttendeeCapacity 1000 ;
    schema1:name "UniProt for proteomics scientists" ;
    schema1:startDate "2022-04-07 15:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:url <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/training/events/uniprot-proteomics-scientists> .

