<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/using-large-language-models-locally> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description "Although most of us use Large Language Models via a web interface, this is not always the ideal scenario. GDPR or intellectual property considerations may prohibit exposing data or even queries to providers of such services. A model may have to be fine-tuned to increase the quality for certain applications. In such circumstances, you may want to deploy an LLM locally, and this training will show you how to do that and give some illustrations of applications you can implement." ;
