<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/webinar-making-sense-of-gene-and-protein-lists-with-functional-enrichment-analysis> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0078>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_0091>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3053> ;
    schema1:coursePrerequisites "None" ;
    schema1:description """Do you have a long list of genes or proteins from omics experiments that you don’t know what to do with? This webinar explains how functional enrichment analysis can be used to understand what these lists mean by employing gene ontology and pathway information to highlight the underlying biology. We’ll discuss the statistics that underpin enrichment analysis methods and some of the most commonly used tools, databases and workflows.\r
\r
Want to get hands-on with functional enrichment analysis? [Come to our workshop on 20 and 21 November](https://www.biocommons.org.au/events/funct-enrich-workshop).\r
Speakers: \r
*Dr Hossein Valipour Kahrood, Bioinformatician, Monash Genomics and Bioinformatics Platform\r
*Dr Cali Willet, Senior Research Bioinformatician, Sydney Informatics Hub, The University of Sydney\r
\r
Date/Time:\r
23 October 2024, 1 - 2 pm AEDT / 12 - 1 pm AEST / 12:30 - 1:30 pm ACDT/ 10 - 11 am AWST (check in your timezone)\r
\r
Who the webinar is for:\r
This webinar is for Australian researchers and bioinformaticians who have gene or protein lists from omics experiments (e.g. RNA-Seq, protein expression). \r
\r
How to join:\r
This webinar is free to join but you must register for a place in advance.\r
\r
[Register here](https://unimelb.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_2qVOM6tZQz6_-MeU5ZH0Mw)""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
