<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/webinar-what-exactly-is-bioinformatics> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0091> ;
    schema1:coursePrerequisites "None" ;
    schema1:description """‘Doing’ bioinformatics to extract, process, analyse, and interpret experimental results is something that all life scientists do as part of their research. But what _exactly_ is bioinformatics? And is there a right (or a wrong) way to do it?\r
\r
In this webinar, Dr Georgie Samaha welcomes you to the vast world of bioinformatics. Georgie will illuminate key concepts including:\r
-What does a typical experiment look like?\r
-What kind of data will I work with?\r
-What is involved in data-preprocessing?\r
-What’s involved in data analysis?\r
-Where can I do bioinformatics? \r
\r
We explore common experimental use cases and share essential - but easy to overlook - practical tips for accessing data, software, and computing resources you need to get your research done.\r
\r
**Speaker:**\r
Dr Georgie Samaha - Product Owner of the Australian BioCommons BioCLI Project and Bioinformatics Group Lead at the Sydney Informatics Hub, The University of Sydney. \r
\r
**Date/Time:** 07 August 2024, 12 - 1pm AEST / 11:30 am - 12:30 pm ACST / 10 - 11 am AWST\r
\r
**Who the webinar is for:**\r
This webinar is for life scientists who are looking to get started or build their skills in bioinformatics.\r
\r
**How to join:**\r
This webinar is free to join but you must register for a place in advance.\r
\r
**[Register here](https://unimelb.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_kcYL2MaTTJ6r-yt3cwbePg)**""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
