<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/workshop-on-computational-pangenomics> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Educators: \r
Jens Stoye, Andreas Rempel, Luca Parmigiani, Tizian Schulz, Roland Wittler, Kassian Kobert (BiGi)\r
\r
Date: \r
20+21.09.2023, 10:00 – 15:00\r
\r
Location: \r
Online\r
\r
Contents: \r
The focus of the Workshop on Computational Pangenomics is to give participants an overview and understanding of commonly used pangenomics tools.\r
\r
Besides an introduction into the motivation and theory behind questions from the field of pangenomics, we will look at specific tools (such as panacus, Corer, PLAST, and SANS) and let the participants explore their usage in hands-on sessions.\r
\r
The workshop will be held online. For the hands-on sessions, virtual machines with the needed software will be provided. Interested participants should have a basic understanding of Linux operating systems to participate in hands-on sessions of the workshop.\r
\r
Learning goals:\r
\r
Introduction to Pangenomics\r
Usage of pangenomics tools\r
Prerequisites:\r
Basic Linux command line usage\r
\r
Keywords:\r
Pangenomics, panacus, Corer, PLAST, SANS\r
\r
Tools:\r
panacus, Corer, PLAST, SANS""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
