<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/workshop-practical-tools-for-managing-moving-and-analysing-data> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Biologists" ] ;
    schema1:description """Are you constantly moving, storing, sharing and analysing data in complex scenarios throughout your research projects?\r
\r
Managing data well is now more important than ever for biological research but it can also be frustrating and difficult to know where to start!\r
\r
This hands-on workshop will explore and discuss data management challenges and introduce simple steps towards managing active research data. Participants will become familiar with CloudStor and its associated tools and services for organising, storing, sharing and analysing data, in a safe and secure way.\r
\r
Topics such as cloud storage, collaborative editing, versioning and data sharing will be discussed and demonstrated. You will learn how to set up an automatic way to move your data to the cloud so that your data is safe and secure. We’ll also show you how CloudStor integrates with data analysis solutions including Juypter Notebooks and Galaxy.\r
\r
This is a hands-on workshop using CloudStor (AARNet’s file sync, share and storage service). CloudStor is available to Australian researchers and provides one terabyte of storage to every individual researcher at AARNet-connected institutions. \r
\r
Trainer: This event will be led by Sara King, AARNet, and hosted by Australian BioCommons.\r
\r
Learning objectives:\r
\r
By the end of this workshop you should be able to:\r
\r
Identify common data management challenges\r
\r
Use CloudStor tools to store, move and manage data\r
\r
Describe methods for integrating CloudStor storage solutions with data analysis\r
\r
Who the workshop is for\r
\r
This hands-on workshop is tailored for biologists and requires no programming experience. \r
\r
Date/Time: 4 December 1:00pm -  4:00pm AEDT\r
\r
How to join\r
\r
The workshop is free but places are strictly limited to Australian life science researchers and students and registration requires an Australian institutional email address. \r
\r
Participation in this workshop requires access to a CloudStor account. You can check if you have access via your institutional subscription by finding your institution’s name on the CloudStor log-in list. If you do not have CloudStor access via your institution, you can still attend, but please advise us in advance so that arrangements can be made.""" ;
    schema1:hasCourseInstance [ a schema1:CourseInstance ;
            dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/CourseInstance/1.0-RELEASE> ;
            schema1:courseMode "onsite" ;
            schema1:endDate "2020-12-04 16:00:00 UTC"^^schema1:Date ;
