    schema1:description """## Abstract

Data access including levels of access are described.  Learners will be able to illustrate data access in terms of the FAIR Principles using companion terms including communications protocol and authentication.  Learners will also be able to interpret the data usage licence associated with different data sets


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - What is data access in the context of FAIR
 - What are the different types of data access?
 - What is a data usage licence?
 - How can you share sensitive data?


## Learning Objectives

- To illustrate data access in terms of the FAIR Principles using companion terms including communications protocol and authentication.
- To interpret the data usage licence associated with different data sets.""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "FAIR Data, Workflows, and Research",
        "data stewardship",
        "dmp",
        "fair" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "Access" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- To illustrate data access in terms of the FAIR Principles using companion terms including communications protocol and authentication.
- To interpret the data usage licence associated with different data sets.""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/fair/tutorials/fair-access/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "2" .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/access-bioinformatics-databases-with-biopython> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """In this 1-hour long project-based course, you will learn how to access, parse, and visualize data from various bioinformatics sequence and structural online databases such as ENTREZ, PDB, KEGG and NCBI using Biopython.
You will also interact with various bioinformatics file formats such as FASTA, PDB, GENBANK and XML along with various parsers to read and modify these files using Biopython.

Note: This course works best for learners who are based in the North America region. We’re currently working on providing the same experience in other regions.""" ;
    schema1:keywords "data-analysis",
        "data-science",
        "health-informatics",
        "life-sciences" ;
    schema1:license <file:///home/runner/work/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/notspecified> ;
    schema1:name "Access Bioinformatics Databases with Biopython" ;
