    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2024-11-06"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2024-03-06"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

Galaxy offers thousands of tools. Many of these tools either have incomplete metadata or are not yet linked to sources of high-quality metadata such as [bio.tools](https://bio.tools/).


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How are Galaxy tools linked to EDAM ontology?
 - How to connect Galaxy tools to bio.tools?
 - What is bio.tools?
 - How to add, and update, entries in bio.tools?


## Learning Objectives

- Identify Galaxy tools without bio.tools entry
- Create a bio.tools entry
- Update a bio.tools entry
- Add EDAM ontology terms to a bio.tools entry
- Link a Galaxy tool to its corresponding bio.tools entry""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Development in Galaxy" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "Adding and updating best practice metadata for Galaxy tools using the bio.tools registry" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Identify Galaxy tools without bio.tools entry
- Create a bio.tools entry
- Update a bio.tools entry
- Add EDAM ontology terms to a bio.tools entry
- Link a Galaxy tool to its corresponding bio.tools entry""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/dev/tutorials/tool-annotation/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "5" .

