<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/advanced-analysis-of-quantitative-proteomics-data-using-r> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "active" ;
    schema1:description """In this course you will learn about using R for the analysis of proteomics data. We will focus on data preprocessing methods and advanced methods for data analysis. In this regard the course will touch upon:\r
    • data normalization\r
    • quality control, handling of missing values\r
    • clustering, heatmaps\r
    • ROC-curves\r
\r
Learning goals:\r
    • Independent usage of R functions for\r
        - Data preprocessing\r
        - Plots and graphs\r
        - Statistical methods for data analysis\r
        - Use of additional R packages\r
    • Deeper understanding of statistical methods applied in differential analyses\r
\r
Prerequisites:\r
    • Basic understanding of high-dimensional data sets from quantitative proteomics or other life sciences;\r
    • Basic knowledge of R (e.g. data import, basic plots, t-test, for loop) and basic knowledge of differential analysis of proteomics data. Both can for example be gained from our e-Learning course “Differential analysis of quantitative proteomics data”.\r
\r
Download Training material here:\r
https://www.denbi.de/images/Training/eLearning/Material_Advanced_Rcourse.zip\r
\r
Download and more information on R here:\r
https://cran.r-project.org/\r
\r
We recommend using an editor such as RStudio, see\r
https://www.rstudio.com""" ;
    schema1:license <file:///home/runner/work/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/notspecified> ;
    schema1:name "Advanced analysis of quantitative proteomics data using R" ;
