    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2025-05-10"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2024-03-24"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

The ocean is a key component of the Earth's climate system. It thus needs continuous real-time monitoring to help scientists better understand its dynamics and predict its evolution.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to use the Pangeo ecosystem to analyse ocean data?
 - How to process Argo data to visualise ocean temperature variations?


## Learning Objectives

- How to fetch Argo Data?
- How to get metadata with xarray netcdf tools?
- Learn to get temperature variations.
- Learn to use an interactive tool to visualise Argo temperature variable on an interactive map.""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Climate",
        "argo",
        "earth-system",
        "ocean",
        "pangeo" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/climate/tutorials/argo_pangeo/workflows/> ] ;
    schema1:name "Analyse Argo data" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- How to fetch Argo Data?
- How to get metadata with xarray netcdf tools?
- Learn to get temperature variations.
- Learn to use an interactive tool to visualise Argo temperature variable on an interactive map.""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/climate/tutorials/argo_pangeo/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "2" .

