    schema1:description """## Abstract

**asynchronous training events**, i.e. MOOC style courses pair pre-recorded and written lesson materials with online participants following along at their own pace and convenience.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - What is asynchronous training?
 - How to deliver asynchronous training using Galaxy?
 - What should be prepared for an asynchronous training event?
 - How is it different than hybrid training?


## Learning Objectives

- Describe asynchronous training
- Organize an asynchronous training event using Galaxy""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Teaching and Hosting Galaxy training" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "Asynchronous training" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Describe asynchronous training
- Organize an asynchronous training event using Galaxy""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/teaching/tutorials/gallantries-async/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "1" .

