<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/basic-statistical-tests> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Helen Brown" ] ;
    schema1:description """1. Introduction\r
\r
2. Hypothesis Testing\r
\r
3. Choosing Between Parametric &amp; Non-Parametric Tests\r
\r
4. T-Test for Comparing Two Groups\r
\r
5. T-Test – Interpreting Software Output\r
\r
6. Paired T-Test\r
\r
7. Mann-Whitney U-Test to Compare Two Groups When Data Are Not Normally Distributed\r
\r
8. Log-Rank Test for Analysing ‘Time to Event’ Data\r
\r
9. Methods to Compare Three or More Groups\r
\r
10. Analysis of Variance (ANOVA)\r
\r
11. Kruskall-Wallis Test for Non-Normal Data\r
\r
12. Hypothesis Testing – Points to Remember\r
\r
13. Reporting Results &amp; Format for P-Values\r
\r
14. Practical Exercise Roundup\r
\r
15. Tests for Binary &amp; Categorical Data – Introduction\r
\r
16. Chi-Square Test &amp; Fisher’s Exact Test - Binary Data\r
\r
17. Chi-Square Test &amp; Fisher’s Exact Test for Unordered Categorical Data\r
\r
18. Tests for Ordinal Categorical Data\r
\r
19. Correlation Analysis\r
\r
20. Regression Analysis\r
\r
21. Spearman Rank Correlation Analysis for Non-Normal Data\r
\r
22. Introduction to Multiple Regression &amp; Logistic Regression\r
\r
23. Summary of Tests\r
\r
24. Going Beyond Simple Comparisons\r
\r
25. Statistical Packages""" ;
