<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/checking-expected-species-and-contamination-in-bacterial-isolate> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0610>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_0622>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3301>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3673>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3697> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Students" ] ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Bérénice Batut" ] ;
    schema1:competencyRequired "Introduction to Galaxy Analyses" ;
    schema1:contributor [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Saskia Hiltemann" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Clea Siguret" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Helena Rasche" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2024-06-27"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2024-03-04"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

Sequencing (determining of DNA/RNA nucleotide sequence) is used all over the world for all kinds of analysis. The product of these sequencers are reads, which are sequences of detected nucleotides. 


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - What are the species in bacterial isolate sequencing data?


## Learning Objectives

- Run a series of tool to identify species in bacterial isolate sequencing data
- Visualize the species abundance""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Ecology",
        "bacteria",
        "illumina",
        "microgalaxy" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "kraken2" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/kraken2> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/ecology/tutorials/bacterial-isolate-species-contamination-checking/workflows/> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/record/10572227> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Recentrifuge" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/Recentrifuge> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Bracken" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/bracken> ] ;
    schema1:name "Checking expected species and contamination in bacterial isolate" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Run a series of tool to identify species in bacterial isolate sequencing data
- Visualize the species abundance""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/ecology/tutorials/bacterial-isolate-species-contamination-checking/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "4" .

