    schema1:datePublished "2024-02-06"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

This tutorial can be followed with any user-defined database but would work best if the clinical metaproteomics database generation module was used (see [Database Generation tutorial](https://github.com/subinamehta/training-material/blob/main/topics/proteomics/tutorials/clinical-mp-database-generation/tutorial.md)). The MetaNovo tool generates a more manageable database that contains identified proteins. The MetaNovo-generated database merged with Human SwissProt (reviewed only) and contaminants (cRAP) databases to generate a compact database (~21.2k protein sequences) that will be used for peptide identification.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to perform database searching?
 - How to extract microbial and Human protein and peptide sequences from the results


## Learning Objectives

- Perform Database searching using two algorithms
- Extract confident peptides and proteins
- Generate a microbial peptide panel for verification""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Proteomics",
        "label-TMT11" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10105821> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/proteomics/tutorials/clinical-mp-2-discovery/workflows/> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "msConvert" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/msconvert> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "MaxQuant" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/maxquant> ] ;
    schema1:name "Clinical Metaproteomics 2: Discovery" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Perform Database searching using two algorithms
- Extract confident peptides and proteins
- Generate a microbial peptide panel for verification""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/proteomics/tutorials/clinical-mp-2-discovery/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "5" .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/clinical-mp-3-verification> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0121> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
