    schema1:datePublished "2018-06-12"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

Most of the GTN content is written in [GitHub Flavored Markdown](https://guides.github.com/features/mastering-markdown/) with some metadata (or variables) found in [YAML](http://yaml.org/) files. Everything is stored on a [GitHub](https://github.com) repository: [https://example.com](https://example.com).


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How can I contribute to an open-source project with GitHub?
 - What is the GitHub flow?


## Learning Objectives

- Fork a repository on GitHub
- Clone a remote repository locally
- Create a branch
- Commit changes
- Push changes to a remote repository
- Create a pull request
- Update a pull request""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Contributing to the Galaxy Training Material" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "Contributing to the Galaxy Training Network with GitHub" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Fork a repository on GitHub
- Clone a remote repository locally
- Create a branch
- Commit changes
- Push changes to a remote repository
- Create a pull request
- Update a pull request""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/contributing/tutorials/github-contribution/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "2" .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/contributing-to-the-uniprot-knowledgebase-how-you-can-help> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0121>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3068> ;
    schema1:description """This webinar will present how the research community can contribute both literature references and annotation to the UniProt database of protein sequence and function (www.uniprot.org).\r
\r
First, we will provide an overview of the resource and then we will focus on describing the functionality to add publications and knowledge to protein entries, including a demo.\r
\r
In this webinar you will also learn how your domain knowledge contribution improves the resource for the general community, and how it can be used as an alternative metric of your research output given that UniProt uses ORCID, a unique identifier for each researcher, as a mechanism for user validation and credit for these contributions.  """ ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "Recorded webinar" ;
    schema1:license <file:///home/runner/work/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/notspecified> ;
    schema1:name "Contributing to the UniProt Knowledgebase: how you can help" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "European Bioinformatics Institute (EBI)" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.ebi.ac.uk> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/training/events/contributing-uniprot-knowledgebase-how-you-can-help-2021> .

