    schema1:description """## Abstract

Sometimes we want to share our workflows outside of Galaxy, like printing it on a poster.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How can I print or screenshot my Workflow in high resolution for a poster or presentation?
 - How can I share high detail images of my Workflows?


## Learning Objectives

- Create a high resolution image of your Workflow, ready for a poster
- Learn how to utilize external tools to make high resolution images of your Workflow
- Learn how to compress high resolution Workflow images to share them in the web""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Using Galaxy and Managing your Data",
        "workflows" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ] ;
    schema1:name "Creating high resolution images of Galaxy Workflows" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Create a high resolution image of your Workflow, ready for a poster
- Learn how to utilize external tools to make high resolution images of your Workflow
- Learn how to compress high resolution Workflow images to share them in the web""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/galaxy-interface/tutorials/workflow-posters/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "3" .

