<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/data-management-plans-for-beginners> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Duration: 2 days a 3 hours\r
\r
In this highly interactive workshop we begin with a short introduction of the research data life cycle and the FAIR data principles. Subsequently, we explore in multiple hands-on sessions what a data management plan (DMP) is. We will sink our teeth into components, language, and examples of DMPs. In light of the FAIR principles, we will evaluate possible problems and solutions and self-assess a drafted DMP for our own projects.\r
\r
Learning Goals:\r
\r
- Know the research life cycle\r
- Know the FAIR principles and understand their importance\r
- Know the expectations for a DMP\r
- Be able to sketch a DMP\r
\r
Prerequisites: none\r
\r
https://zenodo.org/record/5575921#.YW_7nS-21QI""" ;
