<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/ecology-workshop-overview> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """There are no pre-requisites, and the materials assume no prior knowledge about the tools. The data for this workshop are is the Portal Project Teaching Database available on FigShare, with a CC-BY license available for reuse. The Portal Project Teaching Database is a simplified version of the Portal 
Project Database designed for teaching. It is a tabular dataset of observations
of small mammals in a desert ecosystem in Arizona, USA, collected over more than 40 years.
It provides a real world example of 
life-history, population, and ecological data, with sufficient complexity to 
teach many aspects of data analysis and management, but with many complexities
removed to allow students to focus on the core ideas and skills being taught. More information on this dataset The workshop can be taught using R or Python as the base language.""" ;
    schema1:license <file:///home/runner/work/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/notspecified> ;
    schema1:name "Ecology Workshop Overview" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "Data Carpentry" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.datacarpentry.org> ] ;
    schema1:url <http://datacarpentry.github.io/ecology-workshop/> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/ecoregionalization-workflow-tutorial> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0610> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Students" ] ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Pauline Seguineau" ] ;
    schema1:competencyRequired "Introduction to Galaxy Analyses" ;
    schema1:contributor [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Coline Royaux" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Helena Rasche" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Saskia Hiltemann" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Yvan Le Bras" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Ankerl Yassine" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Björn Grüning" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Marie Josse" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2025-06-03"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2024-09-16"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

This tutorial is designed to guide you through the Ecoregionalization Galaxy workflow, demonstrating how to create an ecoregionalization map from occurrences and environmental data using a boosted regression trees model for predictions.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to use the ecoregionalization workflow?
 - How to construct ecoregions from occurrences species data and environmental data?


## Learning Objectives

- Learning how to use the ecoregionalization workflow.
- Learning about boosted regression trees algorithm.
- Learning about Silhouette index and select an appropriate number of cluster
- Learning about Clara clustering algorithm (PAM for large datasets)
- Create an ecoregionalization map""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "EBV workflow",
        "Ecology",
        "biodiversity",
        "earth-system",
        "ecology",
        "gbif",
        "interactive-tools",
        "modeling",
        "ocean",
        "taxonomic data" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/ecology/tutorials/Ecoregionalization_tutorial/workflows/> ] ;
    schema1:name "Ecoregionalization workflow tutorial" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Learning how to use the ecoregionalization workflow.
- Learning about boosted regression trees algorithm.
- Learning about Silhouette index and select an appropriate number of cluster
- Learning about Clara clustering algorithm (PAM for large datasets)
- Create an ecoregionalization map""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/ecology/tutorials/Ecoregionalization_tutorial/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "7" .

