<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/elitma-module-data-management-strategy-finland-28-29-june-2023> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "data steward / data manager" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Node Coordinators" ] ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Mijke Jetten" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Celia van Gelder" ] ;
    schema1:contributor [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Ivan Mičetić" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Danielle Welter" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Vassilios Ioannidis" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Joeri van der Velde" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Riku Riski" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Pinar Alper" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Niclas Jareborg" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Diana Pilvar" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Korbinian Bösl" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Nazeefa Fatima" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Fabio Liberante" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Margreet Bloemers" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Allyson Lister" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Anna Strachotova" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Hervé Ménager" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "active" ;
    schema1:dateCreated "2023-06-29"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2024-03-29"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """ELITMa is a ELIXIR training program in Management, developed for Node Coordinators by ELIXIR-CONVERGE WP6 and WP2 in collaboration. ELITMa is directed to ELIXIR middle management people, namely, the already mentioned Node Coordinators, who could benefit from the complete program. In addition it is also designed for people involved in training, computing, data or bioinformatics services, who  are interested in selected modules, according to their needs and previous background.\r
\r
#Program summary M2 Data management strategy \r
\r
This module aims to guide Node Coordinators and Node Data Managers (f.i. ELIXIR-CONVERGE WP1 member) in strengthening data management in their Node. Its focus are best practices from the ELIXIR portfolio of data management tools and services. After this module, trainees should be able to navigate the ELIXIR data management portfolio and plan for consolidation of the relevant tools and services in their Nodes, aimed at strengthening data management life science research for and by the Nodes’ data stewards and researchers. The module aims to inspire Node Coordinators and Node Data Managers, providing them with new ideas to optimise (if applicable: create) their Nodes' DM strategy in the context of the ELIXIR Programme.\r
\r
You can find more information in the documents\r
\r
#Event\r
\r
The training (two days) is part of a three-day event (27-29 June 2023), in Espoo, Finland. \r
\r
#Funding\r
\r
ELIXIR-CONVERGE has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 Research and Innovation programme under grant agreement No 871075""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:identifier "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.10895079" ;
    schema1:keywords "RDM",
        "Research Data Management",
        "Strategy",
        "Training" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "Training materials" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "ELITMa Module \"Data Management Strategy\" (Finland 28-29 June 2023)" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "ELIXIR Netherlands" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.dtls.nl/courses/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches "This module aims to guide Node Coordinators and Node Data Managers (f.i. ELIXIR-CONVERGE WP1 member) in strengthening data management in their Node. Its focus are best practices from the ELIXIR portfolio of data management tools and services. After this module, trainees should be able to navigate the ELIXIR data management portfolio and plan for consolidation of the relevant tools and services in their Nodes, aimed at strengthening data management life science research for and by the Nodes’ data stewards and researchers. The module aims to inspire Node Coordinators and Node Data Managers, providing them with new ideas to optimise (if applicable: create) their Nodes' DM strategy in the context of the ELIXIR Programme." ;
    schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.10895079> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/elixir-aai-engagement-meetings-materials> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3316> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "software developers, bioinformaticians" ] ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Kristyna Kvizdova" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Miska Husgafvel" ] ;
    schema1:description """ELIXIR AAI which evolved into LS AAI (Login) is a service that other services can use to authenticate their users and manage their access rights. \r
In the **ELIXIR AAI Work Package**, we are preparing regular **Community engagement meetings** where we would like to share and discuss together new AAI needs, requirements and ideas collected from the community, as well as share success stories with other infrastructures. Topics will be selected based on needs and interest and also in regard to future migration to LS AAI.\r
Here you can find information about previous and future **Engagement Meetings' Agenda** and **links to presentation and documentation**.\r
\r
  * You can contact us on support@aai.lifescience-ri.eu\r
\r
###Engagement Call XII.  - 11.9.2025 - Meeting Closed\r
**Date: 11.9.2025** \r
**Description:**\r
The upcoming engagement call will be devoted to presenting the outcomes of the recent service providers’ survey carried out by the LS AAI team. In addition to the survey evaluation, the latter part of the event will feature an “Ask Us Anything” forum, offering participants the opportunity for direct dialogue with the LS AAI team.\r
**Links:**\r
[About Engagement Call XII.] (https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ww7iT_ID-DfpIjs6I87Z_gMsh0dkCsdzWZT99-RsatY/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[Engagement Call Recording] (https://youtu.be/cBHT5xmv9HE)\r
\r
###Engagement Call XI.  - 14.2.2025 -  Meeting Closed\r
**Date: 14.2.2025** \r
**Description:**\r
This call is open to all members of the Life Science community interested in the Life Science AAI roadmap for 2025, with a particular focus on updates and plans relevant to LS Service Providers.\r
In this engagement call we will present the LS AAI Roadmap for 2025, outlining the strategic direction and planned developments for the upcoming year. Key topics will include the enhancements of LS AAI and planned migrations.\r
**Links:**\r
[About Engagement Call XI.] (https://docs.google.com/document/d/1l2YWVIXIQF6NCU9oDAW6VJPHKj5npw4Lh4jWDYfJJq8/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[Engagement Call Recording] (https://youtu.be/kFozN30JWAo)\r
\r
###Engagement Call X.  - 7.10.2024 -  Meeting Closed\r
**Date: 7.10.2024** \r
**Description:**\r
This call is open to anybody from the community interested in ELIXIR’s work in AAI. This time, the topic is an overview of the federated de.NBI Cloud and its integration with LS AAI. de.NBI Cloud is one of the biggest infrastructures in LS AAI and its integration related use cases can be an inspiration for other communities and services. de.NBI Cloud is operated by The German Network for Bioinformatics Infrastructure. More information about de.NBI Cloud is available at https://www.denbi.de/cloud.\r
**Links:**\r
[About Engagement Call X.] (https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FKxCoI6eMS9g0uXTI0RowJeXxmTh847A8IOH4eZVwW4/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[de.NBI Cloud and its integration to LS AAI] (https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1hTsF7tsv9iJXhLv_o4Az38vUPaO2F83nwIgKl_zXnfM)\r
[Engagement Call Recording] (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tjLRITRX4Ho)\r
\r
###Engagement Call IX.  -  Meeting Closed\r
**Date: 28.6.2024** \r
**Description:**\r
This call is open to anybody from the community interested in ELIXIR’s work in AAI. This time, the topic is an overview of infrastructures other than ELIXIR, which are involved in the LS AAI and their utilization of the AAI.\r
**Links:**\r
[About Engagement Call IX.] (https://docs.google.com/document/d/1UA01aoa293Z_5-GrcdPEwrSOhxc2lumMrG2wh1BdK30/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[Infrastructures, projects, and communities utilizing the LS AAI] (https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1-7OOKtoWiKDLLedRwnW1v2KF3z_R81J9knvDOGjjWiI/edit#slide=id.p1)\r
Engagement Call Recording - due to the technical issues, the recording is not available\r
\r
###Engagement Call VIII. - Meeting Closed\r
**Date: 10.4.2024** \r
**Description:**\r
This call is open to anybody from the community interested in ELIXIR’s work in AAI, mainly focusing on the Work Plan of Work Package 2, which represents ELIXIR in the  Life Science AAI.\r
**Links:**\r
[About Engagement Call VIII.] (https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EcP6vdPCMDDpvU0qg4Rc2t2z3pbADn5VebPOZR9Bb2g/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[ELIXIR CP WP2 24-26 work programme] (https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1ZsBV1MVUX9XT-7omVOK6WnuYJhdUEl9G_l5I9kkBE-o/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[Engagement Call Recording] (https://youtu.be/sNefYEbr4ME)\r
\r
###Engagement Call VII. - Meeting Closed\r
**Date: 7.12.2022** \r
**Description:**\r
This call is open to anybody from the community who is interested in GA4GH standards and LS AAI/ELIXIR services what rely/want to rely on GA4GH Passports. We will give overview of **GA4GH in Life Science AAI** and also go through the new **specification of GA4GH v1.2**. There will be enough space also for discussion.\r
**Links:**\r
[About Engagement Call VII.] \r
(https://docs.google.com/document/d/139aOyx7JYWL14RQQ4LZR7lK0-vu2tjB5RH_h1G74M6k/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[GA4GH in LS AAI] (https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1wRWnAWy_Wxpz2XVmkYZmucqXQeFTDKfZdp5_X1jXsl4/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[GA4GH 1.2 specification overview] (https://ga4gh.github.io/data-security/1.2-draft-main/changes-1_2)\r
[Engagement Call Recording] (https://youtu.be/tYWdnlTayEI)\r
\r
\r
###Engagement Call VI. - Meeting Closed\r
**Date: 22.6.2022** \r
**Description:**\r
In this call we provide a short introduction to **Self-Sovereign Identity (SSI)**, a new paradigm for identity and access management. We then demonstrate a proof of concept for writing a researcher’s permissions to access a genomic dataset in their SSI wallet (in their smartphone) and then using it for accessing the datasets in a computing environment.\r
**Links:**\r
[About Engagement Call VI.] \r
(https://docs.google.com/document/d/12YJozEylVPGt34SdDMDXgZXYfsvirX6ZTvFaIJB3WRk/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[Self-Sovereign Identity Introduction slides + Demo]\r
(https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1V6WyoBnGU4BwmQmjBNKdCzsGyh4i3t9lG8MC5iQ-jLo/edit#slide=id.p1)\r
[Engagement Call Recording] (https://youtu.be/qvyLOdrDu7A)\r
\r
###Engagement Call V.  - Meeting Closed\r
**Date: 4.5.2022** \r
**Description:**\r
In this call the implementers of **GA4GH Cloud APIs in ELIXIR** describe how the Workflow Execution Service (WES) and Task Execution Service (TES) enables a researcher to “bring compute to data” and how WES and TES make use of GA4GH Passports and other features of ELIXIR/Life Science AAI.\r
**Links:**\r
[About Engagement Call V.]\r
(https://docs.google.com/document/d/14fQQZJx3OauYtPsqwE5f0m6GYX7hnDqpxhfhKf--6hw/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[ELIXIR Cloud and AAI Driver project]\r
(https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1sOg0gqfF0BheQ9UDYAEPNsV_L5tAXA9ioW1nyXRGd3A/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[Introduction to Passports in the GA4GH Cloud APIs]\r
(https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1bBYotSZGhtU3ud7vSrb5v-uJB37DQx7RwyAECdd3p7E/edit#slide=id.p1)\r
[Update on GA4GH Passports 1.2/2.0]\r
(https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1RhNvu_ensF7dXRUPqRVz3ijhtOtNoUbe961umn6NugI/edit?usp=sharing)\r
\r
###Engagement Call IV. - Meeting Closed\r
**Date: 30.3.2022**\r
**Description:**\r
In this call we would like to present to you the plan and steps of Elixir AAI users and services **migration to LS AAI**. Important part of the call will be discussion.\r
**Links:**\r
[About Engagement Call IV.](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nsMC5vhsOtxonXIjDcdogu_HKGRS-BUIb-LbAPDYqVA/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[Overview of LS AAI Migration]\r
(https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1q0ZE0UlFRjULbXduZs1ZD5kuXRWfPc-Lr8SggVsGWwc/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[Technical overview of LS AAI migration]\r
(https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1-6mJcYL3-QaOWWlK6DZsI1PrOO66a06DI1_o8XJKzsU/edit?usp=sharing)\r
\r
###Engagement Call III. - Meeting Closed\r
**Date: 23.2.2022**\r
**Description:**\r
In the third call, we will take a closer look at AAIs related to the ELIXIR AAI. The first topic would be primarily focused on the **EOSC AAI**. In this part, you will get an insight into what the integration of ELIXIR AAI would look like. The second topic will focus on the guidelines resulting from the AARC project. The final part of the call will be dedicated to advertizing the recent AAI features.\r
**Links:**\r
[About Engagement Call III.](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSIgd7ABzvhwQ13z9e6nS-KTUezu_O6z-O17IufR5pc/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[EOSC Future&amp;EOSC AAI]\r
(https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1e9uwz3ok-Grgqo30Q72zjQ418rIOCwZ-/edit?usp=sharing&amp;ouid=117313583900861114499&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true)\r
[ELIXIR AAI Features update]\r
(https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1VwJmwsdjlwtFs0qUaOjR8xmjAPhbdkZOuiGqGiuaO0A/edit?usp=sharing)\r
\r
###Engagement Call II. - Meeting Closed\r
**Date: 26.1.2022**\r
**Description:**\r
In the second call we will introduce more detailed use cases and follow up of discussion from the 1st engagement call **GA4GH**: ELIXIR community and EGA needs in relevance with proposed changes by NIH/dbGaP.\r
**Links:**\r
[About Engagement Call II.](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gOAdAfENgMtd0XBrD25OcVeR0ImFCu3vMVet8cE_rhc/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[CSC Sensitive Data Desktop]\r
(https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1DTJaEGw-MLsnnOSJ6HoPBBLT5xV8kmxK/edit#slide=id.p1)\r
[GA4GH/AAI update]\r
(https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1N3jLPxMn5JnybuCc0oESsVqBAyQKeaj3-4S0XO3RTOc/edit?usp=sharing)\r
\r
###Engagement Call I. - Meeting Closed\r
**Date: 15.12.2021**\r
**Description:**\r
In this engagement call, we will report about currently discussed future changes in the **GA4GH** AAI OpenID Connect Profile and GA4GH Passport specifications and discuss how they correspond to the needs of the ELIXIR.\r
**Links:**\r
[About Engagement Call I.](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KFt5Vp8CKIXpajmGCSF0WkMjhI8cCg8ljNrNbR_80OY/edit?usp=sharing)\r
[GA4GH passports and ELIXIR AAI](https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1OAbYhEE5hxcPbN7iAMjVntfZKHao4zmYN9Q7UGipClQ/edit?usp=sharing)""" ;
