<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/erknet-education-and-training> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3325> ;
    schema1:description """The European Reference Network for Rare Kidney Diseases (ERKNet), the European Society for Paediatric Nephrology (ESPN) and the International Pediatric Nephrology Association (IPNA) have since January 2020 launched a set of webinars. \r
\r
They take place monthly on Tuesdays 4 pm CET (except summer holidays) and are organized as follows:\r
\r
1. Educational Webinars on Pediatric Nephrology and Rare Kidney Diseases. \r
These webinars cover a full spectrum of pediatric nephrology and rare kidney diseases during three years and can be used in the future for preparing Board Examination in pediatric nephrology (ESPN) and performing the ERKNet Postgraduate Curriculum in Rare Kidney Diseases.\r
\r
2. ERKNet/WGiKD (Working Group on Inherited Kidney Disorders) Advanced Webinars on Rare Kidney Disorders.\r
These webinars will highlight clinical and scientific aspects of rare kidney disorders of pediatric and adult age.\r
\r
3. Best Clinical Practice Webinars\r
These webinars will highlight recently developed guidelines and clinical practice recommendations concerning clinical management of diverse pediatric kidney disorders. \r
\r
The webinars are broadcasted and offer an opportunity to ask questions online. \r
For those who cannot attend live webinars, there is a possibility to see the recorded webinars on the websites of ERKNet, ESPN and IPNA.""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "advanced" ;
    schema1:keywords "Rare Diseases & Research" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "Webinar",
        "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <file:///home/runner/work/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/notspecified> ;
    schema1:name "Postgraduate Curriculum in Rare Kidney Diseases developed by ERKNet" ;
    schema1:url <https://erknet.org/index.php?id=10> .

