    schema1:dateModified "2025-08-05"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2024-12-18"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

Using Galaxy via the SURF Research Cloud (SRC) allows researchers to start Galaxy instances on-demand and analyze their data in a secure environment following the General Data Protection Regulations (GDPR). The instance provides secure authentication, where users must have a SURF Research account prior to this tutorial, have set the SURF Research Access Management (SRAM) authentication method, and connect an SSH key to their accounts. In case you are not familiar with SRC and need help in setting up your accounts, please follow the instructions on the [SURF Knowledge Base](https://servicedesk.surf.nl/wiki/display/WIKI/SURF+Research+Cloud)


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How do I start a Galaxy instance on SURF Research Cloud?
 - How do I link to external storage from my Galaxy workspace?
 - How do I install tools?


## Learning Objectives

- Understand how to work with a Galaxy on-demand instance in SURF Research Cloud""" ;
