<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/genome-assembly-annotation-and-comparative-genomics-ebp-nor-workshop-2024> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0091>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_0622>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_0797> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Bioinformatician" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "active" ;
    schema1:description """Training materials from the 3-day EBP-Nor Genome Assembly, Annotation and Comparative Genomics workshop that was given at the [Norwegian Biodiversity Genomics &amp; Conference 2024](https://www.ebpnor.org/english/events/norwegian-biodiversity-and-genomics-conference-202.html).\r
\r
The repository includes slides and tutorials that covers the process from going from fastq files of your sequenced genome(s) to performing comparative gene analysis. \r
\r
#### Genome Assembly:\r
The Genome Assembly section introduces participants to whole-genome assembly processes using real datasets. It includes:\r
- **GenomeScope2**: Estimating genome size and heterozygosity.\r
- **Smudgeplot**: Inferring ploidy levels from sequencing data.\r
- **HiFiAdapterFilt**: Filtering adapters from PacBio HiFi reads.\r
- **hifiasm**: Assembly of PacBio HiFi sequencing data.\r
- **YaHS**: Scaffolding genome assemblies using Hi-C data.\r
- **gfastats**: Assembly statistics and quality metrics.\r
- **BUSCO**: Evaluating genome assembly completeness.\r
- **Merqury**: Assessing genome assembly accuracy.\r
- **FCS-GX and GRIT Rapid Curation suite**: Manual curation and contamination removal.\r
- **PretextView**: Visualization of genome assemblies.\r
\r
#### Genome Annotation:\r
Participants learn how to annotate genomes effectively through:\r
- **RepeatMasker**: Masking genomic repeats.\r
- **miniprot**: Mapping protein sets to genome assemblies.\r
- **GALBA**: _Ab initio_ gene prediction.\r
- **EvidenceModeler (EVM)**: Combining gene annotation evidence.\r
- **BUSCO**: Evaluating annotation completeness.\r
- **Functional annotation**: Assigning biological functions to genes.\r
\r
#### Comparative Genomics:\r
This section provides practical training in comparative genomic analyses and visualization:\r
- **OrthoFinder**: Identifying orthologous gene groups.\r
- **R visualizations**: Basic visualization of OrthoFinder results.\r
- **CAFE5**: Analysis of gene family evolution.\r
- **GO enrichment analyses with g:Profiler**: Interpretation of functional enrichments using custom GO annotions.""" ;
    schema1:keywords "Annotation",
        "Assembly",
        "Comparative genomics" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "Scripts",
        "Slides",
        "Tutorial" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "Genome assembly, annotation and comparative genomics - EBP-Nor workshop 2024" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "ELIXIR Norway" ;
            schema1:url <http://elixir-norway.org> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://github.com/ebp-nor/workshop-2024/tree/main> .

