    schema1:description """## Abstract

[ProteoRE Galaxy instance](http://www.proteore.org) provides necessary tools to execute a whole annotation pipeline of a protein list identified by LC-MS/MS experiments. This activity introduces these tools and guides you through a simple pipeline using some example datasets based on the study entitled "Proteomic characterization of human exhaled breath condensate".


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to filter out technical contaminants?
 - How to check for tissue-specificity?
 - How to perform enrichment analysis?
 - How to map your protein list to pathways (Reactome)?
 - How to compare your proteome with other studies?


## Learning Objectives

- Execute a complete annotation pipeline of a protein list identified by LC-MS/MS experiments""" ;
