    schema1:description """## Abstract

The tools that are added to Galaxy can have a wide variance in the compute resources that they require and work efficiently on.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to connect Galaxy to a compute cluster?
 - What are job metrics?
 - What sort of information can I collect?
 - Where can I find this information?


## Learning Objectives

- Be familiar with the basics of installing, configuring, and using Slurm
- Understand all components of the Galaxy job running stack
- Understand how the job conf controls Galaxy's jobs subsystem
- Have a strong understanding of Galaxy job destinations
- Understand the purpose and function of Galaxy job metrics""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Galaxy Server administration",
        "ansible",
        "git-gat",
        "jobs" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "Connecting Galaxy to a compute cluster" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Be familiar with the basics of installing, configuring, and using Slurm
- Understand all components of the Galaxy job running stack
- Understand how the job conf controls Galaxy's jobs subsystem
- Have a strong understanding of Galaxy job destinations
- Understand the purpose and function of Galaxy job metrics""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/admin/tutorials/connect-to-compute-cluster/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "61" .

