    schema1:description """## Abstract

N-Tails is a special Proteomics technique to analyze peptide abundancy changes of protein N-termini. Prior to the MS measurement, N-Tails enriches unmodified, as well as acetylated N-termini. Both common and "unusual" N-termini are identified, where "unusual" means that the protein N-terminus was changes.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How can protein N-termini be enriched for LC-MS/MS?
 - How to analyze the LC-MS/MS data?


## Learning Objectives

- Run an N-TAILS data analysis.""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "intermediate" ;
    schema1:keywords "Proteomics" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/proteomics/tutorials/ntails/workflows/> ] ;
    schema1:name "Detection and quantitation of N-termini (degradomics) via N-TAILS" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches "- Run an N-TAILS data analysis." ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/proteomics/tutorials/ntails/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "16" .

