    schema1:description """## Abstract

You may find that your Galaxy files directory has run out of space, but you don't want to move all of the files from one filesystem to another. One solution to this problem is to use Galaxy's hierarchical object store to add an additional file space for Galaxy.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How does Galaxy locate data?
 - How can I have Galaxy use multiple storage locations?


## Learning Objectives

- Setup Galaxy with both the Hierarachical and Distributed Object Storages""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Galaxy Server administration",
        "ansible",
        "storage" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "Distributed Object Storage" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches "- Setup Galaxy with both the Hierarachical and Distributed Object Storages" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/admin/tutorials/object-store/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "28" .

