    schema1:description """## Abstract

This tutorial will guide you to setup an File Transfer Protocol (FTP) server so galaxy users can use it to upload large files. Indeed, as written on the [galaxy community hub](https://galaxyproject.org/ftp-upload/), uploading data directly from the browser can be unreliable and cumbersome. FTP will allow users to monitor the upload status as well as resume interrupted transfers.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How can I setup FTP to be easy for my users?
 - Can I authenticate ftp users with Galaxy credentials?


## Learning Objectives

- Configure galaxy and install a FTP server.
- Use an Ansible playbook for this.""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Galaxy Server administration",
        "data",
        "git-gat" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "Enable upload via FTP" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Configure galaxy and install a FTP server.
- Use an Ansible playbook for this.""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/admin/tutorials/ftp/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "25" .

