    schema1:description """## Abstract

Progress in synthetic biology is enabled by powerful bioinformatics tools such as those aimed to design metabolic pathways for the production of chemicals. These tools are available in SynBioCAD portal which is the first Galaxy set of tools for synthetic biology and metabolic engineering.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to evaluate a set of heterologous pathways ?


## Learning Objectives

- Calculate the production flux of the lycopene target molecule using _Flux Balance Analysis_ tool.
- Compute thermodynamics values to optimize the yield of the reaction producing the lycopene using _Thermo_ tool.
- Compute the global score for the previous annotated pathways.
- Rank the computed heterologous pathways depending on their score.""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Synthetic Biology" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/record/6628296> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/synthetic-biology/tutorials/pathway_analysis/workflows/> ] ;
    schema1:name "Evaluating and ranking a set of pathways based on multiple metrics" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Calculate the production flux of the lycopene target molecule using _Flux Balance Analysis_ tool.
- Compute thermodynamics values to optimize the yield of the reaction producing the lycopene using _Thermo_ tool.
- Compute the global score for the previous annotated pathways.
- Rank the computed heterologous pathways depending on their score.""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/synthetic-biology/tutorials/pathway_analysis/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "7" .

