    schema1:description """## Abstract

Workflows are a powerful Galaxy feature that allows you to scale up your analysis by performing an end-to-end analysis with a single click of a button. In order to keep provenance of the workflow invocation (an invocation of a workflow means one run or execution of the workflow) it can be exported from Galaxy in the form of a [Workflow Run Crate](https://w3id.org/ro/wfrun/workflow) RO-Crate profile.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - What is a Workflow Run Crate?
 - How can I export a Galaxy Workflow Run Crate?


## Learning Objectives

- Understanding, viewing and creating Galaxy Workflow Run Crates""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "FAIR Data, Workflows, and Research",
        "ro-crate",
        "workflows" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "Exporting Workflow Run RO-Crates from Galaxy" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches "- Understanding, viewing and creating Galaxy Workflow Run Crates" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/fair/tutorials/ro-crate-in-galaxy/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "8" .

