    schema1:description """## Abstract

Monitoring is an incredibly important part of server monitoring and maintenance. Being able to observe trends and identify hot spots by collecting metrics gives you a significant ability to respond to any issues that arise in production. Monitoring is quite easy to get started with, it can be as simple as writing a quick shell script in order to start collecting metrics.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to monitor Galaxy with Telegraf
 - How do I set up InfluxDB
 - How can I make graphs in Grafana?
 - How can I best alert on important metrics?


## Learning Objectives

- Setup InfluxDB
- Setup Telegraf
- Setup Grafana
- Create several charts""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Galaxy Server administration",
        "ansible",
        "git-gat",
        "monitoring" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "Galaxy Monitoring with Telegraf and Grafana" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Setup InfluxDB
- Setup Telegraf
- Setup Grafana
- Create several charts""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/admin/tutorials/monitoring/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "50" .

