    schema1:description """## Abstract

This tutorial uses ChIP-seq datasets from a study published by. The goal of this study was to investigate "the dynamics of occupancy and the role in gene regulation of the transcription factor TAL1, a critical regulator of hematopoiesis, at multiple stages of hematopoietic differentiation."


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How is raw ChIP-seq data processed and analyzed?
 - What are the binding sites of TAL1?
 - Which genes are regulated by TAL1?


## Learning Objectives

- Inspect read quality with FastQC
- Perform read trimming with Trimmomatic
- Align trimmed reads with BWA
- Assess quality and reproducibility of experiments
- Identify TAL1 binding sites with MACS2
- Determine unique/common TAL1 binding sites from G1E and Megakaryocytes
- Identify unique/common TAL1 peaks occupying gene promoters
- Visually inspect TAL1 peaks with Trackster""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "ChIP-seq",
        "Epigenetics" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "DeepTools" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/deeptools> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "SAMtools" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/samtools> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.197100> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/epigenetics/tutorials/tal1-binding-site-identification/workflows/> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "BEDTools" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/bedtools> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Trimmomatic" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/trimmomatic> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "BWA" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/bwa> ] ;
    schema1:name "Identification of the binding sites of the T-cell acute lymphocytic leukemia protein 1 (TAL1)" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Inspect read quality with FastQC
- Perform read trimming with Trimmomatic
- Align trimmed reads with BWA
- Assess quality and reproducibility of experiments
- Identify TAL1 binding sites with MACS2
- Determine unique/common TAL1 binding sites from G1E and Megakaryocytes
- Identify unique/common TAL1 peaks occupying gene promoters
- Visually inspect TAL1 peaks with Trackster""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/epigenetics/tutorials/tal1-binding-site-identification/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "11" .

