    schema1:description """## Abstract

This practical aims to familiarize you with the Galaxy user interface. It will teach you how to perform basic tasks such as importing data, running tools, working with histories, creating workflows, and sharing your work.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - Do genes on opposite strands ever overlap?  If so, how often?


## Learning Objectives

- Learn some of the basic concepts of genomics and bioinformatics
- Familiarize yourself with the basics of Galaxy""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Introduction to Galaxy Analyses" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
