    schema1:description """## Abstract

[JupyterLab](https://jupyterlab.readthedocs.io/en/stable) is an [Integrated Development Environment (IDE)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Integrated_development_environment).


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How can I manipulate data using JupyterLab in Galaxy?
 - How can I start a notebook in JupyterLab?
 - How can I import/export dataset from/to my history to/from the notebook?
 - How can I save my notebook to my history?


## Learning Objectives

- Launch JupyterLab in Galaxy
- Start a notebook
- Import libraries
- Use get() to import datasets from your history to the notebook
- Use put() to export datasets from the notebook to your history
- Save your notebook into your history""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Using Galaxy and Managing your Data",
        "interactive-tools" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ] ;
    schema1:name "JupyterLab in Galaxy" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Launch JupyterLab in Galaxy
- Start a notebook
- Import libraries
- Use get() to import datasets from your history to the notebook
- Use put() to export datasets from the notebook to your history
- Save your notebook into your history""" ;
