    schema1:description """## Abstract

"Flow Control" is how we describe when we change the flow of code's execution, based on some conditions. Here we'll learn how to take different actions depending on what data out program sees, or how to run code only if some condition is true.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How can my programs do different things based on data values?


## Learning Objectives

- Write conditional statements including `if`, `elif`, and `else` branches.
- Correctly evaluate expressions containing `and` and `or`.""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Foundations of Data Science",
        "jupyter-notebook" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
