    schema1:description """## Abstract

During sequencing, the nucleotide bases in a DNA or RNA sample (library) are determined by the sequencer. For each fragment in the library, a sequence is generated, also called a **read**, which is simply a succession of nucleotides.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to perform quality control of NGS raw data?
 - What are the quality parameters to check for a dataset?
 - How to improve the quality of a dataset?


## Learning Objectives

- Assess short reads FASTQ quality using FASTQE 🧬😎 and FastQC
- Assess long reads FASTQ quality using Nanoplot and PycoQC
- Perform quality correction with Cutadapt (short reads)
- Summarise quality metrics MultiQC
- Process single-end and paired-end data""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Sequence analysis" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "pycoQC" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/pycoqc> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "FASTQE" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/fastqe> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Cutadapt" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/cutadapt> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/records/61771> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/sequence-analysis/tutorials/quality-control/workflows/> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "NanoPlot" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/nanoplot> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "FastQC" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/fastqc> ] ;
    schema1:name "Quality Control" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Assess short reads FASTQ quality using FASTQE 🧬😎 and FastQC
- Assess long reads FASTQ quality using Nanoplot and PycoQC
- Perform quality correction with Cutadapt (short reads)
- Summarise quality metrics MultiQC
- Process single-end and paired-end data""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/sequence-analysis/tutorials/quality-control/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "48" .

