    schema1:description """## Abstract

Molecular dynamics (MD) is a method to simulate molecular motion by iterative application of Newton's laws of motion. It is often applied to large biomolecules such as proteins or nucleic acids.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How do I use the GROMACS engine in Galaxy?
 - What is the correct procedure for performing a simple molecular dynamics simulation of a protein?


## Learning Objectives

- Learn about the GROMACS engine provided via Galaxy.
- Understand the structure of the molecular dynamics workflow.
- Prepare a short (1 ns) trajectory for a simulation of a protein.""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "intermediate" ;
    schema1:keywords "Computational chemistry" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/record/2598415> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "The Protein Data Bank (PDB)" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/pdb> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/computational-chemistry/tutorials/md-simulation-gromacs/workflows/> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Gromacs" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/gromacs> ] ;
    schema1:name "Running molecular dynamics simulations using GROMACS" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Learn about the GROMACS engine provided via Galaxy.
- Understand the structure of the molecular dynamics workflow.
- Prepare a short (1 ns) trajectory for a simulation of a protein.""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/computational-chemistry/tutorials/md-simulation-gromacs/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "15" .

