            schema1:name "Saskia Hiltemann" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2023-11-09"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2018-12-14"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

Small Non-coding RNAs (ncRNAs) play a vital role in many cellular processes such as RNA splicing, translation, gene regulation. The small RNA-seq is a type of RNA-seq in which RNA fragments are size selected to capture only short RNAs. One of the most common applications of the small RNA-seq is discovering novel small ncRNAs. Mapping the small RNA-seq data reveals interesting patterns that represent the traces of the small RNA processing.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - What do the read profiles of small non-coding RNAs represent?
 - How to cluster the read profiles based on some intrinsic features?


## Learning Objectives

- Difference between mRNA-seq and smallRNA-seq
- Unsupervised grouping of the adjacent reads into read profiles
- Look and learn what the shapes of the read profiles represent
- Clustering of the read profiles by machine learning algorithm""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Transcriptomics" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "SAMtools" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/samtools> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/record/1491876> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/transcriptomics/tutorials/small_ncrna_clustering/workflows/> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "blockbuster" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/blockbuster> ] ;
    schema1:name "Small Non-coding RNA Clustering using BlockClust" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Difference between mRNA-seq and smallRNA-seq
- Unsupervised grouping of the adjacent reads into read profiles
- Look and learn what the shapes of the read profiles represent
- Clustering of the read profiles by machine learning algorithm""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/transcriptomics/tutorials/small_ncrna_clustering/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "8" .

