    schema1:description """## Abstract




## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How do I perform a trajectory analysis using Monocle3 in R?
 - What should I do when Galaxy's Monocle tools are not enough?
 - How do I assign cell types to the clusters?
 - How do I infer lineage relationships between clusters, without a time series?
 - How do I perform batch correction and differential expression analysis in Monocle?


## Learning Objectives

- Identify which operations are necessary to transform an AnnData object into the files needed for Monocle
- Describe the Monocle3 functions in R
- Recognise steps that can be performed in R, but not with current Galaxy tools
- Repeat the Monocle3 workflow and choose appropriate parameter values
- Compare the outputs from Scanpy, Monocle in Galaxy and Monocle in R
- Describe differential expression analysis methods""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "MIGHTS",
        "Single Cell",
        "jupyter-notebook",
        "paper-replication",
        "rmarkdown-notebook" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Quarto/RMarkdown Notebook" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/single-cell/tutorials/scrna-case_monocle3-rstudio/single-cell-scrna-case_monocle3-rstudio.Rmd> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/record/7455590> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "RStudio" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/rstudio> ] ;
    schema1:name "Inferring single cell trajectories with Monocle3 (R)" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Identify which operations are necessary to transform an AnnData object into the files needed for Monocle
- Describe the Monocle3 functions in R
- Recognise steps that can be performed in R, but not with current Galaxy tools
- Repeat the Monocle3 workflow and choose appropriate parameter values
- Compare the outputs from Scanpy, Monocle in Galaxy and Monocle in R
- Describe differential expression analysis methods""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/single-cell/tutorials/scrna-case_monocle3-rstudio/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "13" .

