    schema1:datePublished "2022-09-30"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

This tutorial is a follow-up to the ['Single-cell RNA-seq: Case Study'](http://localhost:4000/training-material/topics/single-cell/index.html). We will use the same sample from the previous tutorials. If you haven’t done them yet, it’s highly recommended that you go through them to get an idea how to [prepare a single cell matrix](http://localhost:4000/training-material/topics/single-cell/tutorials/scrna-case_alevin/tutorial.html), [combine datasets](http://localhost:4000/training-material/topics/single-cell/tutorials/scrna-case_alevin-combine-datasets/tutorial.html) and [filter, plot and process scRNA-seq data](http://localhost:4000/training-material/topics/single-cell/tutorials/scrna-case_basic-pipeline/tutorial.html) to get the data in the form we’ll be working on today.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How can I prepare input files for Monocle starting from an AnnData object?
 - How can I infer lineage relationships between clusters, without a time series?
 - What can trajectory analysis tell us?


## Learning Objectives

- Identify which operations to perform on an AnnData object to obtain the files needed for Monocle
- Follow the Monocle3 workflow and choose the right parameter values
- Compare the outputs from Scanpy and Monocle
- Interpet trajectory analysis results""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "MIGHTS",
        "Single Cell",
        "paper-replication" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
