    schema1:description """## Abstract

RNA-Seq analysis helps researchers annotate new genes and splice variants, and provides cell- and context-specific quantification of gene expression. RNA-Seq data, however, are complex and require both computer science and mathematical knowledge to be managed and interpreted.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How are RNA-Seq results stored?
 - Why are visualization techniques needed?
 - How to select genes for visualizing meaningful results of differential gene expression analysis?


## Learning Objectives

- Manage RNA-Seq results
- Extract genes for producing differential gene expression analysis visualizations
- Visualize meaningful information""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Transcriptomics" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/record/1001880> ] ;
    schema1:name "Visualization of RNA-Seq results with CummeRbund" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Manage RNA-Seq results
- Extract genes for producing differential gene expression analysis visualizations
- Visualize meaningful information""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/transcriptomics/tutorials/rna-seq-viz-with-cummerbund/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "16" .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/hands-on-for-visualization-of-rna-seq-results-with-heatmap2-tutorial> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3308> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Students" ] ;
