            schema1:name "Maria Doyle" ] ;
    schema1:competencyRequired "Introduction to Galaxy Analyses",
        "Mapping",
        "Quality Control" ;
    schema1:contributor [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Björn Grüning" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Saskia Hiltemann" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Helena Rasche" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Nicola Soranzo" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2023-11-09"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2018-12-31"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

Heatmaps are commonly used to visualize RNA-Seq results. They are useful for visualizing the expression of genes across the samples. In this tutorial we show how the **heatmap2** tool in Galaxy can be used to generate heatmaps. The heatmap2 tool uses the heatmap.2 function from the R gplots package. Here we will demonstrate how to make a heatmap of the top differentially expressed (DE) genes in an RNA-Seq experiment, similar to what is shown for the fruitfly dataset in the [RNA-seq ref-based tutorial](http://localhost:4000/training-material/topics/transcriptomics/tutorials/ref-based/tutorial.html). We will also show how a heatmap for a custom set of genes an be created.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to generate heatmaps from RNA-seq data?


## Learning Objectives

- Create heatmaps of RNA-seq data""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Transcriptomics" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/record/2529926> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/transcriptomics/tutorials/rna-seq-viz-with-heatmap2/workflows/> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "ggplot2" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/ggplot2> ] ;
    schema1:name "Visualization of RNA-Seq results with heatmap2" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches "- Create heatmaps of RNA-seq data" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/transcriptomics/tutorials/rna-seq-viz-with-heatmap2/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "13" .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/hands-on-for-visualization-of-rna-seq-results-with-volcano-plot-in-r-tutorial> a schema1:LearningResource ;
