<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/how-to-share-text-mining-results-in-biology> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Dayane Araujo" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Aravind Venkatesan" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Francesco Talo" ] ;
    schema1:description """Overview\r
\r
Though text mining becomes more widespread in biology, an average researcher can rarely use it to their advantage. In this webinar, Europe PMC presents a tool to easily share annotated biological entities and relations with the research community. Europe PMC Annotation Submission System allows text miners and curators in the field of life sciences to make their results available to the public. Annotated concepts can be browsed and searched for both on Europe PMC website as a part of SciLite tool and Advanced search, as well as via the Annotations API.\r
\r
This webinar was recorded on 9th of July 2019. It is best viewed in full-screen mode using Google Chrome. The slides from this webinar can be downloaded below.\r
\r
Audience\r
\r
This webinar is aimed at individuals who wish to learn more about sharing and reusing results of biomedical text-mining. No prior knowledge of bioinformatics is required, but an undergraduate level knowledge of biology would be useful.\r
\r
See the EMBL-EBI training pages for a list of upcoming webinars.\r
\r
No prior knowledge of bioinformatics is required, but an undergraduate-level understanding of biology would be useful.""" ;
    schema1:keywords "Europe PMC",
        "Literature search",
        "Text mining" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "Webinar" ;
    schema1:license <file:///home/runner/work/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/notspecified> ;
    schema1:name "How to Share Text Mining Results in Biology" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "EMBL-EBI" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/training> ],
        [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "European Bioinformatics Institute (EBI)" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.ebi.ac.uk> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://ebi.ac.uk/training/online/course/how-share-text-mining-results-biology> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/how-to-share-text-mining-results-in-biology-d85ab1ee-a64e-4e0d-b1d4-6f7e87f282c9> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0218>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3068> ;
    schema1:description "Though text mining becomes more widespread in biology, an average researcher can rarely use it to their advantage. In this webinar Europe PMC presents a tool to easily share annotated biological entities and relations with the research community. Europe PMC Annotation Submission System allows text miners and curators in the field of life sciences to make their results available to the public. Annotated concepts can be browsed and searched for both on Europe PMC website as a part of SciLite tool and Advanced search, as well as via the Annotations API." ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "Recorded webinar" ;
    schema1:license <file:///home/runner/work/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/notspecified> ;
