            schema1:name "amijalis" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "manulera" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "active" ;
    schema1:dateCreated "2025-04-11"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """Pydna is a python package that provides a human-readable formal descriptions of 🧬 cloning and genetic assembly strategies in Python 🐍 for simulation and verification. Pydna can be used as executable documentation for cloning.\r
\r
Pydna provides simulation of:\r
\r
- Primer design\r
- PCR\r
- Restriction digestion\r
- Ligation\r
- Gel electrophoresis of DNA with generation of gel images\r
- Homologous recombination\r
- Gibson assembly\r
- Golden gate assembly\r
\r
The training material contains documentation to install the library and jupyter notebooks describing how to get started with the library and examples.""" ;
