<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/indexing-and-profiling-microbes-with-metasbt> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0637>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3174>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3697> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Students" ] ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Fabio Cumbo" ] ;
    schema1:competencyRequired "Galaxy Basics for everyone",
        "Introduction to Galaxy Analyses" ;
    schema1:contributor [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Daniel Blankenberg" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2025-08-25"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2025-08-25"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

## Introduction


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - What are Sequence Bloom Trees and how does MetaSBT use them for genomics?
 - How do you build a custom viral database from a set of reference genomes?
 - How can an existing MetaSBT database be updated with new viruses?
 - How do you profile a query viral genome against a database to determine its identity and novelty?
 - How can we interpret the viral genome profiling results?


## Learning Objectives

- Understand the fundamental concepts of MetaSBT for efficient genomic indexing.
- Learn to use the `metasbt_index` tool to create a custom viral database.
- Learn to use the `metasbt_index` tool to update an existing database.
- Learn to use the `metasbt_profile` tool to identify and characterize a query viral genome.
- Be able to interpret the similarity reports generated by the profiling tool.""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Microbiome",
        "diversity",
        "metagenomics",
        "taxonomic profiling" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/records/15882806> ] ;
    schema1:name "Indexing and profiling microbes with MetaSBT" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Understand the fundamental concepts of MetaSBT for efficient genomic indexing.
- Learn to use the `metasbt_index` tool to create a custom viral database.
- Learn to use the `metasbt_index` tool to update an existing database.
- Learn to use the `metasbt_profile` tool to identify and characterize a query viral genome.
- Be able to interpret the similarity reports generated by the profiling tool.""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/microbiome/tutorials/metasbt/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "7" .

