<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/introduction-to-r> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3372> ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Laura Biggins" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Simon Andrews" ] ;
    schema1:description """R is a popular language and environment that allows powerful and fast manipulation of data, offering many statistical and graphical options. This course aims to introduce R as a tool for statistics and graphics, with the main aim being to become comfortable with the R environment. It will focus on entering and manipulating data in R and producing simple graphs. A few functions for basic statistics will be briefly introduced, but statistical functions will not be covered in detail.\r
\r
**Course Content**\r
\r
* What is R\r
* Getting familiar with the R console\r
* Entering Data\r
* Manipulating data\r
* Importing data files\r
* Creating Graphs (boxplots, barplots, scatterplots, line graphs)\r
\r
**Course Material**\r
\r
* [Course Manual (pdf)](http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training/Introduction_to_R/Introduction%20to%20R%20course%20booklet.pdf)\r
* [Course Manual (docx)](http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training/Introduction_to_R/Introduction%20to%20R%20course%20booklet.docx)\r
* [Course Exercises (pdf)](http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training/Introduction_to_R/Introduction%20to%20R%20course%20Exercises.pdf)\r
* [Course Exercises (doc)](http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training/Introduction_to_R/Introduction%20to%20R%20course%20Exercises.doc)\r
* [Data Structures Slides (pdf)](http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training/Introduction_to_R/Introduction%20to%20R%20data%20structures.pdf)\r
* [Data Structures Slides (pptx)](http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training/Introduction_to_R/Introduction%20to%20R%20data%20structures.pptx)\r
* [R command cheatsheet (pdf)](http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training/Introduction_to_R/R%20command%20cheatsheet.pdf)\r
* [Course data (zip)](http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training/Introduction_to_R/Intro_to_R_data_files.zip)""" ;
