\r
5. Paired T-Test Using Two-Way ANOVA &amp; ANOVA With More Effects\r
\r
6. Regression Recap\r
\r
7. General Linear Models (GLMs) - Introduction\r
\r
8. GLM Fitting Categorical &amp; Continuous Effects\r
\r
9. Using GLMs to Adjust for Confounding Variables &amp; Using GLMS for Prediction\r
\r
10. GLMS – general points\r
\r
11. GLMS – checking model assumptions\r
\r
12. GLMs - General Points\r
\r
13. Models for Other Data Types\r
\r
14. Logistic Regression\r
\r
15. Logistic Regression Example – Assessing Risk Factors\r
\r
16. Logistic Regression Example Continued – Predicting Risk\r
\r
17. Logistic Regression – General Points\r
\r
18. Ordinal Logistic Regression\r
\r
19. Survival Analysis\r
\r
20. Repeated Measures Data\r
\r
21. Mixed (or Multilevel) Models\r
\r
22. Choice of Software Package\r
\r
23. Self-Learning Resources""" ;
