    schema1:description "Ensembl Bacteria is a browser for bacterial and archaeal genomes. In this webinar, we will explore Ensembl Bacteria to learn more about the latest data and where it came from, view annotation of molecular interactions involving bacterial genes and comparative genomics data involving key bacterial species. You may either watch the entire presentation from the introduction or navigate directly to a specific section by clicking the links provided below:IntroductionWhy do we need genome browsers?Ensembl Bacteria featuresTools in Ensembl BacteriaFinding a bacterial speciesHelp and documentation" ;
