<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/life-traits-ecorgionalization-workflow> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0610> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Students" ] ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Jean Le Cras" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Yvan Le Bras" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Pauline Seguineau" ] ;
    schema1:competencyRequired "Introduction to Galaxy Analyses" ;
    schema1:contributor [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Saskia Hiltemann" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Jean Le Cras" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Yvan Le Bras" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Björn Grüning" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2025-06-10"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2025-06-02"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

This tutorial is designed to guide you through the Ecoregionalization Galaxy workflow, demonstrating how to create a life traits ecoregionalization map from occurrences and environmental data using a boosted regression tree model for predictions.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to use the life traits ecoregionalization?
 - How to construct ecoregions from occurrences species data and environmental data?


## Learning Objectives

- Learning how to use the ecoregionalization workflow.
- Learning how to collect life traits informations from marine species occurences.
- Learning about boosted regression trees algorithm.
- Learning about Silhouette index and select an appropriate number of clusters.
- Learning about Clara clustering algorithm (PAM for large datasets)objectives.
- Create an ecoregionalization map from life traits data.""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Ecology",
        "biodiversity" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ] ;
    schema1:name "Life Traits Ecoregionalization workflow" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Learning how to use the ecoregionalization workflow.
- Learning how to collect life traits informations from marine species occurences.
- Learning about boosted regression trees algorithm.
- Learning about Silhouette index and select an appropriate number of clusters.
- Learning about Clara clustering algorithm (PAM for large datasets)objectives.
- Create an ecoregionalization map from life traits data.""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/ecology/tutorials/ecoregiolifetraits/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "3" .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/linear-motifs-and-phosphorylation-sites> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
