    schema1:description """## Abstract

# Introduction


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - Which biological questions are addressed by the tutorial?
 - Which bioinformatics techniques are important to know for this type of data?


## Learning Objectives

- Follow a marine omics analysis
- Learn to conduct a secondary metabolite biosynthetic gene cluster (SMBGC) Annotation
- Discover SanntiS a tool for identifying BGCs in genomic &amp; metagenomic data
- Manage fasta files""" ;
