    schema1:contributor [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Björn Grüning" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Saskia Hiltemann" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Marie Josse" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2025-09-16"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2025-08-08"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

The next sections explain how to qualify and calibrate the nitrate sensor mounted on the Argo float **4903881** either tool by tool or by running a pre-defined Galaxy workflow.\r


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to access Argo data?
 - What hat is a DMQC analysis /  QCV analysis?
 - How to qualify and calibrate nitrate in the ocean?


## Learning Objectives

- Learn how to do a QCV analysis on the nitrate variable of the ocean ?""" ;
