    schema1:datePublished "2025-06-30"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """Open Science in the Swedish Context is a modular training programme designed to support researchers in integrating Open Science practices throughout the entire research lifecycle.\r
\r
Based on national and international frameworks — including SUHF’s Färdplan för öppen vetenskap and KB’s Nationella riktlinjer för öppen vetenskap — the course provides practical guidance on key topics such as open publishing, data sharing and reuse, responsible research evaluation, science communication, intellectual property rights, and the future of Open Science.\r
\r
This Figshare collection brings together presentation materials, recorded lectures, and hands-on exercises from the full 10-module course, enabling flexible self-study and reuse.\r
\r
It is intended for researchers, educators, and research support staff seeking to develop their skills and understanding of Open Science within the Swedish context — and beyond.""" ;
