<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/open-with-purpose-how-and-why-to-make-your-data-open> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0219>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3071> ;
    schema1:description """As part of EMBL-EBI’s celebration of Open Access week, this special one-off webinar will give you insight into the benefits of open access data, alongside guidance and tips on managing your data.\r
\r
Featuring four members of EMBL-EBI’s resource teams (from BioSamples, ENA, IntAct/Complex Portal &amp; Europe PMC), you’ll get an overview of Open and FAIR data, insights into submission processes and support, the importance of open literature and some hints, tips and tricks for ensuring your data can easily be made available to others. You’ll also get an opportunity to ask live questions to all four of our speakers, and find out where you can learn more.""" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "Recorded webinar" ;
    schema1:license <file:///home/runner/work/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/notspecified> ;
    schema1:name "Open with purpose: How and why to make your data open" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
