    schema1:datePublished "2025-09-24"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

This tutorial shows how to use **OpenRefine** in Galaxy to clean and visualize data from the **humanities and social sciences**. It has two parts:


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to use OpenRefine in Galaxy to clean your data?
 - How to use a workflow in Galaxy to extract and visualise information from your data?


## Learning Objectives

- Start OpenRefine as an Interactive Tool in Galaxy
- Use OpenRefine to clean your data (remove duplicates, separate multiple values from the same field, etc.)
- Export your cleaned data from OpenRefine to Galaxy
- Use a pre-existing workflow in Galaxy to extract specific information and visualise your findings""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Digital Humanities" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/digital-humanities/tutorials/open-refine-tutorial/workflows/> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17047254> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ] ;
    schema1:name "OpenRefine Tutorial for researching cultural data" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Start OpenRefine as an Interactive Tool in Galaxy
- Use OpenRefine to clean your data (remove duplicates, separate multiple values from the same field, etc.)
- Export your cleaned data from OpenRefine to Galaxy
- Use a pre-existing workflow in Galaxy to extract specific information and visualise your findings""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/digital-humanities/tutorials/open-refine-tutorial/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "2" .

