    schema1:description """## Abstract

Parameter tuning is super important in image analysis. 


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - What are the challenges of using the same settings for every biological image, and how does parameter tuning address these challenges?
 - How can we choose the best filters for preprocessing images for nuclei segmentation?


## Learning Objectives

- Understand the importance of parameter tuning in bioimage analysis for achieving accurate results
- Learn how to perform parameter tuning for segmentation in Galaxy""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Imaging",
        "bioimaging" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/imaging/tutorials/parameter-tuning/workflows/> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "scikit-image" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/scikit-image> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy Image Analysis" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy_image_analysis> ] ;
    schema1:name "Parameter tuning and optimization - Evaluating nuclei segmentation with Galaxy" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Understand the importance of parameter tuning in bioimage analysis for achieving accurate results
- Learn how to perform parameter tuning for segmentation in Galaxy""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/imaging/tutorials/parameter-tuning/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "1" .

