    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2024-03-27"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2024-03-26"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

The persistent identifier is defined.  Learners will be able to define the structure of an identifier and explain its importance.  


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - What is a persistent identifier?
 - What is the structure of identifiers?
 - Why does your dataset need to have an identifier?


## Learning Objectives

- Explain the definition and importance of using identifiers.
- Illustrate what are the persistent identifiers.
- Give examples of the structure of persistent identifiers.""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "FAIR Data, Workflows, and Research",
        "data stewardship",
        "dmp",
        "fair" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "Persistent Identifiers" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
