    schema1:dateModified "2025-06-20"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2025-02-26"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description "The presentation integrates Plazi's learning courses. The lesson is a tutorial to proceed a Quality control of data extracted from publications using the program GoldenGATE Imagine, Plazi’s tool for data extraction from publications, as well as a checklist to avoid and/or correct errors before data liberation to online open repositories." ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "advanced" ;
    schema1:identifier "10.5281/zenodo.15706224" ;
    schema1:keywords "Data curation",
        "Data extraction",
        "Data processing",
        "FAIR Data, Workflows, and Research",
        "GoldenGATE Imagine" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "lessons" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "Plazi: QC Tutorial" ;
    schema1:teaches """Develop an awareness of the functionalities of the computer program used to extract data for scholarly publications: the GoldenGate Imagine - GGI, as well as the step-by-step for data extraction, annotation enhancement, and quality control of data.\r
""" ;
    schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/records/15706224> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/ploting-a-microbial-genome-with-circos> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Students" ] ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Helena Rasche" ] ;
    schema1:competencyRequired "Circos",
        "Visualisation with Circos" ;
    schema1:contributor [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Björn Grüning" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Saskia Hiltemann" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2024-09-17"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2023-11-08"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

Once you're comfortable with [Circos in Galaxy](http://localhost:4000/training-material/topics/visualisation/tutorials/circos/tutorial.html), you might want to explore some real world use cases with Circos such as making a simple Genome Annotation plot, like one might want to publish alongside their genome annotation publication


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How can I visualise common genomic datasets like GFF3, BigWig, and VCF


## Learning Objectives

- Plot an *E. coli* genome in Galaxy
- With tracks for the annotations, sequencing data, and variants.""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "intermediate" ;
    schema1:keywords "Visualisation" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Circos" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/circos> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/visualisation/tutorials/circos-microbial/workflows/> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3591856> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "DeepTools" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/deeptools> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galactic Circos" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galactic_circos> ] ;
    schema1:name "Ploting a Microbial Genome with Circos" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Plot an *E. coli* genome in Galaxy
- With tracks for the annotations, sequencing data, and variants.""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/visualisation/tutorials/circos-microbial/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "3" .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/plotting-complex-figures-with-r> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Simon Andrews" ] ;
    schema1:description """This course is a comprehensive guide to the use of the built in R plotting functionality to construct everything from customised simple plots to complex multi-layered figures. It follows on from the material in our introductory R course and participants are expected to have a basic understanding of R - enough to load and do basic manipulation of datasets.\r
\r
**Course Content**\r
\r
* The R painters model\r
* Core graph types and options\r
* Plot area customisation\r
* Using colour in plots\r
* Adding plot overlays\r
* Useful extension packages\r
* Writing plots to files\r
\r
**Course Material**\r
\r
* [Course Manual (pdf)](http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training/Core_R_Plotting/Core%20R%20Plotting.pdf)\r
* [Course Manual (docx)](http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training/Core_R_Plotting/Core%20R%20Plotting.docx)\r
* [Course Exercises (pdf)](http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training/Core_R_Plotting/Core%20R%20Plotting%20Exercises.pdf)\r
* [Course Exercises (docx)](http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training/Core_R_Plotting/Core%20R%20Plotting%20Exercises.docx)\r
* [Presentation Slides (pdf)](http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training/Core_R_Plotting/core_r_graphs.pdf)\r
* [Presentation Slides (pptx)](http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training/Core_R_Plotting/core_r_graphs.pptx)\r
* [Course data (zip)](http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training/Core_R_Plotting/Core%20R%20Plotting%20Data.zip)""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "intermediate" ;
    schema1:keywords "Babraham Institute",
        "Graph plotting",
        "R Programming" ;
    schema1:license <file:///home/runner/work/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/other-nc> ;
    schema1:name "Plotting complex figures with R" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "Bioinformatics and Biomathematics Training Hub" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.earlham.ac.uk/bbsrc-bioinformatics-and-biomathematics-training-hub> ] ;
    schema1:url <http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/training.html#rplotting> .

