    schema1:description """## Abstract

The cBioPortal is an open-access web platform that provides intuitive access to large-scale cancer genomics datasets. Originally developed to make complex molecular profiling data more accessible to the broader research community, cBioPortal hosts data from thousands of cancer studies and tens of thousands of tumor samples.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to download data from cBioPortal?
 - How to prepare omics data for Flexynesis integration.


## Learning Objectives

- Download Breast cancer data from Metabric through cBioportal using Flexynesis
- Clean and preprocess genomics data
- Format data for downstream integration analysis""" ;
