    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2024-12-19"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2024-12-18"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

Using Pulsar via the SURF Research Cloud (SRC) allows researchers to start Pulsar instances on-demand to expand their computational resources and even access GPUs to help and analyze their data in a secure environment following the General Data Protection Regulations (GDPR).


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How do I start a Pulsar instance on SURF Research Cloud?
 - How do I connect to Pulsar?


## Learning Objectives

- Be able to attach a Pulsar node to Galaxy
- Send jobs to Pulsar""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Galaxy Server administration",
        "deploying" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "Pulsar usage on SURF Research Cloud" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
