        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Fotis E. Psomopoulos" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2023-11-09"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2023-05-15"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

In recent years, RNA sequencing (in short RNA-Seq) has become a very widely used technology to analyze the continuously changing cellular transcriptome, i.e. the set of all RNA molecules in one cell or a population of cells. One of the most common aims of RNA-Seq is the profiling of gene expression by identifying genes or molecular pathways that are differentially expressed (DE) between two or more biological conditions. This tutorial demonstrates a computational workflow for counting and locating the genes in RNA sequences. The first and most critical step in an RNA-seq analysis.\r


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - What are the first steps to process RNA-seq data?


## Learning Objectives

- Learn the basics to process RNA sequences
- Check the quality and trim the sequences with bash
- Use command line STAR aligner to map the RNA sequences
- Estimate the number of reads per gens""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Transcriptomics" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/record/6457007> ] ;
    schema1:name "RNA-seq Alignment with STAR" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Learn the basics to process RNA sequences
- Check the quality and trim the sequences with bash
- Use command line STAR aligner to map the RNA sequences
- Estimate the number of reads per gens""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/transcriptomics/tutorials/rna-seq-bash-star-align/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "6" .

