    schema1:dateModified "2024-09-27"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2024-02-21"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

Genome mining is an important source for various bio-active compounds such as antibiotics and fungicides.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to discover secondary metabolites produced by microorganisms ?
 - How to identify the discovered secondary metabolites in compound libraries ?
 - How to bridge workflow steps using custom scripts ?


## Learning Objectives

- Gene cluster prediction using antiSMAHS.
- Extraction of gene cluster products using a custom script.
- Query of the products in compound libraries using cheminformatic tools.""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Genome Annotation" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "antiSMASH" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/antismash> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "NCBI Resources" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/ncbi_resources> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "chemfp" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/chemfp> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/genome-annotation/tutorials/secondary-metabolite-discovery/workflows/> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/records/10652998> ] ;
    schema1:name "Secondary metabolite discovery" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Gene cluster prediction using antiSMAHS.
- Extraction of gene cluster products using a custom script.
- Query of the products in compound libraries using cheminformatic tools.""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/genome-annotation/tutorials/secondary-metabolite-discovery/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "2" .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/selecting-and-evaluating-preprints-for-journal-club> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3068> ;
    schema1:description """Preprints enable researchers to rapidly share their work publicly before the formal peer review process. This webinar will introduce preprints, demonstrate how to select and evaluate preprints by using tools developed by Europe PMC, and show you how to set up and run a preprint journal club based on the experience run by the Immunology departments at Mount Sinai-Oxford-Karolinska.\r
\r
Europe PMC indexes preprints abstracts and full text COVID-19 preprints from 24 life science preprint servers. Preprints in Europe PMC are linked to data and platforms that comment or evaluate preprints. How to use the linked data and platforms to select and evaluate preprints will be addressed. We will also explore how to set up and run a preprint journal club and share useful tips so you can build your own preprint journal club. This can help you in building your critical thinking whilst promoting awareness of current research.""" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "Recorded webinar" ;
    schema1:license <file:///home/runner/work/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/notspecified> ;
    schema1:name "Selecting and evaluating preprints for Journal Club" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "European Bioinformatics Institute (EBI)" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.ebi.ac.uk> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/training/events/selecting-and-evaluating-preprints-journal-club> .

