<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/semantic-standards> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_0089>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3063>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3071>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_3316>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_4012> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Bioinformaticians" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Biomedical Researchers" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Data Scientists" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Data Managers" ],
        [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Research Scientists" ] ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Personalized Health Informatics Group" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Kristin Gnodke" ] ;
    schema1:contributor [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Sabine Österle" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "active" ;
    schema1:description """This video was developed in the context of the [Swiss Personalized Health Network (SPHN)](https://sphn.ch) initiative and serves as an introduction to the main standards used within the [SPHN Interoperability Framework](https://sphn.ch/network/data-coordination-center/the-sphn-semantic-interoperability-framework/) developed by the SPHN Data Coordination Center (DCC) together with its collaboration partners.\r
\r
Semantic standards gain importance when it comes to FAIR data sharing for research in Personalized Medicine and beyond. This training offers an insight into the most important clinical semantic standards that are relevant in Switzerland or internationally. Advantages, disadvantages and differences between the standards are highlighted and illustrated with practical examples.\r
\r
__Prerequisites:__\r
\r
None\r
\r
__After the training you will be able to:__\r
\r
- Distinguish between classifications and ontologies\r
- Understand the basics of CHOP, ATC, ICD-10, SNOMED CT and LOINC, and their area of application.\r
\r
__Resources:__\r
\r
All resources are available on the [training's GitLab space](https://git.dcc.sib.swiss/sphn-semantic-framework/sphn-training-material/-/tree/master/Semantic%20Standards#semantic-standards)""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "ATC",
        "CHOP",
        "Clinical data",
        "Data semantics",
        "FAIR",
        "ICD",
        "Interoperability",
        "LOINC",
        "Ontology",
        "SNOMED CT",
        "Standards" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "E-learning",
        "Training materials",
        "Video" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "Semantic Standards" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "ELIXIR Switzerland" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.sib.swiss/training/> ],
        <https://ror.org/002n09z45> ;
    schema1:url <https://sphn.ch/training/semantic-standards-training/> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/sentinel-5p-data-visualisation> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Students" ] ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Marie Josse" ] ;
    schema1:competencyRequired "Introduction to Galaxy Analyses" ;
    schema1:contributor [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Saskia Hiltemann" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Helena Rasche" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2025-05-10"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2024-01-26"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

Through this tutorial you will learn here how to access and download Copernicus Data Space Ecosystem (CDSE) data through a jupyterlab Galaxy interactive tool :


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to visualise volcanoes with Sentinel 5 data ?
 - How can we see the evolution of sulfur dioxide and aerosol index through time?
 - How can be used OpenEO ?


## Learning Objectives

- Learn to use OpenEO in a jupyterlab
- Learn to handle satellite data
- Practice on how to visualise netcdf data with Panoply
- Handle going from one interactive tool to another
- Learn to visualise gases around a volcano""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Climate",
        "earth-system",
        "satellite data",
        "volcano" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/climate/tutorials/sentinel5_data/workflows/> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ] ;
    schema1:name "Sentinel 5P data visualisation" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Learn to use OpenEO in a jupyterlab
- Learn to handle satellite data
- Practice on how to visualise netcdf data with Panoply
- Handle going from one interactive tool to another
- Learn to visualise gases around a volcano""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/climate/tutorials/sentinel5_data/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "2" .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/sequence-alignment-with-bowtie2-sandbox-bio> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3168> ;
    schema1:description "Interactive bowtie2 tutorial: learn to align sequencing reads to a reference genome using a command-line interface in your browser." ;
