    schema1:datePublished "2025-03-24"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

# Prerequisites


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How to set up a minimal Onedata dev instance?
 - How can I test the Galaxy &amp; Onedata integration in a sandbox environment?


## Learning Objectives

- Quickly set up a zero-config dockerized Onedata deployment.
- Run Onedata locally for Galaxy development and testing purposes.""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Development in Galaxy",
        "storage" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:name "Setting up a dev Onedata instance" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Quickly set up a zero-config dockerized Onedata deployment.
- Run Onedata locally for Galaxy development and testing purposes.""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/dev/tutorials/onedata-dev-instance/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "2" .

