        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Cristóbal Gallardo" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2025-04-24"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2023-05-03"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

The term **"microbiome"** describes "a characteristic microbial community occupying a reasonably well-defined habitat which has distinct physio-chemical properties. The term thus not only refers to the microorganisms involved but also encompasses their theatre of activity".


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - Which species (or genera, families, ...) are present in my sample?
 - What are the different approaches and tools to get the community profile of my sample?
 - How can we visualize and compare community profiles?


## Learning Objectives

- Explain what taxonomic assignment is
- Explain how taxonomic assignment works
- Apply Kraken and MetaPhlAn to assign taxonomic labels
- Apply Krona and Pavian to visualize results of assignment and understand the output
- Identify taxonomic classification tool that fits best depending on their data""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Microbiome",
        "metagenomics",
        "microgalaxy",
        "taxonomic profiling" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "kraken2" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/kraken2> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Bracken" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/bracken> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "MetaPhlAn" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/metaphlan> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/record/7871630> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "taxonomy_krona_chart" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/taxonomy_krona_chart> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "KrakenTools" ;
