<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/training-rnaseq-biostat-part> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """This course is part of the INRAE training session about “bioinformatics and biostatistics analysis of RNA-seq data” and of the Biostatistics platform “Initiation à LA statistique, niveau 4”. \r
The material provided on the present webpage is related to the biostatistics part and covers the following topics:\r
\r
R and RStudio\r
design of experiments\r
variability\r
count data normalization\r
differential analysis\r
The material has originally been prepared by Ignacio Gonzales, Annick Moisan and myself. The class has already been taught by these persons but also by Gaëlle Lefort and Jérôme Mariette.\r
\r
Pre-requisites: A background in R programming is necessary for this class. Before the class, please download the course material and install R, RStudio and the packages as described below. To produce high quality figures, I will use ggplot2 for plots but will not enter into details about the ggplot2 syntax. If you are not familiar with it, you can just use these command lines or switch to base plots instead.""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "intermediate" ;
    schema1:license <file:///home/runner/work/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/ELIXIR-TrP-KG-training-metadata/notspecified> ;
    schema1:name "training RNASeq biostat part" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "IFB French Institute of Bioinformatics" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.france-bioinformatique.fr> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://www.nathalievialaneix.eu/teaching/rnaseq.html> .

