<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/unsupervised-analysis-of-bone-marrow-cells-with-flexynesis> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_2269> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "Students" ] ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Björn Grüning" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Amirhossein Naghsh Nilchi" ] ;
    schema1:contributor [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Pavankumar Videm" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Björn Grüning" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Amirhossein Naghsh Nilchi" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2025-08-13"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2025-08-10"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

Traditional dimensionality reduction techniques, while useful, often fail to capture the complex non-linear relationships present in high-dimensional data. Deep learning approaches, particularly Variational Autoencoders (VAEs), have emerged as powerful tools for unsupervised analysis of single-cell transcriptomic data. VAEs combine the representational power of neural networks with probabilistic modeling, enabling them to learn meaningful latent representations while accounting for the inherent uncertainty in biological data.


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - How can we identify distinct cell populations in bone marrow single-cell data without prior labels?
 - What cellular patterns and relationships can be discovered through unsupervised deep learning approaches?
 - How does variational autoencoder (VAE) architecture help in dimensionality reduction and feature learning for single-cell data?


## Learning Objectives

- Apply Flexynesis VAE architecture for unsupervised analysis of single-cell bone marrow data
- Perform dimensionality reduction and feature learning using deep learning methods
- Identify and interpret cellular clusters and patterns in high-dimensional single-cell datasets
- Evaluate the quality of unsupervised representations through visualization and clustering metrics""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:keywords "Statistics and machine learning" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Workflows" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/statistics/tutorials/flexynesis_unsupervised/workflows/> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/records/16287482> ] ;
    schema1:name "Unsupervised Analysis of Bone Marrow Cells with Flexynesis" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Apply Flexynesis VAE architecture for unsupervised analysis of single-cell bone marrow data
- Perform dimensionality reduction and feature learning using deep learning methods
- Identify and interpret cellular clusters and patterns in high-dimensional single-cell datasets
- Evaluate the quality of unsupervised representations through visualization and clustering metrics""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/statistics/tutorials/flexynesis_unsupervised/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "2" .

