    schema1:contributor [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Saskia Hiltemann" ] ;
    schema1:creativeWorkStatus "Active" ;
    schema1:dateModified "2024-09-27"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:datePublished "2024-08-06"^^schema1:Date ;
    schema1:description """## Abstract

Beacon v2 is a data query protocol and API that allows the researcher to seek information about specific genomic variants of biomedical research and clinical applications from the data providers (Beacon provider) without 


## About This Material

This is a Hands-on Tutorial from the GTN which is usable either for individual self-study, or as a teaching material in a classroom.


## Questions this  will address

 - What does the term "Beacon" refer to?
 - How can MongoDB be employed to establish a Beacon tailored for your institution?
 - In what manner can variant data and metadata be readied into a format compatible with Beacons?
 - What are the steps involved in importing data into a Beacon seamlessly?
 - How does one perform queries on a Beacon to retrieve information about variants?


## Learning Objectives

- Comprehend the fundamental concepts and applications of Beacons
- Apply skills in utilizing MongoDB to construct and manage Beacons
- Analyze and transform variants and metadata into structures compatible with Beacon requirements
- Execute a step-by-step process to import data into Beacons
- Develop the ability to query Beacons for variants""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "advanced" ;
    schema1:keywords "Variant Analysis" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "e-learning" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Galaxy" ;
            schema1:url <https://bio.tools/tool/galaxy> ],
        [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Associated Training Datasets" ;
            schema1:url <https://zenodo.org/records/10658688> ] ;
    schema1:name "Working with Beacon V2: A Comprehensive Guide to Creating, Uploading, and Searching for Variants with Beacons" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "GTN" ;
            schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/> ] ;
    schema1:teaches """- Comprehend the fundamental concepts and applications of Beacons
- Apply skills in utilizing MongoDB to construct and manage Beacons
- Analyze and transform variants and metadata into structures compatible with Beacon requirements
- Execute a step-by-step process to import data into Beacons
- Develop the ability to query Beacons for variants""" ;
    schema1:url <https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/variant-analysis/tutorials/beaconise_1000hg/tutorial.html> ;
    schema1:version "3" .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/working-with-data-in-r-cfrr> a schema1:LearningResource ;
