    schema1:description """Within the [ELIXIR implementation study INCREASING](https://elixir-europe.org/internal-projects/commissioned-services/increasing-plant-data-findability) we have prepared three plant tool bundles. Each bundle is a systematic organisation of tools to enable their maximum potential to users, including detailed instructions for use. These bundles are designed to work with existing tools, dealing with various plant-derived data, better accessible to the end user. \r
The topics include the plant orthology tools [Ensembl Plants](https://plants.ensembl.org/index.html), [Plaza](https://bioinformatics.psb.ugent.be/plaza/), [Mercator](https://www.plabipd.de/mercator_main.html), [MapMan](https://www.plabipd.de/mapman_main.html), and [GoMapMan](https://gomapman.nib.si/), Knowledge graph resources [KnetMiner](https://knetminer.com/), [AgroLD](http://agrold.southgreen.fr/agrold/), and [Stress Knowledge Map](https://skm.nib.si), the federated search engine [FAIDARE](https://urgi.versailles.inrae.fr/faidare/), data analysis and visualisation tools [DiNaR](https://nib-si.shinyapps.io/DiNAR/) and  [MapMan](https://mapman.gabipd.org/web/guest/home), and phenotyping data publication using [MIAPPE](https://www.miappe.org/) and generic data repositories such as [dataverse](https://dataverse.org/) or [e!DAL-PGP](https://edal-pgp.ipk-gatersleben.de/). \r
\r
To present all three bundles to researchers, an online workshop was organised between October 5th and 6th, 2023. The recordings and materials of these sessions are provided here.""" ;
