<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/events/hands-on-data-analysis-workshop-d95f0050-8a20-4a7a-a65b-bec6855f7f58> a schema1:Course ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/Course/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:description """Format: Bring your laptop with an updated internet browser (Chrome,\r
Firefox or Safari). This is an interactive workshop!\r
\r
Register free here: https://forms.gle/dvrevioB7cmaMMpA6\r
\r
During the workshop, you will have the opportunity to work on a\r
dataset/problem/question of your choice (such as your own research\r
question, or e.g. a Galaxy analysis tutorial) with our assistance.\r
This is also a good opportunity to get more experience on:\r
\r
- Services for sensitive data (TSD)" including computing on the Colossus\r
cluster\r
\r
- NGS data analysis using NeLS Galaxy https://galaxy-uib.bioinfo.no/\r
\r
- How to use the NeLS portal https://nels.bioinfo.no/  for Data\r
Management in your project\r
\r
- How to use StoreBioInfo https://storebioinfo.norstore.no/  for Data\r
Management in your project\r
\r
If you have a specific question you would like to get help with during\r
the workshop, kindly notify us ahead, so we may be prepared. Also, if\r
you have wishes for topics to discuss in plenum for this, and also\r
future workshops, please let us know.\r
\r
We have in the works an introduction to NeLS and Galaxy for students\r
and researchers new to bioinformatics so if you have or know people\r
that would be interested in taking part please watch this space for\r
more information.""" ;
