<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/workshop-fair-data-stewardship-for-the-2020-itn-proevlifecycle> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3071>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_4012> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "PhD candidate" ] ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Mijke Jetten" ],
        [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Celia van Gelder" ] ;
    schema1:description """This material is part of an introductory FAIR data stewardship workshop for the Marie Curie ITN ProEVLifeCycle (The prostate cancer Extracellular Vesicle LifeCycle)\r
\r
FAIR and data stewardship - October 14th, 2020\r
Organiser: Dutch Techcentre For Life Sciences, DTL\r
Setup: Virtual meeting (corona-pandemic)\r
Duration: 2 hours\r
\r
Topics:  \r
* Introduction (the relevance of research data management, research data management and the data life cycle, open science, open access and open data, FAIR guiding principles, data stewardship)\r
* Planning data (data management plans, informed consent procedures, funder and journal requirements, costing data management)\r
* Collecting data (finding data (and the importance of FAIR data), capture data (importance of metadata, pre-registration), data security and privacy)\r
* Processing and analysing data (tools for processing and analysing data, Infrastructure for storing and sharing data, organising data, versioning and documenting data, anonymisation, pseudonymisation and personal data)\r
* Publishing, preserving data &amp; reusing data (what data should be archived, archiving for scientific integrity, archiving for reuse, archiving non-digital data, FAIR data, data rights)""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:identifier "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4687214" ;
    schema1:keywords " Data collection",
        " Data management planning",
        " Data preserving",
        " Data processing",
        " Data reuse",
        " Data sharing",
        "Data analysis" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "Slidedeck" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Workshop FAIR & Data stewardship for the 2021 ITN ProEVLifeCycle" ;
            schema1:url <https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/workshop-fair-data-stewardship-for-the-2021-itn-proevlifecycle> ] ;
    schema1:name "Workshop FAIR & Data stewardship for the 2020 ITN ProEVLifeCycle" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "DTLS - Dutch Techcentre For Life Sciences" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.dtls.nl> ],
        [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "ELIXIR Netherlands" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.dtls.nl/courses/> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4687214> .

<https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/workshop-fair-data-stewardship-for-the-2021-itn-proevlifecycle> a schema1:LearningResource ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/TrainingMaterial/1.0-RELEASE> ;
    schema1:about <http://edamontology.org/topic_3071>,
        <http://edamontology.org/topic_4012> ;
    schema1:audience [ a schema1:Audience ;
            schema1:audienceType "PhD candidate" ] ;
    schema1:author [ a schema1:Person ;
            schema1:name "Mijke Jetten" ] ;
    schema1:description """This material is part of an follow up FAIR data stewardship workshop for the Marie Curie ITN ProEVLifeCycle (The prostate cancer Extracellular Vesicle LifeCycle)\r
\r
FAIR and data stewardship - November 3th, 2021\r
Organiser: Dutch Techcentre For Life Sciences, DTL\r
Setup: Virtual meeting (corona-pandemic)\r
Duration: 2,5 hours\r
\r
Topics:  \r
* FAIR data stewardship generics (slides 4-9)\r
* How to be FAIR aware (slides 10-25)\r
* Recap: group efforts on FAIR data stewardship (slides 26-36)\r
* Recap: ten practices: ‘prepare well to prevent data disaster’ (slides 37-47)\r
* Next steps: FAIR awareness and group actions (slides 48-50)\r
\r
It also includes the outcomes of the FAIR-Aware tool (https://fairaware.dans.knaw.nl/), based on Vesa Akerman, Linas Cepinskas, Maaike Verburg, &amp; Mokrane Mustapha. (2021). FAIR-Aware: Assess Your Knowledge of FAIR (v1.0.1). Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5084861""" ;
    schema1:educationalLevel "beginner" ;
    schema1:identifier "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5704716" ;
    schema1:keywords " Data management planning",
        " Data preserving",
        "Data analysis",
        "Data collection",
        "Data processing",
        "Data reuse",
        "Data sharing" ;
    schema1:learningResourceType "Slidedeck" ;
    schema1:license <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> ;
    schema1:mentions [ a schema1:Thing ;
            schema1:name "Workshop FAIR & Data stewardship for the 2020 ITN ProEVLifeCycle" ;
            schema1:url <https://tess.elixir-europe.org/materials/workshop-fair-data-stewardship-for-the-2020-itn-proevlifecycle> ] ;
    schema1:name "Workshop FAIR & Data stewardship for the 2021 ITN ProEVLifeCycle" ;
    schema1:provider [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "DTLS - Dutch Techcentre For Life Sciences" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.dtls.nl> ],
        [ a schema1:Organization ;
            schema1:name "ELIXIR Netherlands" ;
            schema1:url <http://www.dtls.nl/courses/> ] ;
    schema1:url <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5704716> .

